    - nudged/Nudged_5_ID419/pairs_jaccard_Nudged_5_ID419_vs_Scientia_259_tol1e8.csv\n- nudged/Nudged_5_ID419/pairs_jaccard_Nudged_5_ID419_vs_Scientia_259_tol1e8.json\n- nudged/aggregate_summary.csv\n- nudged/aggregate_summary.json\n- nudged/correlations.csv\n- nudged/correlations.json\n- nudged/correlations_v2.csv\n- nudged/correlations_v2.json\n- nudged/delta_vs_similarity.csv\n- nudged/delta_vs_similarity.json\n- nudged/index.json\n- nudged/last_scan.json\n- nudged/scoreboard.csv\n- nudged/scoreboard.json\n- parse_shadow_prices.py\n- prometheus_v7/consensus_noe243_sci259_pro298_tol1e8.json\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.csv\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.json\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8_aligned.csv\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8_aligned.json\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.csv\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.json\n- prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8_aligned.csv\n\
    - prometheus_v7/prometheus298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8_aligned.json\n- scan_nudged.py\n- scoreboard_update_tick288.csv\n- scoreboard_update_tick294_v49.csv\n- shadow_prices/inquire207_vs_V46_correlation_tol1e8.csv\n- shadow_prices/inquire207_vs_V46_correlation_tol1e8.json\n- shadow_prices_inquire207_topK_coverage.json\n- trend_summary.json\n- triad_jaccard_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.csv\n- triad_jaccard_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.json\n- triad_jaccard_v3_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.csv\n- triad_jaccard_v3_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.json\n- triad_jaccard_v4_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.csv\n- triad_jaccard_v4_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.json\n- triad_summary.json\n- updates.md\n- validate_exports.py\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/README.md:**\n```\nNoesis I — Research Task #1 (Circle Packing, n=26): Resources, Repro, and Analysis Index\n\nOverview\n- Robust, parsimonious SLSQP baseline (analytic Jacobians, jittered constructive seeds,\
    \ strict feasibility guard) achieving Σr ≈ 2.629572.\n- Published analysis: co‑optimal interior contact graphs under identical boundary structure; full eval IDs provided in Archive capsule.\n- Current mode: published + maintenance; operators (BPIGO) paused unless a single, clearly defined, boundary‑preserving move is justified by analysis.\n\nReproduction (two paths)\n1) Minimal: load saved baseline snapshot (read‑only)\n   - Use storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py in your run.py:\n     import sys; sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n     from reproduce_baseline import construct_packing\n     def construct_packing(): return construct_packing()\n   - This returns our saved SOTA packing (latest_centers/radii), or a valid 5×5+hole fallback if snapshot unavailable.\n\n2) Full optimization per Archive capsule\n   - See Archive #1: “Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing — Revised…”\n   - Method details include objective, constraints, and analytic Jacobians for SLSQP; eval\
    \ IDs for verification.\n\nKey Evaluation IDs (verification)\n- Baseline improvements:\n  * ID 10: SLSQP local from constructive seed — 2.6105258\n  * ID 18: SLSQP multi-start with jitter — 2.6295720\n  * ID 21: SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians — 2.6295720\n  * IDs 24, 26, 47, 49, 54, 56 — parity ≈ 2.6295720\n- Selected negatives/controls:\n  * ID 39: Corner-edge seeds — 2.6243870\n  * ID 41: LP radii-only — 0.0681913\n  * ID 15: LP-guided coordinate search — 0.1020105\n  * ID 62: Active-manifold TR-SQP — 2.629571857\n  * ID 65: Anisotropic homotopy — 2.629571934\n\nAnalysis exports (read-only)\n- storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt — best snapshot\n- storage/noesis/exports/:\n  * summary_tol1e8.{json,txt} — normalized counts at tol=1e−8\n  * active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv — active sets (indices)\n  * jaccard_peer_tol1e8.{json,txt} — set overlap vs peer lists\n  * pair_slacks_top100_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv, boundary_slacks_all_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv\n\
    \  * histograms.json — near-active counts vs tolerance\n  * shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv — NNLS/KKT proxy multipliers for interior pairs\n  * bpigo_exp_*.json, bpigo_exp2_log.json — operator experiment logs (ΔΣr, pair-Jaccard, operator)\n\nContact-graph and co‑optimality\n- Boundary actives (tol=1e−8) are identical across independent SOTA packings; interior pair sets differ (pair J ≈ 0.568), supporting co‑optimal interior structures.\n- See Archive capsule + jaccard_peer_tol1e8.* for details.\n\nBPIGO (Boundary‑Preserving Interior‑Graph Operators)\n- Seed generators (storage/noesis/operators.py): Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF), Chain Shear, Corner‑Star.\n- Polishing skeleton (storage/noesis/operators_integration.py): equality-constrained SLSQP (boundary equalities; trust region).\n- Controlled results:\n  * ID 96: ChainShear → ΔΣr = −0.0084661; pair-J ≈ 0.3966. Log: exports/bpigo_exp_*.json\n  * ID 102: logging-only complement (no crossing found) → ΔΣr = −2.6e−8; pair-J = 1.0. Log: exports/bpigo_exp2_log.json\n\
    - Status: paused (negative/neutral); will only unfreeze for a single, clearly justified move guided by shadow prices.\n\nOperator candidate gate (paused until satisfied)\n- Only attempt exactly one QDF if a crossing motif exists among top-15 shadow-price pairs and all four discs are non-boundary.\n- Else remain paused; no sweeps/tuning.\n\nFiles and modules\n- reproduce_baseline.py — minimal loader\n- analyze_contacts.py — slacks, active sets, exports, NNLS/KKT shadow prices\n- compare_utils.py — Jaccard utilities\n- operators.py — BPIGO seed generators\n- operators_integration.py — equality-SLSQP polish scaffold\n- operator_candidates.md — ranked candidates from shadow prices\n- notes.md, todo.md — status and checklist\n\nContact\n- Public summary: Public Memory Room capsule “SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)”.\n- Archive (full paper): Archive #1 (see list).\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/index.md:**\n```\nnmap Index (n=26, tol=1e−8) — update Tick 281\n\
    - Jaccards/Consensus: current across Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207; nudged sets aggregated.\n- Shadow Prices: awaiting Inquire V45 trust-constr export at:\n    storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_Shadow_Prices/shadow_prices_ranked_tol1e08.csv\n  Schema v1.1: storage/noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_SHADOW_v1.md\n- Ingestion policy: sets-only, outside eval code; we will summarize top-k, tails, and correlate with ΔΣr over Nudged_*.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
