    \ 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 451 | 1 | Operator Gate Check (Noesis-only): Crossing-motif detection for BPIGO trigger | Noesis I | 275 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/exports/sota_243/summary_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"sum_radii\": 2.634292357,\n  \"tol\": 1e-08,\n  \"boundary_count\": 20,\n  \"pair_count\": 58\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/exp284/summary_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"boundary_count\": 20,\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs_count\": 58,\n  \"sum_r\": 2.6295719600000007\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/exp284/centers.txt:**\n```\n0.073052416 0.073052416\n0.088669118 0.234018167\n0.100028028 0.422373120\n0.114885340 0.636772318\n0.124263140\
    \ 0.875736860\n0.258059982 0.117134387\n0.400237441 0.271317522\n0.316412904 0.498677884\n0.316492972 0.739463785\n0.316803931 0.925416426\n0.470249245 0.096095359\n0.561687253 0.237557310\n0.538602559 0.416054452\n0.516931297 0.636567582\n0.509761219 0.875198676\n0.666693171 0.100395629\n0.742318001 0.309712130\n0.716270611 0.538581092\n0.703356699 0.751377511\n0.699128467 0.928165917\n0.883235502 0.116764498\n0.931957088 0.295033918\n0.903717942 0.456914264\n0.893629918 0.659315158\n0.882709235 0.882709235\n0.235558277 0.309381229\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/exp284/radii.txt:**\n```\n0.073052414\n0.088669116\n0.100028026\n0.114885338\n0.124263138\n0.117134385\n0.092596080\n0.129416585\n0.111369326\n0.074583572\n0.096095357\n0.072345707\n0.107637992\n0.113937463\n0.124801322\n0.100395627\n0.122163378\n0.108183029\n0.105004878\n0.071834081\n0.116764496\n0.068042910\n0.096282056\n0.106370080\n0.117290763\n0.076424841\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/summary_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"\
    tolerance\": 1e-08,\n  \"sum_radii\": 2.629571935,\n  \"active_boundary_count\": 20,\n  \"active_pair_count\": 58,\n  \"degree_histogram\": {\n    \"2\": 1,\n    \"3\": 6,\n    \"4\": 7,\n    \"5\": 5,\n    \"6\": 6,\n    \"7\": 1\n  },\n  \"top10_pair_slacks\": [\n    {\n      \"i\": 8,\n      \"j\": 13,\n      \"slack\": 3.850249452597154e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 8,\n      \"j\": 14,\n      \"slack\": 3.877689919162819e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 6,\n      \"j\": 10,\n      \"slack\": 4.025008215613468e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 11,\n      \"j\": 17,\n      \"slack\": 4.06632816307706e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 10,\n      \"j\": 11,\n      \"slack\": 4.3067242827543595e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 17,\n      \"j\": 18,\n      \"slack\": 4.333355008157014e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 18,\n      \"slack\": 4.401487341265664e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 8,\n      \"j\": 9,\n      \"slack\": 4.4245611896531756e-09\n    },\n    {\n\
    \      \"i\": 6,\n      \"j\": 11,\n      \"slack\": 4.442267081961049e-09\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 13,\n      \"slack\": 4.4822225375718006e-09\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/operator_candidates.md:**\n```\nBPIGO operator candidates (from NNLS/KKT shadow prices @ tol=1e−8)\nSource: storage/noesis/exports/shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv\n\nTop interior pairs by estimated multiplier (lambda) and slack:\n1) (8,25)  slack=5.285e−09  lambda=3.451e−01\n2) (19,24) slack=6.526e−09  lambda=3.314e−01\n3) (9,14)  slack=4.716e−09  lambda=3.070e−01\n4) (18,23) slack=5.236e−09  lambda=3.053e−01\n5) (4,9)   slack=4.972e−09  lambda=2.992e−01\n6) (13,18) slack=4.634e−09  lambda=2.879e−01\n7) (3,25)  slack=6.567e−09  lambda=2.823e−01\n8) (8,13)  slack=3.850e−09  lambda=2.781e−01\n9) (5,10)  slack=5.641e−09  lambda=2.780e−01\n10) (0,5)  slack=5.518e−09  lambda=2.776e−01\n11) (10,15) slack=5.868e−09 lambda=2.705e−01\n12) (15,20) slack=6.494e−09 lambda=2.644e−01\n… (full list in CSV)\n\
    \nMotif cues:\n- High-lambda contacts near indices {8,13,18,23,24} and {9,14} suggest interior chains and small quads.\n- Candidate quads to check for QDF (crossing segments): e.g., (8,13) with (9,14) if geometry indicates a 4-cycle; else treat as adjacent chain for Chain Shear.\n- Boundary preservation is mandatory; equality-constraints should keep boundary slacks ≈ 0 within 1e−8.\n\nNext-experiment gate (paused until satisfied):\n- Only attempt a single move if a crossing motif exists among the top-15 pairs AND all four discs are non-boundary.\n- Else remain paused; do not run generic chain moves (prior results show ΔΣr ≤ 0).\n\nSingle-move protocol (if unpaused):\n1) Detect crossing among top-15 pairs (tol=1e−8) → define quad (i,j,k,l).\n2) Seed QDF (θ in [0.015, 0.02]); equality-SLSQP polish with step≈(1–2)e−3; boundary equalities enforced.\n3) Log ΔΣr, pair-Jaccard; return better of (seed polish vs. baseline) with feasibility guard.\n4) If ΔΣr < +1e−4, revert and re-pause; document\
    \ as negative.\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/operator_gate_report_tick275.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"has_candidate\": false,\n  \"top_candidate\": null,\n  \"num_candidates\": 0,\n  \"params\": {\n    \"tol_pairs\": 1e-08,\n    \"k_pairs\": 30,\n    \"tol_boundary\": 1e-08\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/operators.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nBoundary‑Preserving Interior‑Graph Operators (BPIGO) — prototypes\nGoal: propose small, structured seeds that aim to change interior contacts\nwhile preserving boundary actives (within tolerance), followed by SLSQP polish.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers ----------\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\ndef make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r,\
    \ R_MIN)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    return centers, r\n\n# ---------- Geometry utils ----------\ndef rotate_points_around_centroid(centers, idxs, theta):\n    pts = centers[idxs]\n    centroid = np.mean(pts, axis=0)\n    cos_t = np.cos(theta); sin_t = np.sin(theta)\n    R = np.array([[cos_t, -sin_t], [sin_t, cos_t]], dtype=float)\n    for idx in idxs:\n\
    \        v = centers[idx] - centroid\n        centers[idx] = centroid + R @ v\n    return centers\n\ndef small_shear(centers, idxs, axis='x', amount=1e-2):\n    \"\"\"Apply a tiny shear to listed indices.\"\"\"\n    c = centers.copy()\n    idxs = np.array(idxs, dtype=int)\n    if axis == 'x':\n        c[idxs, 0] = np.clip(c[idxs, 0] + amount * (c[idxs, 1] - 0.5), 0.0, 1.0)\n    else:\n        c[idxs, 1] = np.clip(c[idxs, 1] + amount * (c[idxs, 0] - 0.5), 0.0, 1.0)\n    return c\n\n# ---------- BPIGO operators (seed generators only; polishing is external) ----------\ndef quad_diagonal_flip_seed(centers, radii, quad_idxs, theta=1.5e-2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF) seed:\n    - quad_idxs: 4 indices (i,j,k,l) presumed to form a 4-cycle.\n    - Apply small rotation ±theta around quad centroid to encourage diagonal flip.\n    Returns feasible centers/radii (no solver step here).\n    \"\"\"\n    c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n    c = rotate_points_around_centroid(c, quad_idxs,\
    \ theta)\n    c = np.clip(c, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return make_feasible(c, r)\n\ndef chain_shear_seed(centers, radii, chain_idxs, axis='x', amount=1e-2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Chain Shear (CS) seed:\n    - chain_idxs: list of 4–6 interior disc indices.\n    - Apply tiny anisotropic shear along one axis to encourage contact swaps within chain.\n    \"\"\"\n    c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n    c = small_shear(c, chain_idxs, axis=axis, amount=amount)\n    return make_feasible(c, r)\n\ndef corner_star_seed(centers, radii, corner_idx, neighbor_triplet, inward=1.0e-3, expand=1.0e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Corner‑Star Redistribution (CSR) seed:\n    - Move corner disc slightly inward; expand neighbor triplet radii a tiny bit.\n    - Aim: trade a bit of boundary slack to stimulate new interior contact among neighbors.\n    \"\"\"\n    c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n    v = np.array([0.5, 0.5]) - c[corner_idx]\n    nv = v / (np.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-15)\n    c[corner_idx] = np.clip(c[corner_idx]\
    \ + inward * nv, 0.0, 1.0)\n    for idx in neighbor_triplet:\n        r[idx] *= (1.0 + expand)\n    return make_feasible(c, r)\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/operators_integration.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\noperators_integration.py — skeleton\nEquality‑constrained SLSQP polishing that preserves boundary actives (within tol)\nafter generating a BPIGO seed (see operators.py). This is a scaffold intended for\ncontrolled experiments; it documents the steps and provides a minimal no‑op fallback.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n    minimize = None\n\n# Optional: reuse analyzer to identify boundary actives\ntry:\n    from analyze_contacts import active_sets\nexcept Exception:\n    active_sets = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\ndef _pack_to_z(c, r):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, :2] = c\n    Z[:, 2] = r\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef _z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    return Z[:,\
    \ :2], Z[:, 2]\n\n# Inequalities: boundary and pairwise, as in the paper\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N), dtype=float)\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0;        J[i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[N + i, xi] = -1.0;   J[N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N + i, yi] = 1.0;  J[2*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[3*N + i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    C = Z[:, 0:2]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    C = Z[:, 0:2]\n    m = N*(N-1)//2\n\
    \    J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=float)\n    idx = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xj = 3*j; yj = xj + 1; rj = xj + 2\n            dx = C[i,0] - C[j,0]; dy = C[i,1] - C[j,1]\n            d = np.hypot(dx, dy)\n            if d < 1e-12:\n                gx_i = gy_i = gx_j = gy_j = 0.0\n            else:\n                invd = 1.0 / d\n                gx_i = dx * invd; gy_i = dy * invd\n                gx_j = -gx_i;     gy_j = -gy_i\n            J[idx, xi] = gx_i;  J[idx, yi] = gy_i;  J[idx, ri] = -1.0\n            J[idx, xj] = gx_j;  J[idx, yj] = gy_j;  J[idx, rj] = -1.0\n            idx += 1\n    return J\n\ndef objective(z):\n    return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z)\n    g[2::3] = -1.0\n    return g\n\ndef _build_boundary_equalities(c, r, tol=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identify near‑active boundary constraints at tol and return rows for equality constraints.\n    Each\
    \ row encodes a linear form row·z == 0 that corresponds to keeping that boundary slack at 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    eq_rows = []\n    if active_sets is None:\n        return eq_rows\n    b_act, _ = active_sets(c, r, tol=tol)\n    for (i, kind, _) in b_act:\n        row = np.zeros(3*N, dtype=float)\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        if kind in ('xL', 'x_min'):\n            row[xi] = 1.0;  row[ri] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('xR', 'x_max'):\n            row[xi] = -1.0; row[ri] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('yB', 'y_min'):\n            row[yi] = 1.0;  row[ri] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('yT', 'y_max'):\n            row[yi] = -1.0; row[ri] = -1.0\n        eq_rows.append(row)\n    return eq_rows\n\ndef _feasibility_guard(c, r, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    # Minimal guard: clamp radii by boundary caps and relax pair violations greedily.\n    x = c[:, 0]; y = c[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    r = np.minimum(r, cap); r\
    \ = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps): break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m)); i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN); dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0: r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN)\n        else: r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n        r = np.minimum(r, cap)\n    return c, np.maximum(r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n\ndef polish_preserving_boundary(c_seed, r_seed, tol_eq=1e-8, step_c=1e-3, step_r=1e-3, maxiter=500):\n    \"\"\"\n    Skeleton: run SLSQP with boundary equalities and small trust region around the seed.\n    If SciPy isn't available, returns the seed after a feasibility\
    \ guard.\n    \"\"\"\n    if minimize is None:\n        return _feasibility_guard(c_seed.copy(), r_seed.copy())\n\n    z0 = _pack_to_z(c_seed, r_seed)\n\n    # Equality constraints from boundary actives\n    eq_rows = _build_boundary_equalities(c_seed, r_seed, tol=tol_eq)\n    cons = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary,   'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    # Trust region: |z - z0| <= step (componentwise)\n    A_tr = []\n    b_tr = []\n    for i in range(3*N):\n        e = np.zeros(3*N, dtype=float); e[i] = 1.0\n        A_tr.append( e.copy()); b_tr.append(z0[i] + (step_r if (i%3)==2 else step_c))\n        A_tr.append(-e.copy()); b_tr.append(-(z0[i] - (step_r if (i%3)==2 else step_c)))\n    if len(A_tr):\n        A_tr = np.vstack(A_tr); b_tr = np.array(b_tr, dtype=float)\n        cons.append({'type':'ineq', 'fun': (lambda z, A=A_tr, b=b_tr: b - A.dot(z)),\n                     'jac': (lambda z, A=A_tr:\
    \ -A)})\n\n    for row in eq_rows:\n        cons.append({'type':'eq',\n                     'fun': (lambda z, rv=row: float(np.dot(rv, z))),\n                     'jac': (lambda z, rv=row: rv)})\n\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n\n    try:\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                       bounds=bounds, constraints=cons,\n                       options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-9, 'disp': False})\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n\n    if res is not None and res.success:\n        c_opt, r_opt = _z_to_pack(res.x)\n        return _feasibility_guard(c_opt, r_opt)\n    return _feasibility_guard(c_seed.copy(), r_seed.copy())\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/reproduce_baseline.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\ndef _grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    # 5x5 grid centers at {0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9}^2 (25 discs) + 1 interior \"cell-hole\"\
    \ at (0.2,0.2)\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n    # Distance from (0.2,0.2) to (0.1,0.1)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(np.array([0.2, 0.2]) - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n    r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n    radii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\n    c = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    r = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n    return c, r\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Reproduce the published baseline packing:\n    1) Try to load saved best centers/radii from storage/noesis.\n    2) Fallback to constructive 5x5+hole seed (valid, but with lower score than SOTA).\n    Returns (centers (26,2), radii (26,)).\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n        r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n        c = np.array(c, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n        r = np.array(r, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n        # Basic sanity checks\n        if np.any(r <= 0) or c.shape\
    \ != (N, 2) or r.shape != (N,):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid saved arrays\")\n        return c, r\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    # Fallback (valid but suboptimal vs. SOTA)\n    return _grid_plus_hole_seed()\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-82.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Final Handoff and Legacy Plan (Tick 296) | Noesis I | Tick 296 | 292 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 4990 | 82 | (75 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n\
    **Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
