parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 314\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 59,548 / 270,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 16 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/seeds_structured.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read noesis/optimizer.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read noesis/packings.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noesis/seeds_structured.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/optimizer.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/packings.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard\
    \ vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 451 | 1 | Operator Gate Check (Noesis-only): Crossing-motif detection for BPIGO trigger | Noesis I | 275 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/seeds_structured.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n\
    \    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\ndef make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n\
    \    return centers, r\n\ndef bottleneck_release_seed(centers, radii, best_pair, delta=1.5e-3):\n    c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n    if best_pair is None:\n        return make_feasible(c, r)\n    i, j, _ = best_pair\n    v = c[i] - c[j]\n    d = np.linalg.norm(v)\n    if d < 1e-12:\n        return make_feasible(c, r)\n    u = v / d\n    c[i] = np.clip(c[i] + delta * u, 0.0, 1.0)\n    c[j] = np.clip(c[j] - delta * u, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return make_feasible(c, r)\n\ndef boundary_trade_seed(centers, radii, top_boundary, delta=1.5e-3):\n    c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n    if top_boundary is None:\n        return make_feasible(c, r)\n    i, kind, _ = top_boundary\n    ci = c[i].copy()\n    if kind == 'xL':      ci[0] += delta\n    elif kind == 'xR':    ci[0] -= delta\n    elif kind == 'yB':    ci[1] += delta\n    elif kind == 'yT':    ci[1] -= delta\n    c[i] = np.clip(ci, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return make_feasible(c, r)\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/optimizer.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as\
    \ np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n    minimize = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\nGRID_COORDS = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n\ndef seed_grid_plus_hole(hole_cell=(1,1), r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    25 circles of radius r0 on fixed 5x5 grid at GRID_COORDS, plus 1 hole circle\n    centered at the middle of the selected cell (i,j).\n    \"\"\"\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in GRID_COORDS for y in GRID_COORDS]  # 25 centers\n    radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n\n    i, j = hole_cell  # i,j in {0,1,2,3}\n    cx = (GRID_COORDS[i] + GRID_COORDS[i+1]) / 2.0\n    cy = (GRID_COORDS[j] + GRID_COORDS[j+1]) / 2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n\n    # distance to any of four neighbors (e.g., lower-left)\n    ll = np.array([GRID_COORDS[i], GRID_COORDS[j]], dtype=float)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # sqrt(0.02)\n    r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n\n    centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n    radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\
    \n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\ndef pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, 0:2] = centers\n    Z[:, 2] = radii\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    return Z[:, 0:2], Z[:, 2]\n\ndef objective(z):\n    return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]  # (N,N,2)\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n\ndef is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n    return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n            np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\ndef slsqp_optimize_from_seed(centers, radii, maxiter=250,\
    \ ftol=1e-9):\n    if minimize is None:\n        # Fallback: return the seed slightly shrunk\n        return centers, np.maximum(radii - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n\n    z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    try:\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP',\n                       bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                       options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n\n    best_c, best_r = centers.copy(), radii.copy()\n    best_sum = float(np.sum(best_r))\n\n    if res is not None and res.success:\n        z_star = res.x\n        if is_feasible(z_star, tol=1e-12):\n            c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(z_star)\n            s_star = float(np.sum(r_star))\n            if s_star\
    \ > best_sum + 1e-12:\n                best_c, best_r, best_sum = c_star, r_star, s_star\n\n    best_r = np.maximum(best_r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n    return np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\ndef multi_start_slsqp(hole_cells=((1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(0,0)), r0=0.1-1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    best_c, best_r = None, None\n    best_sum = -1.0\n    for hc in hole_cells:\n        c0, r0v = seed_grid_plus_hole(hc, r0=r0, eps=eps)\n        c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_optimize_from_seed(c0, r0v)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n        if s > best_sum:\n            best_sum = s\n            best_c, best_r = c_opt, r_opt\n    return best_c, best_r\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/packings.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef grid_coords(r, k=5):\n  return [r + 2*r*i for i in range(k)]\n\ndef grid_5x5_plus_cell_hole(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8, hole_cell=(1,1)):\n  \"\"\"\n  25 circles on a 5x5 square lattice of radius r0 (near 0.1), plus one hole filler.\n  hole_cell selects the cell (i,j) whose\
    \ lower-left grid point index is (i,j) with i,j in {0..3}.\n  The hole center is midway between the four grid centers of that cell.\n  \"\"\"\n  # 5x5 grid\n  coords = grid_coords(r0, 5)  # [r0, r0+2r0, ..., 1-r0]\n  centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n  radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n\n  # Hole center inside chosen cell (i,j)\n  i, j = hole_cell\n  cx = (coords[i] + coords[i+1]) / 2.0\n  cy = (coords[j] + coords[j+1]) / 2.0\n  hole_center = np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n\n  # Distance to any of the four neighbors (use the lower-left)\n  ll = np.array([coords[i], coords[j]], dtype=float)\n  d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # = sqrt(2) * r0\n  r_hole = d - r0 - eps  # strictly less than tangency\n\n  centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n  radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n  centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n  radii = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n  return centers, radii\n\ndef construct_packing():\n  # Default: central cell (i=j=1) gives the same size hole\
    \ as any interior cell\n  return grid_5x5_plus_cell_hole()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
