parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 315\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 63,064 / 270,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/exports/sota_243/index.md` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read noesis/exports/index.md` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read noesis/analyze_contacts.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read noesis/compare_utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noesis/exports/sota_243/index.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/exports/index.md will be displayed below.\n- File content\
    \ for noesis/analyze_contacts.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/compare_utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2:\
    \ 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 451 | 1 | Operator Gate Check (Noesis-only): Crossing-motif detection for BPIGO trigger | Noesis I | 275 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/exports/sota_243/index.md:**\n```\nSOTA 243 (Σr=2.6342924) — Artifact Index (tol=1e−8)\nPaths\n- Active sets: storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n                storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n- Summary:     storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/summary_tol1e8.json\n- Centers/Radii (canonical snapshot): storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt\n                                      storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt\n- Pointer:     storage/noesis/exports/SOTA_LATEST.txt → sota_243/\n\nCross-lineage comparisons\n- vs Scientia (Eval 259, Σr=2.6358957): boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.589041 (43/73)\n  files: storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\nNotes\n- Feasibility guard and final tiny shrink (1e−9) used in all runs.\n- Analysis uses published exports only (no eval‑code peer reads).\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/exports/index.md:**\n```\nCross-lineage and nmap summary\
    \ — Tick 133 (updated)\nPaths:\n  - Jaccards (n=26): storage/noesis/exports/\n  - nmap (n=24..30): storage/noesis/nmap/\n\nn=26 (tol=1e−8) vs Noesis\n- Aletheia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.5676 — jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json\n- Inquire:  boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.5676 — jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json\n- Scientia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7576 — jaccard_scientia_tol1e8.json\n- Peer-to-peer: jaccard_peers_tol1e8.json\n\nNew SOTA (eval-specific)\n- Aletheia eval155 (Σr≈2.6319369): boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7059 vs Noesis — jaccard_aletheia_eval155_tol1e8.json\n\nnmap (n=24..30)\n- Aggregates: storage/noesis/nmap/{aggregate_summary.json,.csv,best_by_n.csv}\n- Trend (best-by-n curve): storage/noesis/nmap/{trend_summary.json,best_curve.csv}\n- Per-n Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia): storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json (summary: jaccards_as_summary.md)\n- ΔΣr vs similarity (A vs S): storage/noesis/nmap/{delta_vs_similarity.json,.csv}\n- Consensus sets @ tol=1e−8:\n  * n=26 (Noesis,\
    \ Aletheia, Inquire, Scientia) and n=29 (Aletheia, Scientia):\n    storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json\n- Snapshot: peak at n=29 with Σr≈2.766433 (Scientia); similarity (A↔S) declines toward the peak (n=29 pairs J≈0.506); n=26 shows full boundary consensus but interior variants.\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/analyze_contacts.py:**\n```\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef compute_slacks(centers, radii):\n    centers = np.asarray(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.asarray(radii, dtype=float)\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    x = centers[:, 0]\n    y = centers[:, 1]\n    r = radii\n    # Boundary slacks\n    s_xL = x - r\n    s_xR = 1.0 - x - r\n    s_yB = y - r\n    s_yT = 1.0 - y - r\n    # Pairwise slacks\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    s_pairs = dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n    return (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs\n\ndef active_sets(centers, radii, tol=1e-9):\n    (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs\
    \ = compute_slacks(centers, radii)\n    n = len(radii)\n    boundary_actives = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((int(i), 'xL', float(s_xL[i])))\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((int(i), 'xR', float(s_xR[i])))\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((int(i), 'yB', float(s_yB[i])))\n        if s_yT[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((int(i), 'yT', float(s_yT[i])))\n    pair_actives = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            v = s_pairs[i, j]\n            if v <= tol:\n                pair_actives.append((int(i), int(j), float(v)))\n    return boundary_actives, pair_actives\n\ndef report(centers, radii, path='storage/noesis/contact_report.txt', tol=1e-9):\n    centers = np.asarray(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.asarray(radii, dtype=float)\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs = compute_slacks(centers, radii)\n    boundary_actives, pair_actives =\
    \ active_sets(centers, radii, tol=tol)\n\n    # Degree from pair actives\n    deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=int)\n    for (i, j, _) in pair_actives:\n        deg[i] += 1\n        deg[j] += 1\n\n    # Top-10 smallest pair slacks (over all pairs, not just actives)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    spu = s_pairs[iu]\n    order = np.argsort(spu)[:10]\n    top10 = []\n    for k in order:\n        i = int(iu[0][k]); j = int(iu[1][k])\n        top10.append({'i': i, 'j': j, 'slack': float(spu[k])})\n\n    lines = []\n    lines.append(f\"Contact Report (tolerance={tol})\")\n    lines.append(f\"Number of circles: {n}\")\n    lines.append(f\"Boundary actives: {len(boundary_actives)}\")\n    lines.append(f\"Pair actives: {len(pair_actives)}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    lines.append(\"Boundary contacts:\")\n    for (i, kind, slack) in boundary_actives:\n        lines.append(f\"  Circle {i}, {kind}, slack={slack:.12e}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    lines.append(\"Pair contacts:\")\n    for (i, j,\
    \ slack) in pair_actives:\n        lines.append(f\"  Circles ({i},{j}), slack={slack:.12e}\")\n\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(path, 'w') as f:\n            f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return {\n        'boundary_actives': boundary_actives,\n        'pair_actives': pair_actives,\n        'degree': deg,\n        'top10_pair_slacks': top10\n    }\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/compare_utils.py:**\n```\nimport os, csv, json, math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _boundary_slacks(centers, radii):\n    c = np.asarray(centers, float)\n    r = np.asarray(radii, float)\n    x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n    return x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r\n\ndef _pair_slacks(centers, radii):\n    c = np.asarray(centers, float)\n    r = np.asarray(radii, float)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    return dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n\ndef _active_sets_direct(centers,\
    \ radii, tol):\n    s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = _boundary_slacks(centers, radii)\n    sp = _pair_slacks(centers, radii)\n    n = len(radii)\n    b = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'xL', float(s_xL[i])))\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'xR', float(s_xR[i])))\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'yB', float(s_yB[i])))\n        if s_yT[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'yT', float(s_yT[i])))\n    p = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if sp[i, j] <= tol:\n                p.append((int(i), int(j), float(sp[i, j])))\n    return b, p, sp\n\ndef _tol_tag(tol: float) -> str:\n    # hyphenless tag like '1e8' for 1e-8\n    try:\n        e = int(round(math.log10(tol)))\n        return f'1e{abs(e)}'\n    except Exception:\n        return '1e8'\n\ndef _save_set_csv(items, path):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        wr = csv.writer(f)\n\
    \        for it in items:\n            wr.writerow(list(it))\n\ndef compute_and_export_from_pack(centers, radii, tol=1e-8, out_dir='storage/noesis/exports'):\n    # Direct computation (no external deps), robust to lineage changes\n    n = len(radii)\n    b_acts, p_acts, sp = _active_sets_direct(centers, radii, tol)\n    b_set = set((i, kind) for (i, kind, _) in b_acts)\n    p_set = set((min(i, j), max(i, j)) for (i, j, _) in p_acts)\n    # Degree\n    degree = np.zeros(n, dtype=int)\n    for (i, j, _) in p_acts:\n        degree[i] += 1\n        degree[j] += 1\n    # Top-10 smallest pair slacks (all pairs)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    spu = sp[iu]\n    order = np.argsort(spu)[:10]\n    top10 = [{'i': int(iu[0][k]), 'j': int(iu[1][k]), 'slack': float(spu[k])} for k in order]\n\n    tag = _tol_tag(tol)\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    # Contact report\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, 'contact_report.txt'), 'w') as f:\n        f.write(f\"Contact Report (tolerance={tol})\\\
    n\")\n        f.write(f\"Number of circles: {n}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"Boundary actives: {len(b_acts)}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"Pair actives: {len(p_acts)}\\n\\n\")\n        f.write(\"Boundary contacts:\\n\")\n        for (i, kind, slack) in b_acts:\n            f.write(f\"  Circle {i}, {kind}, slack={slack:.12e}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"\\nPair contacts:\\n\")\n        for (i, j, slack) in p_acts:\n            f.write(f\"  Circles ({i},{j}), slack={slack:.12e}\\n\")\n\n    # CSV exports\n    _save_set_csv(sorted(list(b_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_boundary_tol{tag}.csv'))\n    _save_set_csv(sorted(list(p_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_pairs_tol{tag}.csv'))\n\n    # Degree histogram as dict of str->count (to ensure JSON keys serializable)\n    hist = {}\n    binc = np.bincount(degree)\n    for k, v in enumerate(binc):\n        if v > 0:\n            hist[str(k)] = int(v)\n\n    # Summary JSON matching the accepted debugger format\n    summary = {\n        \"tolerance\"\
    : tol,\n        \"sum_radii\": float(np.sum(radii)),\n        \"active_boundary_count\": len(b_set),\n        \"active_pair_count\": len(p_set),\n        \"degree_histogram\": hist,\n        \"top10_pair_slacks\": top10\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f\"summary_tol{tag}.json\"), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\n    return b_set, p_set\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
