- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 316\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 68,630 / 270,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 18 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'is_active tolerance sweep and histogram refresh for n=26 (analysis-only)' (ID: 512) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719350000004\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/exports/operator_gate_sweep_latest.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read noesis/nmap/constraints_from_consensus.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noesis/exports/operator_gate_sweep_latest.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/constraints_from_consensus.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'is_active tolerance sweep and histogram refresh for n=26 (analysis-only)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID:\
    \ 512.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n\
    | 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 451 | 1 | Operator Gate Check (Noesis-only): Crossing-motif detection for BPIGO trigger | Noesis I | 275 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/exports/operator_gate_sweep_latest.json:**\n```\n\
    {\n  \"generated_at\": \"2025-10-20T03:31:28Z\",\n  \"settings\": [\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 15,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 20,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 25,\n      \"num_candidates\": 2,\n      \"top_candidate\": {\n        \"quad\": [\n          8,\n          25,\n          2,\n          7\n        ],\n        \"score\": 0.2115534\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 30,\n      \"num_candidates\": 2,\n      \"top_candidate\": {\n        \"quad\": [\n          8,\n          25,\n          2,\n          7\n        ],\n        \"score\": 0.2115534\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 40,\n      \"num_candidates\": 5,\n      \"top_candidate\": {\n        \"quad\": [\n          8,\n          25,\n          2,\n          7\n        ],\n        \"score\"\
    : 0.2115534\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-09,\n      \"k\": 60,\n      \"num_candidates\": 7,\n      \"top_candidate\": {\n        \"quad\": [\n          8,\n          25,\n          2,\n          7\n        ],\n        \"score\": 0.2115534\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 15,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 20,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 25,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 30,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 40,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 5e-09,\n      \"k\": 60,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n\
    \      \"k\": 15,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"k\": 20,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"k\": 25,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"k\": 30,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"k\": 40,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"k\": 60,\n      \"num_candidates\": 0,\n      \"top_candidate\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"has_any_candidate\": true,\n  \"best_candidate\": {\n    \"tol\": 1e-09,\n    \"k\": 25,\n    \"quad\": [\n      8,\n      25,\n      2,\n      7\n    ],\n    \"score\": 0.2115534\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/constraints_from_consensus.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nconstraints_from_consensus.py\nUtilities to:\n  1) Convert\
    \ consensus JSON to simple equality-constraint CSVs\n     (boundary equalities and pair-contact equalities).\n  2) Optionally validate residuals against Noesis baseline packing.\nPolicy: Reads ONLY Noesis lineage files plus our own consensus JSON under storage/noesis/nmap/.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\n\nTOL = 1e-8\n\ndef load_json(path):\n  with open(path, 'r') as f:\n    return json.load(f)\n\ndef write_csv(path, rows, header=None):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(path, 'w') as f:\n    if header:\n      f.write(header + '\\n')\n    for row in rows:\n      f.write(','.join(map(str, row)) + '\\n')\n\ndef consensus_to_csv(consensus_path, out_prefix):\n  data = load_json(consensus_path)\n  bcore = data.get('boundary_core', [])\n  pcore = data.get('pairs_core', [])\n\n  # Boundary: rows as (idx, wall), wall in {xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax}\n  b_rows = [(int(i), str(w)) for (i, w) in bcore]\n  # Pairs: rows as (i, j) with i<j\n  p_rows =\
    \ [(min(int(i), int(j)), max(int(i), int(j))) for (i, j) in pcore]\n\n  write_csv(f'{out_prefix}_boundary_eq.csv', b_rows, header='i,wall')\n  write_csv(f'{out_prefix}_pairs_eq.csv', p_rows, header='i,j')\n  return {'boundary_rows': len(b_rows), 'pairs_rows': len(p_rows)}\n\ndef residuals_for_noesis(consensus_path, centers_path, radii_path, out_json):\n  data = load_json(consensus_path)\n  bcore = data.get('boundary_core', [])\n  pcore = data.get('pairs_core', [])\n\n  c = np.loadtxt(centers_path, dtype=float).reshape(-1, 2)\n  r = np.loadtxt(radii_path, dtype=float).reshape(-1,)\n\n  # Residuals: value of equality expressions (should be ≈0)\n  # Boundary equalities\n  b_res = []\n  for (i, w) in bcore:\n    i = int(i); w = str(w)\n    if w == 'xmin': val = c[i, 0] - r[i]\n    elif w == 'xmax': val = 1.0 - c[i, 0] - r[i]\n    elif w == 'ymin': val = c[i, 1] - r[i]\n    elif w == 'ymax': val = 1.0 - c[i, 1] - r[i]\n    else: val = np.nan\n    b_res.append(float(val))\n\n  # Pair-contact\
    \ equalities\n  p_res = []\n  for (i, j) in pcore:\n    i = int(i); j = int(j)\n    d = float(np.hypot(c[i, 0] - c[j, 0], c[i, 1] - c[j, 1]))\n    val = d - (r[i] + r[j])\n    p_res.append(float(val))\n\n  out = {\n    'tol': TOL,\n    'n_boundary_eq': len(b_res),\n    'n_pairs_eq': len(p_res),\n    'boundary_residual_min': float(np.min(b_res)) if b_res else None,\n    'boundary_residual_max': float(np.max(b_res)) if b_res else None,\n    'pairs_residual_min': float(np.min(p_res)) if p_res else None,\n    'pairs_residual_max': float(np.max(p_res)) if p_res else None,\n    'boundary_within_tol': int(np.sum(np.abs(b_res) <= TOL)),\n    'pairs_within_tol': int(np.sum(np.abs(p_res) <= TOL))\n  }\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_json), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n  return out\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n  # Generate CSVs for n=26 and n=29 (A↔S) from our consensus JSONs\n  base = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n  n26 = f'{base}/consensus_n26_tol1e8.json'\n\
    \  n29 = f'{base}/consensus_n29_Aletheia_Scientia_tol1e8.json'\n\n  if os.path.exists(n26):\n    consensus_to_csv(n26, f'{base}/n26_consensus')\n    # Optional residuals vs Noesis snapshot if available\n    c_path = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n    r_path = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n    if os.path.exists(c_path) and os.path.exists(r_path):\n      residuals_for_noesis(n26, c_path, r_path, f'{base}/n26_consensus_residuals.json')\n\n  if os.path.exists(n29):\n    consensus_to_csv(n29, f'{base}/n29_consensus_AS')\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each\
    \ `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
