parts:
- text: "Gate found a candidate quad only at stricter tol and larger K (tol=1e-9, K=25): [8,25,2,7]. I’ll verify all four discs are interior (non-boundary) at tol=1e-8, then perform exactly one QDF attempt with boundary equalities and SLSQP polish; log ΔΣr and Jaccard, and return the better of baseline vs candidate.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Single BPIGO QDF on quad [8,25,2,7] with boundary equalities (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"bpigo, qdf, slsqp, equality, feasibility-guard\"\nabstract: \"Runs one controlled Quad Diagonal Flip on quad [8,25,2,7] if all four discs are interior at tol=1e-8. Uses equality-constrained SLSQP to preserve boundary contacts, strict feasibility guard, and 1e-9 final shrink. Logs ΔΣr and pair-set Jaccard vs baseline; returns the better packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json, time\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import minimize  # just\
    \ to ensure SciPy is present\n  except Exception:\n      minimize = None\n\n  # Allow importing lineage utilities\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  try:\n      from analyze_contacts import active_sets\n      from operators import quad_diagonal_flip_seed\n      from operators_integration import polish_preserving_boundary\n  except Exception:\n      active_sets = None\n      quad_diagonal_flip_seed = None\n      polish_preserving_boundary = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n  TOL_EQ = 1e-8\n  QUAD = [8, 25, 2, 7]\n\n  P_CENTERS = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  P_RADII   = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  OUT_LOG   = 'storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_attempt_latest.json'\n\n  def _ensure_dir(p):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n\n  def _load_snapshot():\n      # Load lineage snapshot or return a conservative fallback\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt(P_CENTERS, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(P_RADII, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n\
    \          if np.any(r <= 0):\n              raise ValueError(\"non-positive radius\")\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          centers = []\n          radius = 0.08\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < N:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          return np.array(centers, float), np.full(N, radius, float)\n\n  def _final_shrink(c, r, eps=SAFETY):\n      return c, np.maximum(r - eps, R_MIN)\n\n  def _pair_set_from_actives(pair_actives):\n      # pair_actives: list of (i,j,slack)\n      return set((min(int(i), int(j)), max(int(i), int(j))) for (i,j,_) in pair_actives)\n\n  def _jaccard(a, b):\n      if not a and not b:\n          return 1.0\n      inter = len(a & b)\n      union = len(a | b)\n      return (inter/union) if union > 0 else 0.0\n\n  def _write_log(obj):\n      try:\n          _ensure_dir(OUT_LOG)\n          with open(OUT_LOG, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(obj,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c0, r0 = _load_snapshot()\n      c0, r0 = _final_shrink(c0, r0)\n\n      baseline_sum = float(np.sum(r0))\n      result = {\n          'generated_at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime()),\n          'quad': QUAD,\n          'tol_eq': TOL_EQ,\n          'baseline_sum': baseline_sum,\n          'attempted': False,\n          'reason': None\n      }\n\n      # Preconditions: SciPy and lineage operators/contacts must be available\n      if (minimize is None) or (active_sets is None) or (quad_diagonal_flip_seed is None) or (polish_preserving_boundary is None):\n          result['reason'] = 'missing_dependencies'\n          _write_log(result)\n          return c0, r0\n\n      # Check that all four discs are interior (non-boundary) at tol=1e-8\n      b_act, p_act = active_sets(c0, r0, tol=TOL_EQ)\n      boundary_indices = set(i for (i, kind, slack) in b_act)\n      if any(i in boundary_indices\
    \ for i in QUAD):\n          result['reason'] = 'quad_has_boundary_disc'\n          _write_log(result)\n          return c0, r0\n\n      # Generate QDF seeds (±theta) and polish with boundary equalities\n      thetas = [1.5e-2, -1.5e-2]\n      best_c, best_r = c0.copy(), r0.copy()\n      best_sum = baseline_sum\n      chosen_theta = None\n\n      for th in thetas:\n          c_seed, r_seed = quad_diagonal_flip_seed(c0, r0, QUAD, theta=th)\n          c_opt, r_opt = polish_preserving_boundary(c_seed, r_seed, tol_eq=TOL_EQ, step_c=1e-3, step_r=1e-3, maxiter=500)\n          c_opt, r_opt = _final_shrink(c_opt, r_opt)\n          s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n          if s > best_sum + 1e-12:\n              best_sum = s\n              best_c, best_r = c_opt, r_opt\n              chosen_theta = th\n\n      # Compute pair-set Jaccard vs baseline at tol=1e-8 for reporting\n      _, p_baseline = active_sets(c0, r0, tol=TOL_EQ)\n      _, p_best = active_sets(best_c, best_r, tol=TOL_EQ)\n      pairs_base\
    \ = _pair_set_from_actives(p_baseline)\n      pairs_best = _pair_set_from_actives(p_best)\n      j_pairs = _jaccard(pairs_base, pairs_best)\n\n      result.update({\n          'attempted': True,\n          'chosen_theta': chosen_theta,\n          'candidate_sum': best_sum,\n          'delta_sum': float(best_sum - baseline_sum),\n          'pair_jaccard_vs_baseline': j_pairs,\n          'baseline_pair_count': len(pairs_base),\n          'candidate_pair_count': len(pairs_best)\n      })\n      _write_log(result)\n\n      return best_c.astype(float), best_r.astype(float)\n```"
