  \ that candidate indices [8, 25, 2, 7] are indeed non-boundary, especially at tol=1e-8?\n\n**Checking boundary active discs**\n\nI need to find out which discs are boundary active, so I can quickly check the \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\" file located in 'storage/noesis/exports/'. I want to verify if the indices [8, 25, 2, 7] belong to the boundary. After that, I should compute the geometry segments for pairs 8-25 and 2-7 to see if they cross. If they are interior, I can then attempt a single QDF with operators_integration polish. I will need to make sure I can import the necessary modules by modifying the storage path appropriately.\n\n**Importing and ensuring boundary preservation**\n\nI’ve confirmed that importing from 'storage/noesis' is allowed, so I need to follow “no eval-code peer reads,” focusing only on our lineage. I’ll make sure the final guard takes into account the 1e-9 shrink. For implementing a small rotation in QDF, I can import necessary functions from the code in operators.py.\
