- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 321\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol — Noesis II\n- Goals: (a) push score; (b) publish analyses at maturity (≥1/100 ticks).\n- Guards: sets-only peer ingestion; strict feasibility guard; 1e-9 final shrink.\n- Operators: run exactly one BPIGO move only if gate SAT at tol=1e-8 (top-15 crossing, all non-boundary).\n- Active tracks:\n  1) Recovery v4 replica (running): extended SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians.\n  2) Boundary-equality SLSQP (submitted): enforce consensus boundary equalities during SLSQP.\n  3) Analysis: tolerance sweep + gate sweep done; publish cleaned figures when rooms open.\n- Next: If no ≥+0.001 gain, pivot to consensus-constrained seeding and KKT-guided single-move design.\n```\n\
    - Agent Token Budget: 90,374 / 270,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 23 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 243**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J)\n**ID:** 243\n**Tags:** optimization, slsqp, multi-start, analytic-jacobians, recovery, feasibility-guard\n**Abstract:** Recover ≈2.62957 baseline after snapshot overwrite via diverse constructive seeds: 5×5 grid with multiple cell-hole placements, each with jittered variants. Use SLSQP with analytic Jacobians, strict feasibility guard, and final tiny shrink. Log per-start scores; save best packing to storage/noesis/latest_*.\n**Score:** 2.6342923548213792\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom math import hypot\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n\
    \    minimize = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# ---------------- Utilities ----------------\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\ndef feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY, max_iter=6000):\n    c = np.clip(np.array(centers, float), 0.0, 1.0)\n    r = np.array(radii, float)\n    r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt((diff**2).sum(axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n        dj = min(need\
    \ - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.9995, R_MIN)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= max(di, 0.0)\n            r[j] -= max(dj, 0.0)\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r - final_shrink, R_MIN)\n    return c, r\n\n# ---------------- Constructive seeds ----------------\ndef grid_centers(r0=0.1):\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    return np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords], dtype=float)  # 25 centers\n\ndef nearest_grid_dist(hole, grid):\n    d = np.sqrt(((grid - hole)**2).sum(axis=1))\n    return float(np.min(d))\n\ndef grid_plus_hole_seed(hole=(0.2, 0.2), r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    g = grid_centers(r0)\n    hole = np.array(hole, dtype=float)\n    dmin = nearest_grid_dist(hole, g)\n    r_hole = max(dmin - r0 - eps, R_MIN)  # ensure non-overlap to nearest grid neighbor\n    centers = np.vstack([g, hole[None, :]])\n    radii = np.array([r0]*25 + [r_hole], dtype=float)\n\
    \    return feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\ndef jitter_seed(c0, r0, rng, amp=2.5e-3):\n    c = c0.copy(); r = r0.copy()\n    jitter = rng.randn(*c.shape) * amp\n    c = np.clip(c + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n    r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=1e-9))\n    return feasibility_guard(c, r, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\n# ---------------- SLSQP formulation ----------------\ndef pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, :2] = centers\n    Z[:, 2] = radii\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    return Z[:, :2], Z[:, 2]\n\ndef objective(z):\n    return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z)\n    g[2::3] = -1.0\n    return g\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N),\
    \ dtype=float)\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0;        J[i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[N + i, xi] = -1.0;   J[N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N + i, yi] = 1.0;  J[2*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[3*N + i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    centers = Z[:, :2]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    centers = Z[:, :2]\n    m = N*(N-1)//2\n    J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=float)\n    idx = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xj = 3*j; yj = xj + 1; rj = xj + 2\n            dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]\n            dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n  \
    \          d = hypot(dx, dy)\n            if d < 1e-12:\n                gx_i = gy_i = gx_j = gy_j = 0.0\n            else:\n                invd = 1.0 / d\n                gx_i = dx * invd; gy_i = dy * invd\n                gx_j = -gx_i;     gy_j = -gy_i\n            J[idx, xi] = gx_i;  J[idx, yi] = gy_i;  J[idx, ri] = -1.0\n            J[idx, xj] = gx_j;  J[idx, yj] = gy_j;  J[idx, rj] = -1.0\n            idx += 1\n    return J\n\ndef is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n    return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n            np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\ndef slsqp_polish(centers, radii, maxiter=900, ftol=1e-9):\n    if minimize is None:\n        return feasibility_guard(centers, radii)\n    z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary,   'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n\
    \    ]\n    try:\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                       bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                       options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n    if res is not None and res.success and is_feasible(res.x, tol=1e-12):\n        c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(res.x)\n        return feasibility_guard(c_star, r_star, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n    return feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n\n# ---------------- Main ----------------\ndef construct_packing():\n    # Multiple hole placements (midpoints of 0.2-spaced grid cells)\n    holes = [\n        (0.2, 0.2), (0.2, 0.4), (0.4, 0.2), (0.4, 0.4),\n        (0.6, 0.6), (0.8, 0.8), (0.8, 0.6), (0.6, 0.8)\n    ]\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(424242)\n    amps = [0.0, 1.5e-3, 2.5e-3, 3.5e-3, 5.0e-3, 7.0e-3]\n    repeats = 2  # for non-zero amps\n\n    seeds = []\n    for hole\
    \ in holes:\n        c_base, r_base = grid_plus_hole_seed(hole=hole)\n        seeds.append((c_base, r_base, hole, 0.0))\n        for amp in amps[1:]:\n            for rep in range(repeats):\n                c_j, r_j = jitter_seed(c_base, r_base, rng, amp=amp)\n                seeds.append((c_j, r_j, hole, amp))\n\n    best_c = None; best_r = None; best_s = -1.0\n    total = len(seeds)\n    for idx, (c, r, hole, amp) in enumerate(seeds, 1):\n        c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_polish(c, r, maxiter=900, ftol=1e-9)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n        print(f\"[start {idx}/{total}] hole={hole} amp={amp:.4e} sum_r={s:.9f}\")\n        if s > best_s + 1e-12:\n            best_c, best_r, best_s = c_opt, r_opt, s\n            print(f\"  New best: {best_s:.9f} (hole={hole}, amp={amp:.4e})\")\n\n    print(f\"[final] best_sum_r={best_s:.9f}\")\n    try:\n        np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', best_c, fmt='%.9f')\n        np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt',   best_r, fmt='%.9f')\n\
    \    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return np.array(best_c, float), np.array(best_r, float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[start 1/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.610525814\n  New best: 2.610525814 (hole=(0.2, 0.2), amp=0.0000e+00)\n[start 2/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.614095805\n  New best: 2.614095805 (hole=(0.2, 0.2), amp=1.5000e-03)\n[start 3/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.622405385\n  New best: 2.622405385 (hole=(0.2, 0.2), amp=1.5000e-03)\n[start 4/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.486338125\n[start 5/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.484458954\n[start 6/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.465681994\n[start 7/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.613257050\n[start 8/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.603700084\n[start 9/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.611241691\n[start 10/88] hole=(0.2, 0.2) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.612030160\n[start 11/88] hole=(0.2,\
    \ 0.2) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.606428815\n[start 12/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.541421080\n[start 13/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.623934600\n  New best: 2.623934600 (hole=(0.2, 0.4), amp=1.5000e-03)\n[start 14/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.620452282\n[start 15/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.613681178\n[start 16/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.615333469\n[start 17/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.606738834\n[start 18/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.476574532\n[start 19/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.615747033\n[start 20/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.626930134\n  New best: 2.626930134 (hole=(0.2, 0.4), amp=5.0000e-03)\n[start 21/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.418719180\n[start 22/88] hole=(0.2, 0.4) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.634292355\n  New best: 2.634292355 (hole=(0.2, 0.4), amp=7.0000e-03)\n[start 23/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.629571960\n[start 24/88]\
    \ hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.506642666\n[start 25/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.611301334\n[start 26/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.483765209\n[start 27/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.493312680\n[start 28/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.607332534\n[start 29/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.614504971\n[start 30/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.416642888\n[start 31/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.609107074\n[start 32/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.623916507\n[start 33/88] hole=(0.4, 0.2) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.596168738\n[start 34/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.609506906\n[start 35/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.606947643\n[start 36/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.505328665\n[start 37/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.612791369\n[start 38/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.489781831\n[start 39/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.601349174\n\
    [start 40/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.605299945\n[start 41/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.612872007\n[start 42/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.606221292\n[start 43/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.606456939\n[start 44/88] hole=(0.4, 0.4) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.412706053\n[start 45/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.609506906\n[start 46/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.611261475\n[start 47/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.510437231\n[start 48/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.613581046\n[start 49/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.507158948\n[start 50/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.620744197\n[start 51/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.612475762\n[start 52/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.447835488\n[start 53/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.611672139\n[start 54/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.619704927\n[start 55/88] hole=(0.6, 0.6) amp=7.0000e-03\
    \ sum_r=2.611672139\n[start 56/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.610525814\n[start 57/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.509919194\n[start 58/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.509002700\n[start 59/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.615247519\n[start 60/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.611445034\n[start 61/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.605023966\n[start 62/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.628337623\n[start 63/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.611269377\n[start 64/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.424443063\n[start 65/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.602990527\n[start 66/88] hole=(0.8, 0.8) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.605429366\n[start 67/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.622459436\n[start 68/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.514209942\n[start 69/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.616780278\n[start 70/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.609058114\n[start 71/88] hole=(0.8,\
    \ 0.6) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.615573144\n[start 72/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.614078583\n[start 73/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.479331813\n[start 74/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.606972524\n[start 75/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.458691591\n[start 76/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.614411974\n[start 77/88] hole=(0.8, 0.6) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.392142749\n[start 78/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=0.0000e+00 sum_r=2.541421080\n[start 79/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.625172644\n[start 80/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=1.5000e-03 sum_r=2.620452281\n[start 81/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.618744082\n[start 82/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=2.5000e-03 sum_r=2.619072680\n[start 83/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.610868392\n[start 84/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=3.5000e-03 sum_r=2.460397097\n[start 85/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.428616716\n[start 86/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=5.0000e-03 sum_r=2.620845134\n\
    [start 87/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.607182896\n[start 88/88] hole=(0.6, 0.8) amp=7.0000e-03 sum_r=2.620723884\n[final] best_sum_r=2.634292355\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 246**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8\n**ID:** 246\n**Tags:** analysis, export, active-sets, reproducibility\n**Abstract:** Read the saved SOTA packing (latest_*), compute boundary/pair active sets at tol=1e-8, and export CSV/JSON artifacts under storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/. Return the same packing; no optimization or peer reads.\n**Score:** 2.634292357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np, os, json\n\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\ndef load_saved_best():\n    c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt').reshape(N,\
    \ 2)\n    r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt').reshape(N,)\n    return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n\ndef compute_slacks(centers, radii):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]; r = radii\n    s_xL = x - r\n    s_xR = 1.0 - x - r\n    s_yB = y - r\n    s_yT = 1.0 - y - r\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    s_pairs = dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n    return (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs\n\ndef export_active_sets(centers, radii, tol=TOL, prefix='storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'):\n    os.makedirs(prefix, exist_ok=True)\n    (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs = compute_slacks(centers, radii)\n    # Boundary CSV\n    b_lines = [\"i,kind,slack\"]\n    for i in range(N):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: b_lines.append(f\"{i},xL,{s_xL[i]:.12e}\")\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: b_lines.append(f\"{i},xR,{s_xR[i]:.12e}\")\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: b_lines.append(f\"{i},yB,{s_yB[i]:.12e}\")\n       \
    \ if s_yT[i] <= tol: b_lines.append(f\"{i},yT,{s_yT[i]:.12e}\")\n    with open(f\"{prefix}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\", \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(\"\\n\".join(b_lines) + \"\\n\")\n    # Pair CSV\n    p_lines = [\"i,j,slack\"]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    for (i, j, s) in zip(iu[0], iu[1], s_pairs[iu]):\n        if s <= tol:\n            p_lines.append(f\"{i},{j},{s:.12e}\")\n    with open(f\"{prefix}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\", \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(\"\\n\".join(p_lines) + \"\\n\")\n    # Summary JSON\n    summary = {\n        \"sum_radii\": float(np.sum(radii)),\n        \"tol\": tol,\n        \"boundary_count\": len(b_lines) - 1,\n        \"pair_count\": len(p_lines) - 1\n    }\n    with open(f\"{prefix}/summary_tol1e8.json\", \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    c, r = load_saved_best()\n    export_active_sets(c, r, tol=TOL, prefix='storage/noesis/exports/sota_243')\n    # Also copy a canonical pointer to latest\
    \ SOTA exports\n    try:\n        os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n        with open('storage/noesis/exports/SOTA_LATEST.txt', 'w') as f:\n            f.write('Eval 243, sum_radii ≈ 2.634292, tol=1e-8, folder=storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/\\n')\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 243` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 246` (in Research Counter);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 243 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 246 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26\
    \ SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 451 | 1 | Operator Gate Check (Noesis-only): Crossing-motif detection for BPIGO trigger | Noesis I | 275 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied\
