  \ with equalities to fix boundaries. Trust-constrained optimization might be useful since previous attempts showed negative results. \n\nI can submit another experiment since we’re allowed two concurrent ones, but I’ll remember to avoid endless sweeps.\n\n**Exploring limited attempts**\n\nI think some limited high-value attempts are okay for the situation.\n\nWe could try \"homotopy radius shrinkers to relieve the interior,\" but I had negative results with Noesis. \n\nAnother option is using \"consensus-constrained seeds\" for sampling along boundary equalities, but we didn't see improvement when we attempted that before.\n\nThere's also the \"KKT guided operator design,\" which prioritizes pairs with high shadow prices, but the gate parameters weren't satisfied.\n\nI can prepare a Private Memory note summarizing the SOTA reproduction, gate results, and our plan.\n\nWith a token budget of 115k/270k used, I should read the dual-tolerance gate output file to check for any crossing quads\
  \ found.\n\n**Preparing for analysis and results**\n\nI haven't read the results yet, but I think I should prepare a Private Memory reply summarizing the SOTA reproduction, noting that \"SOTA_243 centers/radii have changed from the earlier baseline.\" \n\nI need to update the meta prompt to reflect that SOTA has been regained. After that, I'll pause heavy optimization and focus on analysis tasks, creating an \"analysis_draft_update\" in Private Memory.\n\nI might also set a TODO to draft an \"Archive submission skeleton,\" including a 100-word abstract. However, I can’t create an Archive capsule until I'm matured, so I'll prepare the draft in Private Memory.\n\nSoon, I should check the results of \"running experiment 531\" and call \"rank score\" to see the scoreboard. Alternatively, I can look into \"review 525\" for logs, but those aren’t accessible right now. I can fetch logs for finished evaluations using \"review evaluation_id\" instead. Lastly, I'll read the storage path for logs\
  \ we wrote.\n\n**Planning incremental actions**\n\nThe question is about incremental steps, and I see that the last message shows our current state. I'll issue some actions with minimal commentary: \n\nFirst, I’ll read the dual-tolerance gate output and create a brief note in Private Memory to update meta. Proposing to back up the new SOTA snapshot to exports/sota_243, but since that was already done, I might just confirm that latest_centers/radii reflect SOTA.\n\nNext, I’ll set \"page_size 20\" and use \"rank score\" to see our standing, noting that I know the current SOTA of 2.6342924 isn't necessarily global. Other lineages could be higher but might not show since the scoreboard is limited to our lineage.\n\nI’ll read the necessary files and summarize that \"SOTA restored\" in Private Memory, adjust our plan accordingly, and focus on writing drafts. Actions will include reading operator statistics, replying with a summary, and tracking our current test. Finally, I’ll craft the necessary\
  \ commands and avoid heavy formatting."
