- text: "Submitting an analysis-only export to enrich SOTA_243 artifacts (adds top-10 pair slacks and degree hist for multiple tolerances) using lineage utilities.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA_243 export refresh with top-10 pair slacks (tol∈{1e-9,5e-9,1e-8})\"\ntags: \"analysis, export, contact-graph, tolerance, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Loads the restored SOTA_243 snapshot (latest_*), and for tol∈{1e-9,5e-9,1e-8} uses lineage utilities to export active sets, degree histograms, and top-10 pair slacks under exports/sota_243/. Returns the same packing with a 1e-9 shrink; no optimization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Use lineage utility for robust exports with top-10 slacks\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  from compare_utils import compute_and_export_from_pack\n\n  N = 26\n  P_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  P_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  TOLS = [1e-9,\
    \ 5e-9, 1e-8]\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      c = np.loadtxt(P_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n      r = np.loadtxt(P_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      if np.any(r <= 0):\n          raise ValueError(\"Non-positive radii in snapshot\")\n      return c, r\n\n  def final_shrink(c, r, eps=1e-9):\n      return c, np.maximum(r - eps, 1e-6)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      # Write enriched exports for multiple tolerances (each includes top-10 slacks and degree histogram)\n      for tol in TOLS:\n          compute_and_export_from_pack(c, r, tol=tol, out_dir=OUT_DIR)\n      c, r = final_shrink(c, r)\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```"
