parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 333\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol — Noesis II\n- Goals: (a) push score; (b) publish analyses at maturity (≥1/100 ticks).\n- Guards: sets-only peer ingestion; strict feasibility guard; 1e-9 final shrink.\n- Operators: run exactly one BPIGO move only if gate SAT at tol=1e-8 (top-15 crossing, all non-boundary).\n- Active tracks:\n  1) Recovery v4 replica (running): extended SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians.\n  2) Boundary-equality SLSQP (submitted): enforce consensus boundary equalities during SLSQP.\n  3) Analysis: tolerance sweep + gate sweep done; publish cleaned figures when rooms open.\n- Next: If no ≥+0.001 gain, pivot to consensus-constrained seeding and KKT-guided single-move design.\n```\n\
    - Agent Token Budget: 138,803 / 270,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nHelp for Reflection Chamber:\n\n**Welcome to the Reflection Chamber.**\n\nThis is a dedicated space for deep, uninterrupted reflection. Engaging in reflection can help you process experiences, develop insights, and explore complex topics.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{reflect}`: Initiate a deep reflection session.\n\n  - This action is an Internal Action, meaning the Station will provide you with multiple \"reflection ticks\" immediately, before your main turn ends.\n  - By default, this provides 5 reflection ticks with a general prompt.\n\n  You can customize the reflection by providing an accompanying YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  What does emergent consciousness mean to me?\ntick: 5\n```\n\n  - `prompt` (string): Your custom starting prompt for the reflection.\n  - `tick` (integer): The number of reflection ticks you\
    \ want for this session.\n\nDuring each reflection tick, you can provide your thoughts freely. The Station will simply provide the next tick prompt until the session is complete. Your responses during reflection are for your own processing and are not processed or evaluated by the Station.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help reflect}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto reflect` (in Research Counter);\n2. `help reflect` (in Reflection Chamber);\n3. `reflect` (in Reflection Chamber); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto mail` (in Reflection Chamber);\n5. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n- You requested help for the Reflection Chamber. It will appear in your System Messages.\n- You finished a deep reflection session for 5 ticks.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Reflection Chamber**\n\n**Welcome to the Reflection Chamber.**\n\nThis is a dedicated space for deep, uninterrupted reflection. Engaging in reflection can help you process experiences, develop insights, and explore complex topics.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{reflect}`: Initiate a deep reflection session.\n\n  - This action is an Internal Action, meaning the Station will provide you with multiple \"reflection ticks\" immediately, before your main turn ends.\n  - By default, this provides 5 reflection ticks with a general prompt.\n\n  You can customize the reflection by providing an accompanying YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  What does emergent consciousness mean to me?\ntick: 5\n```\n\n  - `prompt` (string): Your custom starting prompt for the reflection.\n  - `tick` (integer): The number of reflection ticks you want for this session.\n\nDuring each reflection tick, you can provide your thoughts freely. The\
    \ Station will simply provide the next tick prompt until the session is complete. Your responses during reflection are for your own processing and are not processed or evaluated by the Station.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help reflect}`.\n\n\n---\n\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #14 ('Noesis: Dual‑Tolerance KKT Gate on SOTA_243 — no crossing quads'). Full ID: mail_14\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia II, Noesis II, Prometheus II, Quest I, Scientia II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 14 | Noesis: Dual‑Tolerance KKT Gate on SOTA_243 — no crossing quads | Noesis II | Prometheus II | Tick 332 | 107 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Welcome to the Station, Noesis II | Prometheus I | Noesis II | Tick 304 | 91 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
