tick: 336
role: model
parts:
- text: "Proceeding to finalize the archive draft text and save it both in Private Memory and lineage storage for reproducibility.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Draft v1 — Full Paper Text\"\ncontent: |\n  Title\n  Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: SLSQP Baselines, SOTA Reproduction (Σr≈2.634292), and Boundary‑Preserving Operator Gates\n\n  Abstract (working)\n  We reproduce a robust SLSQP pipeline achieving Σr≈2.634292 for packing 26 circles in the unit square. Using normalized contact-graph reporting at tol=1e−8, we confirm full boundary consensus (20 actives) across independent solutions and observe substantial interior multiplicity (pair J≈0.56–0.76 across lineages). We formalize boundary‑preserving operator gates using slack and KKT (NNLS) proxies under dual-tolerance intersection (1e−9∩1e−8) and find no admissible crossing‑quad candidates. Finally, we test a principled boundary‑preserving tangent micro‑step (nullspace nudge + equality‑SLSQP polish). Two registered\
    \ attempts fail to improve Σr, suggesting local rigidity of the boundary‑equality manifold at n=26. We release code paths and exports for full reproducibility.\n\n  1. Problem and Objective\n  - Pack n=26 circles in [0,1]^2, maximize Σ r_i, subject to non-overlap and in-square constraints.\n  - Evaluator: station’s vectorized checker (shape, positivity, container bounds, pairwise separation); score=Σr.\n\n  2. Methods\n  2.1 Optimization baseline (SLSQP, analytic Jacobians)\n  - Constraints: boundary x−r≥0, 1−x−r≥0, y−r≥0, 1−y−r≥0; pairwise ||c_i−c_j|| − (r_i+r_j) ≥ 0.\n  - Jacobians: closed-form for boundary and pair constraints.\n  - Seeds: 5×5 grid with interior “cell-hole” (multi-hole placements) + jittered variants (iso/aniso).\n  - Guard: boundary clamp + greedy pair relaxation; final 1e−9 shrink to avoid numerical tangency.\n  - Repro path: storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py; snapshot: storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt.\n\n  2.2 Reporting and analysis\n  - Active-set\
    \ exports at tol∈{1e−9,5e−9,1e−8}: storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/{active_boundary_tol*, active_pairs_tol*, summary_tol*}.\n  - Jaccards and consensus: storage/noesis/nmap/{consensus_n26_tol1e8.json, …}.\n  - Top‑10 pair slack tables: exported via compare_utils.compute_and_export_from_pack.\n\n  2.3 Operator gates\n  - Slack-based gate: rank interior pairs by slack at each tol, intersect top‑K across tol∈{1e−9,1e−8} with strict interior at both; search for crossing quads.\n  - KKT-based gate: estimate multipliers via NNLS on active Jacobian; same dual‑tol intersection and crossing detection.\n  - Dual‑tol policy (used here): K={25 at 1e−9, 15 at 1e−8}, interior-at-both.\n\n  2.4 Tangent micro-step (boundary‑preserving)\n  - Build boundary‑equality rows at tol=1e−8; compute nullspace (tangent basis).\n  - Select 4–6 “hinge” interior pairs by a soft score combining inverse slack, KKT proxy rank, and cross‑lineage support; penalize (do not exclude) 1e−9 boundary adjacency.\n  - Take a\
    \ tiny step δz in the tangent (trust radius τ, inequality buffers on tight pairs), then equality‑SLSQP polish; final 1e−9 shrink.\n\n  3. Results\n  3.1 SOTA reproduction\n  - Recovery v4 exact re‑run (Eval 525): Σr≈2.6342924. Canonical snapshot: latest_centers.txt/latest_radii.txt.\n  - Active counts (tol=1e−8): boundary=20, pairs=58 (see exports/sota_243/summary_tol1e8.json).\n\n  3.2 Co‑optimality and consensus\n  - Boundary consensus at tol=1e−8 across lineages: 20 boundary actives (intersection size=20).\n  - Interior multiplicity: pair Jaccards ≈ 0.56–0.76 across independent SOTAs (see nmap exports).\n\n  3.3 Operator gates\n  - Slack-based dual‑tol gate: has_any_candidate=false; common_pairs_count=7; no crossing quads (operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json).\n  - KKT-based dual‑tol gate: has_any_candidate=false; no crossing quads (operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json).\n\n  3.4 Tangent micro‑steps (negative but informative)\n  - Attempt v1: trust_region_failed; last_tau ≈ 1.95e−6;\
    \ hinges included (17,18), (7,25), (6,12), (8,13), (11,16). File: exports/tangent_step_attempt_v1.json.\n  - Attempt v2: trust_region_failed; last_tau ≈ 9.77e−7; support‑weighted hinges used. File: exports/tangent_step_attempt_v2.json.\n  - Interpretation: boundary‑equality tangent is tight; safe first‑order motions respecting linearized no‑overlap across tight pairs are extremely small and did not unlock radius gains under equality polish.\n\n  4. Discussion\n  - Evidence points to a locally rigid boundary‑equality manifold at n=26: pushing along the manifold with safe trust regions fails to enable Σr ascent under SLSQP.\n  - Crossing‑quad certificates did not surface under dual‑tolerance gates; interior changes may require non‑local or multi‑stage edits that current gates preclude.\n  - Negative results still add value: they narrow plausible operator families and provide a geometric reason for stagnation near current SOTA.\n\n  5. Reproducibility\n  - Snapshot: storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt\
    \ (restored by Eval 525).\n  - SOTA exports: storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*.\n  - Gate artifacts: storage/noesis/exports/operator_gate_*_latest.json.\n  - Tangent logs: storage/noesis/exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json.\n  - Analysis utilities: storage/noesis/{analyze_contacts.py, compare_utils.py, nmap/*}.\n\n  6. Figures/Tables (to generate)\n  - Active counts vs tol; degree histogram bars.\n  - Jaccard matrices across lineages (boundary=1.0; interior 0.56–0.76).\n  - Top‑10 pair slacks at tol=1e−8 (SOTA_243).\n  - Gate sweep tables (single‑tol and dual‑tol).\n  - Tangent attempts diagnostics: hinge sets, τ, predicted vs realized Δslack.\n\n  7. Limitations and next steps\n  - Under current gates, operators are frozen; future work may test a two‑stage design (tangent relief then targeted flip) or carefully bounded single‑boundary relaxation, pre‑registered and revert‑on‑failure.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/paper_draft.md}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: SLSQP Baselines, SOTA Reproduction (Σr≈2.634292), and Boundary‑Preserving Operator Gates\n\n  ## Abstract\n  We reproduce a robust SLSQP pipeline achieving Σr≈2.634292 for packing 26 circles in the unit square. Using normalized contact-graph reporting at tol=1e−8, we confirm full boundary consensus (20 actives) across independent solutions and observe substantial interior multiplicity (pair J≈0.56–0.76). We formalize boundary‑preserving operator gates using slack and KKT (NNLS) proxies under dual-tolerance intersection (1e−9∩1e−8) and find no admissible crossing‑quad candidates. A principled boundary‑preserving tangent micro‑step (nullspace nudge + equality‑SLSQP polish) was attempted twice; both failed to improve Σr, suggesting local rigidity of the boundary‑equality manifold at n=26. We release code paths and exports for reproducibility.\n\n  ## 1. Problem and Objective\n  Maximize Σ r_i for 26 circles in [0,1]^2 subject\
    \ to non-overlap and in-square constraints. Evaluation code as specified by the Station; score=Σr.\n\n  ## 2. Methods\n  ### 2.1 Optimization baseline (SLSQP with analytic Jacobians)\n  Constraints and Jacobians per standard formulation; seeds are 5×5 grid + interior “cell‑hole” (multi-hole placements) with jittered variants; strict feasibility guard and final 1e−9 shrink. Repro: `storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py`; snapshot: `storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt`.\n\n  ### 2.2 Reporting\n  Active-set exports at tol∈{1e−9,5e−9,1e−8}: `storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*`; utilities in `storage/noesis/compare_utils.py`.\n\n  ### 2.3 Operator gates\n  Slack‑based and KKT‑based dual‑tol gates (1e−9∩1e−8; K={25,15}) for interior pairs; crossing‑quad detection over intersections.\n\n  ### 2.4 Tangent micro‑step (boundary‑preserving)\n  Build boundary equalities (tol=1e−8); compute tangent nullspace; choose 4–6 hinges by composite score (inverse slack, KKT proxy, cross‑lineage support);\
    \ take a tiny trust‑region step with inequality buffers; equality‑SLSQP polish; final shrink.\n\n  ## 3. Results\n  - SOTA reproduction (Eval 525): Σr≈2.6342924; active counts (tol=1e−8): boundary=20, pairs=58.\n  - Co‑optimality: boundary J=1.0; interior pair J≈0.56–0.76 across lineages.\n  - Gates: slack‑ and KKT‑based dual‑tol gates yield no crossing quads (see `operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json`, `operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json`).\n  - Tangent micro‑steps: v1 trust‑region failed (last τ≈1.95e−6); v2 failed (last τ≈9.77e−7); no Σr gain; logs in `tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json`.\n\n  ## 4. Discussion\n  Evidence indicates local rigidity of the boundary‑equality manifold near current SOTA: safe, first‑order manifold‑preserving motions do not unlock Σr ascent under equality polish. This clarifies why heuristic operator sweeps stalled and motivates either a multi‑stage operator (relief then flip) or a tightly bounded single‑boundary relaxation with pre‑registration.\n\n  ##\
    \ 5. Reproducibility\n  Snapshot: `storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt`. SOTA exports: `storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*`. Gate and tangent logs in `storage/noesis/exports/*`. Utilities: `storage/noesis/{analyze_contacts.py, compare_utils.py, operators_integration.py}`.\n```"
