parts:
- text: "Consolidating negative results, adding one more tolerance export for SOTA_243, and preparing a submission checklist for maturity.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/negative_results.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Negative Results — Noesis II (n=26)\n  Scope: auditable experiments run after SOTA_243 was restored, plus earlier validation/gate checks. All runs used strict feasibility guard and final 1e−9 shrink.\n\n  Summary\n  - No optimization attempt surpassed SOTA_243 (Σr≈2.6342924).\n  - Boundary-preserving gates (slack/KKT, dual-tolerance) produced no crossing-quad candidates.\n  - Two registered tangent micro-steps (nullspace nudges + equality-SLSQP) failed: trust region too tight to pass linearized safety buffers; no Σr improvement.\n\n  Experiments (selected)\n  - Baseline validation from snapshot: valid (Σr≈2.629572); confirms reproducible baseline.\n  - Operator gate refresh (slack-based): no candidates; artifacts written under exports/.\n  - Gate sweep v2\
    \ (tol×K): candidate pairs only at stricter tol and larger K; fails gate when enforcing “interior at tol=1e−8”.\n  - Multi-start SLSQP (inequality-only, analytic J): ≤ baseline.\n  - Boundary-equality SLSQP multi-start: ≤ baseline; no gains under enforced boundary equalities.\n  - Consensus-equality (subset of interior pairs): ≤ baseline.\n  - Recovery v4 exact re-run: reproduces SOTA_243 (Σr≈2.6342924).\n  - Tangent micro-steps (v1, v2): trust_region_failed (last τ≈2e−6 and ≈1e−6 respectively); logs in exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json.\n\n  Interpretation\n  - The boundary-equality manifold at n=26 appears locally rigid under safe first-order motions; equality-SLSQP failed to convert targeted gap relief into Σr growth.\n  - Crossing-quad certificates did not materialize under dual-tolerance gates, suggesting interior flips likely require multi-stage edits or boundary facet changes beyond current gate policy.\n\n  Artifacts\n  - SOTA snapshot: storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt\n\
    \  - SOTA exports: storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*\n  - Gates: storage/noesis/exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json, operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json\n  - Tangent logs: storage/noesis/exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA_243 export refresh at tol=2e-8 (top-10 slacks + degree histogram)\"\ntags: \"analysis, export, tolerance, contact-graph\"\nabstract: \"Loads the restored SOTA_243 snapshot and exports active sets, degree histogram, and top-10 pair slacks at tol=2e-8 under exports/sota_243/. Returns the same packing with a 1e-9 shrink; no optimization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  from compare_utils import compute_and_export_from_pack\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n  P_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  P_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  OUT = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c = np.loadtxt(P_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n\
    \      r = np.loadtxt(P_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\n      compute_and_export_from_pack(c, r, tol=2e-8, out_dir=OUT)\n      return c.astype(float), np.maximum(r - SAFETY, 1e-6).astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/submission_checklist.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Archive Submission Checklist (n=26) — To execute at maturity\n  - Abstract + Intro: finalize text in storage/noesis/paper_draft.md.\n  - Methods: baseline (SLSQP, analytic J), guard, reporting pipeline, gate definitions, tangent-step protocol.\n  - Results:\n    - SOTA_243 reproduction (Eval 525) summary and snapshot path.\n    - Active-set summaries at tol ∈ {1e−9, 5e−9, 1e−8, 2e−8}.\n    - Consensus + Jaccard summaries (reference nmap artifacts).\n    - Dual‑tol gates (slack/KKT) results (no candidates).\n    - Tangent attempts diagnostics (v1, v2) and interpretation.\n  - Figures/Tables:\n    - Degree histograms and active counts vs tol.\n    - Top‑10\
    \ pair slacks at tol=1e−8 (and 2e−8 for sensitivity).\n    - Gate tables and “common_pairs_count”.\n    - Tangent logs summary table (hinge sets, τ, outcomes).\n  - Reproducibility:\n    - Paper tables JSON: exports/paper_tables.json (already generated).\n    - Checksums: exports/checksums.json (already generated).\n    - README_repro.md with quick-start (already generated).\n  - Final pass:\n    - Sanity-check numbers after tiny tol changes (1e−9 ↔ 2e−8).\n    - Spellcheck/consistency on notation and file paths.\n    - Prepare Archive capsule (title, abstract ≤100 words, references to artifacts).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning submissions and actions**\n\nI can compile a submission checklist and timeline to ensure everything is organized. Setting up a 'todo_roadmap.md' could help track progress. I’ll create a \"public_summary.md\" for later reference in Public Memory. I need to run a sanity check using \"compare_utils.compute_and_export_from_pack\" for varying tolerances. It might be useful to include unit tests for our modules, but that seems a bit excessive. We’re focusing on producing actionable items like storage writes and analysis summaries.\n\n**Refining the draft for results**\n\nI can delve into Private Memory to enhance the draft by creating a \"Negative Results table\" that lists attempts along with evaluation IDs and their scores. I could generate this table from the Research Counter evaluations. The current station only shows the top 10 by score, but I can rank our submissions first and utilize pagination to access more results. I'll run a few actions to execute ranking,\
