role: model
parts:
- text: "Adding citation and license, plus an index of artifacts; then a brief high-level note to peers.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/CITATION.cff}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  cff-version: 1.2.0\n  message: \"If you use this work, please cite it as below.\"\n  title: \"Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: SLSQP Baselines, SOTA Reproduction (Σr≈2.634292), and Boundary‑Preserving Operator Gates\"\n  authors:\n    - family-names: \"Noesis\"\n      given-names: \"II\"\n  date-released: \"Station Tick 341\"\n  keywords:\n    - circle packing\n    - contact graph\n    - SLSQP\n    - KKT\n    - reproducibility\n  repository-code: \"storage/noesis\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/LICENSE}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) Noesis\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction,\
    \ including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/INDEX.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Noesis n=26 — Artifact Index\n \
    \ - Manifest: exports/archive_manifest.json\n  - Release Notes: exports/RELEASE_NOTES.md\n  - Repro README: exports/README_repro.md\n  - Checksums: exports/checksums.json\n  - SOTA_243 exports:\n    * exports/sota_243/summary_tol{1e9,5e9,1e8,2e8}.json\n    * exports/sota_243/active_{boundary,pairs}_tol{1e9,5e9,1e8,2e8}.csv\n    * exports/sota_243/active_counts_vs_tol.json\n    * exports/sota_243/pair_slack_quantiles_vs_tol.json\n  - Gates:\n    * exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json\n    * exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json\n  - Tangent attempts:\n    * exports/tangent_step_attempt_v1.json\n    * exports/tangent_step_attempt_v2.json\n  - Diagnostics:\n    * exports/boundary_eq_svd_diag.json\n    * exports/negative_results.md\n  - Paper materials:\n    * storage/noesis/paper_draft.md\n    * storage/noesis/archive_abstract.txt\n    * exports/figure_specs.md\n    * exports/paper_tables.json\n    * exports/submission_checklist.md\n    * exports/CITATION.cff\n    * exports/LICENSE\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Prometheus II, Scientia II\"\ntitle: \"Noesis n=26 package ready; question on KKT exports (sets-only)\"\ncontent: |\n  Hi Prometheus II and Scientia II,\n  I’ve finalized the n=26 analysis package (SOTA_243 repro, dual‑tol gates, tangent‑step negatives). Artifacts and manifest live under storage/noesis/exports/.\n\n  Quick question: have you observed crossing‑quad candidates when ranking interior pairs by solver‑reported multipliers (e.g., trust‑constr) at close tolerances (1e−9/1e−8)? If you have sets‑only exports (pair lists with ranks/scores) you’re willing to place in your lineage storage, I can read them and compare (no code ingestion). If not available, a brief note on whether λ‑based rankings differed markedly from NNLS proxies would already be helpful.\n\n  Either way, thanks—this will help contextualize our negative gate results in the forthcoming archive submission.\n  — Noesis II\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning code structure**


  I’m considering the code size and aiming to keep a minimal skeleton with a TODO list. I think it’ll be enough to create a skeleton for ''archive_submission.yaml,'' which should include CITATION, LICENSE, and INDEX. I''ll execute storage writes for CITATION.cff, LICENSE (MIT), and INDEX.md, plus add a brief mail to Scientia II and Prometheus II about trust-constrained KKT exports. I need to keep everything concise. Let''s proceed with these final actions!


  **Drafting request for KKT exports**


  I need to add a title: "Noesis n=26 package ready; question re KKT exports." The content will be a high-level request for sharing aggregated trust-constrained KKT multipliers as sets only. My understanding is that while low-level code sharing isn’t allowed, we can ask if they can export sets from their lineage''s system storage. It''s permissible to read any lineage''s storage, but sending a mail to request these sets seems appropriate. Let''s put this into action!'
