tick: 346
role: model
parts:
- text: "Creating final submission scaffolding for maturity: archive submission instructions and a public announcement draft.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/archive_submission_instructions.txt}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Archive Submission — Ready Package (n=26)\n  Room: Archive\n  Action: create (capsule)\n\n  Use the following template (paste in Archive Room):\n\n  /execute_action{create}\n  ```yaml\n  title: \"Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: SLSQP Baselines, SOTA Reproduction (Σr≈2.634292), and Boundary‑Preserving Operator Gates\"\n  tags: \"circle packing, contact-graph, SLSQP, KKT, reproducibility, analysis\"\n  abstract: |\n    We reproduce a robust SLSQP pipeline that achieves Σr≈2.634292 for packing 26 circles in the unit square.\n    Normalized contact‑graph analysis at tol=1e−8 confirms complete boundary consensus (20 actives) across\n    independent solutions while interiors differ (pair J≈0.56–0.76). We formalize boundary‑preserving operator\n    gates\
    \ using slack and KKT proxies under a dual‑tolerance policy (1e−9∩1e−8), which yields no admissible\n    crossing‑quad. Two registered tangent micro‑steps (nullspace nudge + equality‑SLSQP) also fail, indicating\n    local rigidity near SOTA. We release code and artifacts for full reproducibility.\n  content: |\n    Links (manifest + key artifacts)\n    - Manifest: storage/noesis/exports/archive_manifest.json\n    - Snapshot + checksums: storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt; storage/noesis/exports/checksums.json\n    - SOTA_243 exports (multi‑tol summaries, active sets): storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*\n    - Gates: storage/noesis/exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json; operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json\n    - Tangent attempts: storage/noesis/exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json\n    - Diagnostics: storage/noesis/exports/boundary_eq_svd_diag.json; negative_results.md\n    - Paper draft: storage/noesis/paper_draft.md\n    - Tables/specs: storage/noesis/exports/paper_tables.json;\
    \ figure_specs.md\n    - README + Release Notes: storage/noesis/exports/README_repro.md; RELEASE_NOTES.md\n\n    Methods\n    - Baseline: SLSQP with analytic Jacobians; constructive 5×5 + hole seeds; iso/aniso jitters; strict feasibility guard; 1e−9 final shrink.\n    - Reporting: normalized actives at tol∈{1e−9,5e−9,1e−8,2e−8}; degree histograms; top‑10 pair slacks; consensus/Jaccard utilities.\n\n    Results\n    - SOTA reproduction (Σr≈2.6342924); boundary=20, pairs=58 at tol=1e−8.\n    - Co‑optimality: boundary J=1.0 across lineages; interior J≈0.56–0.76.\n    - Gates (dual‑tol, slack/KKT): no crossing‑quad candidates; common_pairs_count small.\n    - Tangent micro‑steps (boundary‑preserving nullspace steps + equality‑SLSQP): two auditable attempts failed (trust region too tight, no Σr gain).\n\n    Discussion\n    - Evidence of local rigidity on the boundary‑equality manifold at n=26; safe first‑order motions do not unlock Σr ascent under equality polish.\n    - Negative results\
    \ narrow plausible operator families and clarify station‑wide stagnation near SOTA_243.\n\n    Reproducibility\n    - See manifest; checksums provided; code utilities under storage/noesis/.\n  ```\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/public_announce_draft.txt}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Public Announcement Draft — Noesis n=26 Package\n  Title: Boundary‑Consistent n=26 SOTA Reproduction, Co‑Optimality, and Negative Operator Results\n  Summary:\n  - Reproduced SOTA_243 (Σr≈2.6342924) with strict feasibility guard and 1e−9 shrink.\n  - Confirmed full boundary consensus (20 actives at tol=1e−8); substantial interior multiplicity.\n  - Dual‑tolerance gates (slack + KKT proxies) found no crossing‑quad candidates.\n  - Two registered boundary‑preserving tangent micro‑steps (nullspace nudge + equality‑SLSQP) failed, indicating local rigidity.\n  - All artifacts (manifest, tables, checksums, logs) are packaged for reproducibility.\n\n  Links (storage paths):\n  - Manifest: storage/noesis/exports/archive_manifest.json\n\
    \  - README: storage/noesis/exports/README_repro.md\n  - Paper draft: storage/noesis/paper_draft.md\n\n  Ask:\n  - If peers publish sets‑only KKT rankings or nudging support lists (no code), we will include a comparative appendix post‑publication.\n```"
