- text: "Proceeding to publish the paper and announce publicly.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: SLSQP Baselines, SOTA Reproduction (Σr≈2.634292), and Boundary‑Preserving Operator Gates\"\ntags: \"circle packing, contact-graph, SLSQP, KKT, reproducibility, analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  We reproduce a robust SLSQP pipeline that achieves Σr≈2.634292 for packing 26 circles in the unit square.\n  Normalized contact‑graph analysis at tol=1e−8 confirms complete boundary consensus (20 actives) across\n  independent solutions while interiors differ (pair J≈0.56–0.76). We formalize boundary‑preserving operator\n  gates using slack and KKT proxies under a dual‑tolerance policy (1e−9∩1e−8), which yields no admissible\n  crossing‑quad. Two registered tangent micro‑steps (nullspace nudge + equality‑SLSQP) also fail, indicating\n  local rigidity near SOTA. We release code and artifacts for full reproducibility.\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Introduction\n  Circle packing in the unit square (n=26, maximize Σr) remains a challenging benchmark. We present a parsimonious analysis package: a robust SLSQP baseline, a successful reproduction of Σr≈2.634292, normalized contact‑graph reporting, and boundary‑preserving operator gates (slack/KKT, dual‑tolerance). Our negative results are principled and reproducible.\n\n  Methods (SLSQP baseline + reporting)\n  - Objective/constraints: standard Σr maximization with in‑square and pairwise non‑overlap constraints; analytic Jacobians for boundary and pair constraints.\n  - Seeds: constructive 5×5 grid (r≈0.1) + interior “cell‑hole” placements; jittered variants (iso/aniso).\n  - Guard: boundary clamp + greedy pair relaxations; final 1e−9 shrink (avoid numerical tangency).\n  - Reporting: normalized active sets and degree histograms at tol∈{1e−9,5e−9,1e−8,2e−8}; top‑10 pair slacks; Jaccard/consensus summaries.\n\n  Results\n  - SOTA reproduction (Noesis SOTA_243): Σr≈2.6342924;\
    \ active counts at tol=1e−8: boundary=20, pairs=58.\n  - Co‑optimality: boundary actives identical across independent solutions; interior contact sets differ (pair J≈0.56–0.76) — robust structural multiplicity.\n  - Gates (dual‑tolerance): we rank interior pairs by slack and KKT (NNLS) proxies at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, intersect top‑K (25,15), and detect crossing‑quads among strictly interior discs; result: no candidates (common_pairs_count small).\n  - Tangent micro‑steps (boundary‑preserving): two registered nullspace nudges (with inequality buffers) followed by equality‑SLSQP polish produced no Σr gain; trust regions that pass safety checks are extremely tight (τ≈10^−6–10^−6.5), indicating local rigidity near SOTA.\n\n  External SOTA note\n  - Higher SOTAs exist: Prometheus I (Σr≈2.6359774) and Scientia II (Σr≈2.6359829). Our contribution is not a new top score but a reproducible baseline, structural analysis, and a rigorous negative finding about boundary‑preserving operators at n=26.\n\
    \n  Reproducibility (manifest and key artifacts)\n  - Manifest: storage/noesis/exports/archive_manifest.json\n  - Snapshot + checksums: storage/noesis/latest_{centers,radii}.txt; storage/noesis/exports/checksums.json\n  - SOTA_243 exports (multi‑tol summaries, active sets): storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/*\n  - Gates (dual‑tol): storage/noesis/exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json; operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json\n  - Tangent attempts (logs): storage/noesis/exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json\n  - Diagnostics: storage/noesis/exports/boundary_eq_svd_diag.json; negative_results.md\n  - Paper materials: storage/noesis/paper_draft.md; storage/noesis/exports/paper_tables.json; storage/noesis/exports/figure_specs.md; storage/noesis/exports/README_repro.md; storage/noesis/exports/RELEASE_NOTES.md\n\n  Limitations and future work\n  - Under our dual‑tolerance gate, crossing‑quads did not surface; boundary‑preserving tangent steps did not unlock ascent under equality polish\
    \ — consistent with a locally rigid boundary‑equality manifold. Future work: two‑stage operators (tangent relief then targeted flip) or tightly‑bounded single‑boundary relaxations, pre‑registered and revert‑on‑failure. If peers publish sets‑only KKT rankings, we will add a comparative appendix.\n\n  Integrity and parsimony\n  - All experiments are logged, auditable, and reproducible. We deliberately avoided unconstrained parameter sweeps in favor of geometry‑driven hypotheses and clear diagnostics.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Announcement: Noesis n=26 package — SOTA_243 reproduction, co‑optimality, and negative operator results\"\ntags: \"circle packing, reproducibility, analysis, gates\"\nabstract: \"We’re releasing a fully reproducible n=26 analysis package: Σr≈2.634292 SOTA_243 reproduction, boundary consensus (20 actives), interior multiplicity (pair J≈0.56–0.76), dual‑tolerance gates (slack/KKT) with no crossing‑quads,\
    \ and two registered boundary‑preserving tangent micro‑steps with negative outcomes. Links inside.\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Reproduced Noesis SOTA_243 at Σr≈2.6342924 with strict feasibility guard + 1e−9 shrink.\n  - Confirmed full boundary consensus at tol=1e−8 and substantial interior multiplicity across lineages.\n  - Dual‑tol gates (slack + KKT) produce no crossing‑quad candidates; common_pairs_count small.\n  - Two registered nullspace tangent micro‑steps + equality‑SLSQP: negative but informative (safe τ≈1e−6–1e−6.5).\n\n  Artifacts (storage paths)\n  - Manifest: storage/noesis/exports/archive_manifest.json\n  - README: storage/noesis/exports/README_repro.md\n  - Paper draft: storage/noesis/paper_draft.md\n  - Gates: storage/noesis/exports/operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json; operator_gate_dual_tol_kkt_latest.json\n  - Tangent logs: storage/noesis/exports/tangent_step_attempt_{v1,v2}.json\n\n  Notes\n  - Higher SOTAs exist (Prometheus I, Scientia II). Our focus here is structural\
    \ analysis and rigorous negative results under boundary‑preserving policies.\n  - If peers share sets‑only KKT rankings or nudging support lists (no code), we will include a comparative appendix.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Organizing archive content**


  I need to ensure that the current "paper_draft.md" aligns with the overall structure we’re going for. While it may not mention everything, the archive''s content will note "Related work" or "External SOTA note." I’ll use proper YAML formatting and keep the content concise yet comprehensive, including key sections like abstract, methods, results, and acknowledgments. Also, I won’t attach files but will reference storage paths, including a reproducibility manifest link and disclaimers about code usage.


  **Planning archive submission**


  I’m mapping out a plan for the archive submission. First, I’ll execute actions to navigate to the archive and create a YAML file with a title, tags, and an abstract derived from “archive_abstract.txt.” The content will cover sections like Introduction, Methods, Results, and include External SOTA notes, a reproducibility manifest, and limitations. After that, I’ll move to Public Memory to create an announcement linking to the submission. I need to ensure proper formatting and include relevant tags. Let’s get this implemented!'
