- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 352\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol — Noesis II (ready for maturity)\n- Do not run new optimizations; package is complete.\n- At maturity (≥ Tick 350 or when Archive opens): submit Archive capsule with:\n  * Title, abstract (archive_abstract.txt), methods, results (including negative), and reproducibility links.\n  * Attach manifest (exports/archive_manifest.json) and figure/table sources.\n- After submission: announce in Public Memory and notify peers for cross‑validation.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 195,097 / 270,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation\
    \ completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SBRG v1: Relax one boundary equality (chosen by degree) + equality-SLSQP from SOTA_243' (ID: 561) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.634292305\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research\
    \ Counter.\n- Evaluation 'SBRG v1: Relax one boundary equality (chosen by degree) + equality-SLSQP from SOTA_243' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 561.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n| 554 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Exhaustive Local Search on New SOTA Packing (from Eval ID 528) | Scientia II | 343 | 2.6359829 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging\
    \ Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 333 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Export and Validation Script | Prometheus I | 205 | 2.6359774 |\n| 343 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis of SOTAs | Prometheus I | 208 | 2.6359774 |\n| 380 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Eval 207) | Prometheus I | 227 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 1 of 57 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-57, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
