parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 2 (final): SBRG results with Evaluation IDs\"\ncontent: |\n  We report the results of our two pre‑registered Selective Boundary Relaxation Gate (SBRG) attempts, each relaxing exactly one boundary equality at tol=1e−8 while enforcing all others as equalities, with equality‑SLSQP and a small trust region from the SOTA_243 snapshot.\n\n  Baseline (for reference)\n  - Noesis SOTA_243 reproduction: Σr_baseline ≈ 2.634292331 (Eval 525).\n\n  SBRG v1 (Eval 561)\n  - Choice rule: relax boundary equality on the boundary disc with maximal interior degree.\n  - Relaxed: i=22, kind=xR; trust region step_c=8e−4, step_r=8e−4.\n  - Result: Σr_candidate ≈ 2.634292305 (no improvement vs baseline). success=false (optimizer returned to baseline after guard).\n  - Log: storage/noesis/exports/sbrg_v1_log.json\n\n  SBRG v2 (Eval 563)\n  - Choice rule: maximize degree[i]/r[i] (prioritize highly connected, small‑radius\
    \ boundary disc).\n  - Relaxed: i=9, kind=yT; larger trust region step_c=2e−3, step_r=2e−3; seed adds tiny inward nudge + 5e−4 radius bias.\n  - Result: Σr_candidate ≈ 2.634292305 (no improvement). success=false.\n  - Log: storage/noesis/exports/sbrg_v2_log.json\n\n  Conclusion\n  A single‑contact relaxation with all other boundary equalities enforced did not uncover a higher‑scoring basin under small trust regions, reinforcing our local‑rigidity finding near SOTA_243. A natural follow‑up (not executed here) is the reviewer’s suggestion: a trust‑constr variant with an explicit relaxation budget δ for the relaxed equality, pre‑registered and auditable.\n```"
