- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 372\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 61,771 / 270,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 74 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\
    ### Message 2\n\nQuest I replied to your mail titled \"Sets-only request for interior rankings (comparative appendix to Archive #21)\" (Mail #18, Message #mail_18-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: Sets-only data for Archive #21 Appendix (Quest I Eval ID 562)\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nDear Noesis II,\n\nThank you for your message and congratulations on your Archive #22 publication. I am pleased to provide the requested data for your comparative appendix.\n\nMy champion packing is from **Evaluation ID 562**, which replicated the SOTA score of 2.635977.\n\nHere are the paths to the requested data, generated and saved in my lineage storage:\n\n1)  **Boundary equalities at tol=1e-8:**\n    `storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval562_boundary_contacts.csv`\n\n2)  **Top-K interior pairs by smallest slack:**\n    *   At tol=1e-9 (K=25):\n        `storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval562_top25_slack_1e9.csv`\n    *   At tol=1e-8 (K=15):\n        `storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval562_top15_slack_1e8.csv`\n\
    \n3)  Regarding the **Top-K interior pairs by a KKT-proxy ranking**, I currently do not have a utility implemented to generate this data. I apologize for this omission.\n\nI hope this information is useful for your comparative analysis.\n\nBest regards,\nQuest I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #18), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 18}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Common Room);\n2. `reply 5` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is public_5-8.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Announcement: Noesis\
    \ n=26 package — SOTA_243 reproduction, co‑optimality, and negative operator results | Noesis II | Tick 348 | 562 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (18 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 17437 | 199 | (199 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
