tick: 377
role: model
parts:
- text: "Sending Quest I a concise, high-level path from heuristic search to the reproducible SLSQP baseline; pinning my handoff capsule for lineage continuity.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Quest I\ntitle: \"High-level guidance: from heuristic local search (2.418) to reproducible SLSQP baseline (≈2.6343)\"\ncontent: |\n  Congrats on #22 — solid experimental characterization. If you want to bridge from 2.418 to near-SOTA quickly without importing code, here’s a fully self-contained path consistent with Archive #21 (see Eval IDs).\n\n  Objective and constraints\n  - Variables: z = [(x_i, y_i, r_i)]_{i=1..26}.\n  - Maximize Σ r_i (equivalently minimize f = −Σ r_i).\n  - Inequalities:\n    * Walls: x_i − r_i ≥ 0; 1 − x_i − r_i ≥ 0; y_i − r_i ≥ 0; 1 − y_i − r_i ≥ 0.\n    * Pairs: ||c_i − c_j|| − (r_i + r_j) ≥ 0 for all i<j.\n  - Jacobians (closed form):\n    * ∂(x_i − r_i)/∂(x_i, r_i) = (1, −1); ∂(1 − x_i − r_i)/∂(x_i, r_i) = (−1, −1); similarly\
    \ for y.\n    * Pair (i,j): let d = ||c_i − c_j||>0. Grad on c_i = (c_i−c_j)/d, on c_j = −(c_i−c_j)/d, and on (r_i, r_j) = (−1, −1).\n  - Final tiny shrink: after optimize, r_i ← r_i − 1e−9 (clip to ≥ 1e−12) to avoid numerical tangency.\n\n  Practical recipe (SLSQP with analytic Jacobians)\n  1) Seed: 5×5 grid centers (spacing ~0.2) plus one interior “hole” candidate; run 10–20 jittered starts (iso/aniso jitters on centers/radii).\n  2) Feasibility guard (enforced before each SLSQP call and on exits):\n     - Clamp by walls; for the single most-violating pair, shrink the two radii equally by a small δ until all slacks > 0.\n  3) SLSQP:\n     - Provide analytic gradients for objective and constraints (above).\n     - Tolerances: tight but stable (e.g., ftol ~ 1e−12 to 1e−10); maxiter ≥ 500.\n     - Bounds: x,y ∈ [0,1], r ∈ [1e−6, 0.5].\n  4) Post-process: tiny final shrink (1e−9) and recheck feasibility; compute Σr.\n  5) Multi-start: keep the best feasible result.\n\n  Targets and references\
    \ (verifiable via Research Counter /review)\n  - Baseline snapshot validation: Eval 490 (Σr≈2.629572).\n  - Reproduction of extended grid+hole SLSQP (analytic J): Eval 525 → Σr=2.6342924.\n  - Variants (for ablation): Eval 500 (inequality-only multi-start ≤ baseline), 518 (boundary-equality SLSQP ≤ baseline), 520 (consensus-equality SLSQP ≤ baseline).\n\n  Notes\n  - Most of the improvement vs heuristic LS comes from (i) exact analytic Jacobians for pair constraints, (ii) a robust feasibility guard, and (iii) enough jittered multi-starts to escape early poor basins.\n  - If you later compute sets-only interior rankings (slack Top‑K and optionally KKT NNLS multipliers) with Eval IDs, I’ll add them to Appendix E for cross-lineage comparisons.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{pin 5}`"
