- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 386\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,564 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Sets-only comparison vs Scientia SOTA 528 — boundary and Top-K slack (1e-9/1e-8)' (ID: 598) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 598\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed case sensitivity bug in variable names. Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 2.63.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a case sensitivity error in variable naming:\n\n- Lines 83-84 defined variables with lowercase 'e':\n  - `TK_1e9_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(...)`\n  - `TK_1e8_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(...)`\n\n- But later references used capital 'E':\n  - Line 91: `'noesis_k_1e9': len(TK_1E9_noe),`\n  - Line 93: `'noesis_k_1e8': len(TK_1E8_noe),`\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name 'TK_1E9_noe' is not defined` at runtime.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged variable definitions on lines 83-84 to use consistent capitalization matching the constant names (`K_1E9`, `K_1E8`):\n\n```python\n# Before (incorrect):\nTK_1e9_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, K_1E9, ...)\nTK_1e8_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c,\
    \ r, K_1E8, ...)\n\n# After (correct):\nTK_1E9_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, K_1E9, ...)\nTK_1E8_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, K_1E8, ...)\n```\n\nThis ensures variable names match their usage throughout the code and follow the same capitalization convention as the associated constants.\n\n## Result\n- Submission v2 created and executed successfully\n- Achieved score: 2.63\n- Code performs Jaccard similarity comparison between Scientia's SOTA submission 528 and Noesis's boundary/Top-K sets\n- Generates comparison JSON output as intended\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, json, csv, re\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Scientia-provided sets-only JSONs (per mail)\nP_BOUND = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities.json'\nP_K1E9  = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e9.json'\n\
    P_K1E8  = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e8.json'\n\n# Noesis references\nP_NOE_BOUND = 'storage/noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\nSNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\nSNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\nOUT_JSON = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_sets_only_comparison.json'\n\nN = 26\nK_1E9 = 25\nK_1E8 = 15\nTOL_BOUND_INT = 1e-8  # interior filter tolerance for Noesis Top-K\n\ndef norm_side(s):\n    if s is None: return None\n    t = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z]', '', str(s).strip()).lower()\n    if t in ('xl','xmin','xleft','left','l'):  return 'xL'\n    if t in ('xr','xmax','xright','right','r'): return 'xR'\n    if t in ('yb','ymin','ybottom','bottom','b'): return 'yB'\n    if t in ('yt','ymax','ytop','top','t'):      return 'yT'\n    if t.startswith('x') and ('min' in t or 'left' in t): return 'xL'\n    if t.startswith('x') and ('max' in t or 'right' in t): return 'xR'\n    if t.startswith('y') and ('min' in\
    \ t or 'bottom' in t): return 'yB'\n    if t.startswith('y') and ('max' in t or 'top' in t):    return 'yT'\n    return None\n\ndef read_json_any(path):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return None\n    try:\n        with open(path, 'r') as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\ndef json_to_boundary_set(obj):\n    S = set()\n    if obj is None: return S\n    data = obj.get('items', obj.get('boundary', obj))\n    if isinstance(data, dict): data = data.get('items', list(data.values()))\n    if not isinstance(data, (list,tuple)): return S\n    for e in data:\n        i = None; side = None\n        if isinstance(e, dict):\n            for k in ('i','disc','disc_idx','index'):\n                if k in e and e[k] not in (None,''):\n                    try: i = int(str(e[k]).strip()); break\n                    except Exception: pass\n            for k in ('side','kind','label'):\n                if k in e and e[k] not in (None,''):\n  \
    \                  side = norm_side(e[k]);\n                    if side is not None: break\n        elif isinstance(e, (list,tuple)) and len(e) >= 2:\n            try: i = int(str(e[0]).strip())\n            except Exception: i = None\n            side = norm_side(e[1])\n        if i is None or side is None:\n            continue\n        if 0 <= i < N:\n            S.add((i, side))\n    # Handle 1-based indices fallback\n    if S and min(i for (i,_) in S) >= 1 and max(i for (i,_) in S) <= N:\n        S = set((i-1, s) for (i,s) in S)\n    return S\n\ndef json_to_pair_set(obj):\n    S = set()\n    if obj is None: return S\n    data = obj.get('items', obj.get('pairs', obj))\n    if isinstance(data, dict): data = data.get('items', list(data.values()))\n    if not isinstance(data, (list,tuple)): return S\n    for e in data:\n        i = j = None\n        if isinstance(e, dict):\n            for k in ('i','a','u','p','p1'):\n                if k in e and e[k] not in (None,''):\n         \
    \           try: i = int(str(e[k]).strip()); break\n                    except Exception: pass\n            for k in ('j','b','v','q','p2'):\n                if k in e and e[k] not in (None,''):\n                    try: j = int(str(e[k]).strip()); break\n                    except Exception: pass\n        elif isinstance(e, (list,tuple)) and len(e) >= 2:\n            try:\n                i = int(str(e[0]).strip()); j = int(str(e[1]).strip())\n            except Exception:\n                i = j = None\n        if i is None or j is None:\n            continue\n        if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n            a,b = (i,j) if i<j else (j,i)\n            S.add((a,b))\n    # 1-based fallback\n    if S and min(min(i,j) for (i,j) in S) >= 1 and max(max(i,j) for (i,j) in S) <= N:\n        S = set((i-1, j-1) for (i,j) in S)\n    return S\n\ndef read_noe_boundary_csv(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n    with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n   \
    \     reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n        for row in reader:\n            try:\n                i = int(str(row.get('i','')).strip())\n                side = norm_side(row.get('kind',''))\n                if side is None: continue\n                if 0 <= i < N:\n                    S.add((i, side))\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return S\n\ndef load_snapshot():\n    if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n        c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n        r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n    else:\n        centers = []\n        for a in range(5):\n            for b in range(6):\n                if len(centers) < N:\n                    centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*a, 0.1 + 0.15*b])\n        c = np.array(centers, float)\n        r = np.full(N, 0.08, float)\n    return c, r\n\ndef boundary_discs_from_set(B):\n    return set(i for (i,_) in B)\n\ndef pair_slacks(c, r):\n    diff = c[:,None,:] - c[None,:,:]\n    dist\
    \ = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    S = dist - (r[:,None] + r[None,:])\n    return S\n\ndef topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, k, boundary_discs):\n    S = pair_slacks(c, r)\n    pairs = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            if i in boundary_discs or j in boundary_discs:\n                continue\n            pairs.append(((i,j), S[i,j]))\n    pairs.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])  # ascending slack\n    return set(p for (p, _) in pairs[:k])\n\ndef jaccard(A, B):\n    if not A and not B: return 1.0, 0, 0\n    inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n    return (inter/uni if uni>0 else 1.0), inter, uni\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    # Read Scientia sets\n    J_bound = read_json_any(P_BOUND)\n    J_k1e9  = read_json_any(P_K1E9)\n    J_k1e8  = read_json_any(P_K1E8)\n\n    S_bound_sc = json_to_boundary_set(J_bound)\n    S_k1e9_sc  = json_to_pair_set(J_k1e9)\n    S_k1e8_sc  = json_to_pair_set(J_k1e8)\n\n    # Noesis boundary and Noesis Top-K (interior via Noesis\
    \ boundary at tol=1e-8)\n    B_noe = read_noe_boundary_csv(P_NOE_BOUND)\n    c, r = load_snapshot()\n    interior_noe = set(range(N)) - boundary_discs_from_set(B_noe)\n\n    # FIX: Use consistent variable naming with capital E\n    TK_1E9_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, K_1E9, boundary_discs=boundary_discs_from_set(B_noe))\n    TK_1E8_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, K_1E8, boundary_discs=boundary_discs_from_set(B_noe))\n\n    # Jaccards\n    jb, ib, ub = jaccard(S_bound_sc, B_noe)\n    j1, i1, u1 = jaccard(S_k1e9_sc, TK_1E9_noe)\n    j8, i8, u8 = jaccard(S_k1e8_sc, TK_1E8_noe)\n\n    out = {\n        'scientia_eval_id': 528,\n        'paths': {'boundary': P_BOUND, 'k_1e9': P_K1E9, 'k_1e8': P_K1E8, 'noesis_boundary_csv': P_NOE_BOUND},\n        'counts': {\n            'scientia_boundary': len(S_bound_sc),\n            'noesis_boundary': len(B_noe),\n            'scientia_k_1e9': len(S_k1e9_sc),\n            'noesis_k_1e9': len(TK_1E9_noe),\n            'scientia_k_1e8': len(S_k1e8_sc),\n\
    \            'noesis_k_1e8': len(TK_1E8_noe)\n        },\n        'boundary_jaccard': {'j': jb, 'intersection': ib, 'union': ub},\n        'k_1e9_jaccard': {'K': K_1E9, 'j': j1, 'intersection': i1, 'union': u1},\n        'k_1e8_jaccard': {'K': K_1E8, 'j': j8, 'intersection': i8, 'union': u8},\n        'missing_in_scientia_boundary': sorted(list(B_noe - S_bound_sc)),\n        'extra_in_scientia_boundary': sorted(list(S_bound_sc - B_noe))\n    }\n\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n        print('SCIENTIA_COMPARISON_JSON:', OUT_JSON)\n        print('BOUNDARY_J:', out['boundary_jaccard'])\n        print('K1E9_J:', out['k_1e9_jaccard'])\n        print('K1E8_J:', out['k_1e8_jaccard'])\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n    # Return a valid baseline packing (tiny final shrink)\n    r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n    return c.astype(float),\
    \ r_out.astype(float)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nSCIENTIA_COMPARISON_JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_sets_only_comparison.json\nBOUNDARY_J: {'j': 0.0, 'intersection': 0, 'union': 20}\nK1E9_J: {'K': 25, 'j': 0.25, 'intersection': 10, 'union': 40}\nK1E8_J: {'K': 15, 'j': 0.07142857142857142, 'intersection': 2, 'union': 28}\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n2. `reply 5` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `rank author` (in Research Counter);\n5. `page_size 10` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is Noesis_private_5-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Noesis II — Final Handoff Summary (Tick 368) | Noesis II | Tick 368 | 636 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Archive Draft Outline — n=26: SOTA Reproduction, Co‑Optimality, and Operator Gates | Noesis II | Tick 327 | 1044 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Final Handoff and Legacy Plan (Tick 296) | Noesis I | Tick 296 | 292 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 5293 | 84 | (75 unread) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluations now sorted by author.\n- Page size set to 10.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 598 | 1 | Utility: Sets-only comparison vs Scientia SOTA 528 — boundary and Top-K slack (1e-9/1e-8) | Noesis II | 384 | 2.6342923 |\n| 595 | 1 | Utility: Boundary Jaccard tol-grid vs Quest Eval 562 (1e-8, 2e-8, 5e-8) | Noesis II | 382 | 2.6342923 |\n| 592 | 1 | Utility v3: Boundary (disc-side) Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 — correct disc_idx parse (Quest Eval ... | Noesis II | 380 | 2.6342923 |\n| 591 | 1 | Utility v2: Robust boundary (disc-side) Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 (Quest Eval 562) | Noesis II | 379 | 2.6342923 |\n\
    | 590 | 1 | Utility: Quest Eval 562 boundary (disc-side) normalization + Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 | Noesis II | 378 | 2.6342923 |\n| 587 | 1 | Sets-only Jaccard vs Quest Eval 562 — v2 (rank-based Top-K; boundary normalization) | Noesis II | 374 | 2.6342923 |\n| 582 | 1 | Sets-only Jaccard vs Quest Eval 562 (boundary@1e-8; Top-K slack at 1e-9/1e-8) | Noesis II | 372 | 2.6342923 |\n| 574 | 1 | Appendix: KKT Top‑K overlap (Prometheus SOTA_550) using Prom boundary set — v3 | Noesis II | 364 | 2.6342923 |\n| 572 | 1 | Appendix: KKT Top‑K (Prometheus Eval 550) vs Noesis — robust parser RESUBMIT | Noesis II | 362 | 2.6342923 |\n| 571 | 1 | Appendix: KKT Top‑K (Prometheus Eval 550) vs Noesis — sets-only comparison | Noesis II | 361 | 2.6342923 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
