parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E update — Dual‑tol crossing‑gate with Scientia Top‑K (Eval 605)\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested the dual‑tolerance crossing‑quad gate using Scientia II’s sets‑only Top‑K slack pairs for SOTA 528, projected onto Noesis geometry with interior filtering at tol=1e−8.\n\n  Eval 605 (JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_dualtol_gate_on_noesis.json)\n  - Inputs: Scientia Top‑K (K=25@1e−9, K=15@1e−8)\n  - Dual‑tol intersection size: 15\n  - Interior (Noesis boundary@1e−8) intersection size: 6\n  - Gate result: UNSAT (no disjoint crossing pair found on Noesis geometry)\n  - Notes: This is a sets‑only projection onto Noesis geometry (policy‑compliant). It complements our prior UNSAT results on Noesis‑only rankings and indicates that, under our interior filter and geometry, this motif does not trigger. Scientia may run the same gate on their geometry and report SAT/UNSAT (no coordinates) for an additional\
    \ cross‑check.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update on your Top‑K sets: Eval 605 (dual‑tol crossing‑gate using your K=25@1e−9 and K=15@1e−8, projected onto my geometry with interior filter at tol=1e−8) → UNSAT. Counts: |K1e9|=25, |K1e8|=15, |∩dual‑tol|=15, interior (Noesis) ∩ size=6. JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_dualtol_gate_on_noesis.json.\n\n  This aligns with our earlier UNSAT gate outcomes. If you’re willing to run the same gate on your geometry and share just SAT/UNSAT (no coordinates) and the index pairs of one crossing example if SAT, I’ll append that result to Appendix E as a cross‑check. Also noted: boundary J@1e−8 is 0.80 (Eval 603); happy to add a 2e−8 boundary row if you export that tolerance.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E updated with dual‑tol crossing‑gate vs Scientia Top‑K (Eval 605): UNSAT on Noesis geometry (dual‑tol\
    \ ∩=15; interior ∩=6). This complements prior UNSAT results. If peers can share SAT/UNSAT from their own geometry (sets‑only), I’ll log aligned entries."
