tick: 395
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Scientia boundary@2e-8 Jaccard vs Noesis boundary@2e-8 (schema-verified)\"\ntags: \"utility, boundary, sets-only, jaccard, tolerance\"\nabstract: \"Parses Scientia’s 2e−8 boundary JSON (0-based {disc, side} under boundary_equalities), compares to Noesis boundary derived from snapshot slacks at tol=2e−8; logs counts, intersection/union, Jaccard, and diff sets; returns baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv, re\n  import numpy as np\n\n  P_BOUND_SCI = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json'\n  OUT_JSON    = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_boundary_jaccard_tol2e8.json'\n\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 2e-8\n\n  def norm_side(s):\n      if s is None: return None\n      t = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z]', '', str(s).strip()).lower()\n      if\
    \ t in ('xl','xmin','xleft','left','l'):  return 'xL'\n      if t in ('xr','xmax','xright','right','r'): return 'xR'\n      if t in ('yb','ymin','ybottom','bottom','b'): return 'yB'\n      if t in ('yt','ymax','ytop','top','t'):      return 'yT'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('min' in t or 'left' in t): return 'xL'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('max' in t or 'right' in t): return 'xR'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('min' in t or 'bottom' in t): return 'yB'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('max' in t or 'top' in t):    return 'yT'\n      return None\n\n  def read_scientia_boundary(path):\n      S = set()\n      meta = {'exists': os.path.exists(path), 'parsed': 0, 'rows': 0}\n      if not meta['exists']: return S, meta\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          obj = json.load(f)\n      items = obj.get('boundary_equalities', [])\n      if not isinstance(items, list):\n          items = obj.get('items', obj.get('boundary', []))\n          if isinstance(items, dict):\n         \
    \     items = list(items.values())\n      for e in items:\n          meta['rows'] += 1\n          if not isinstance(e, dict): \n              continue\n          i_raw = e.get('disc', e.get('i', e.get('disc_idx', None)))\n          s_raw = e.get('side', e.get('kind', e.get('label', None)))\n          try:\n              i = int(str(i_raw).strip())\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          side = norm_side(s_raw)\n          if side is None: \n              continue\n          # per Scientia: 0-based indices\n          if 0 <= i < N:\n              S.add((i, side)); meta['parsed'] += 1\n          elif 1 <= i <= N:\n              S.add((i-1, side)); meta['parsed'] += 1\n      return S, meta\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      else:\n          centers = []\n          for a in range(5):\n    \
    \          for b in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < N:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*a, 0.1 + 0.15*b])\n          c = np.array(centers, float)\n          r = np.full(N, 0.08, float)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, tol=TOL):\n      S = set()\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      s = {\n          'xL': x - r,\n          'xR': 1.0 - x - r,\n          'yB': y - r,\n          'yT': 1.0 - y - r\n      }\n      for i in range(N):\n          for side, slack in s.items():\n              if slack[i] <= tol + 1e-12:\n                  S.add((i, side))\n      return S\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      S_sci, meta = read_scientia_boundary(P_BOUND_SCI)\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      S_noe = boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, tol=TOL)\n\n      inter = len(S_sci & S_noe)\n      uni   = len(S_sci | S_noe) if (S_sci or S_noe) else 0\n      j     = (inter / uni) if uni > 0 else 1.0\n\n      out = {\n          'paths': {'scientia_boundary_2e8':\
    \ P_BOUND_SCI},\n          'tol': TOL,\n          'scientia_count': len(S_sci),\n          'noesis_count': len(S_noe),\n          'intersection': inter,\n          'union': uni,\n          'jaccard': j,\n          'missing_in_scientia': sorted(list(S_noe - S_sci)),\n          'extra_in_scientia': sorted(list(S_sci - S_noe)),\n          'meta': meta,\n          'note': 'Boundary comparison at tol=2e-8 using schema-verified {disc, side} with 0-based indices.'\n      }\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n          print('SCIENTIA_BOUNDARY_TOL2E8_JSON:', OUT_JSON)\n          print('COUNTS sci/noe/int/uni:', len(S_sci), len(S_noe), inter, uni)\n          print('JACCARD:', j)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n      # Return baseline pack (tiny final shrink) for valid evaluation\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n    \
    \  return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for exporting boundary@2e−8 and for running the gate on your side. I’ve queued a schema‑verified boundary@2e−8 Jaccard vs my snapshot at the same tol (Eval pending). Once it finishes, I’ll append the result (with JSON path) to Appendix E and send you the “missing/extra” disc‑side entries if any remain.\n\n  Also noted: I’ll incorporate your gate SAT/UNSAT outcome (sets‑only) when you have it, to log both geometries side‑by‑side.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Coding Utility Function**\n\nI'm preparing to code a utility titled \"Utility: Scientia boundary@2e-8 Jaccard vs Noesis boundary@2e-8 (schema-verified).\" The tags will include \"utility,\" \"boundary,\" \"sets-only,\" \"jaccard,\" and \"tolerance.\" \n\nThe abstract summarizes that it will parse Scientia's boundary JSON at 2e-8 and compare it to the Noesis boundary from the same snapshot, logging Jaccard and returning a baseline. \n\nI'll define functions like norm_side and read_scientia_boundary_json, handle necessary imports like 'np', and ensure proper output while printing counts. Let's get this implemented!"
