    : 0, \"noesis_count\": 25, \"note\": \"CSV was header-only; awaiting re-export with rows\" },\n        \"k15_1e8\": { \"eval_ids\": [609], \"jaccard\": 0.20 }\n      },\n      \"gate_on_noesis\": {\n        \"eval_ids\": [609, 613],\n        \"result\": \"UNSAT\",\n        \"dual_intersection_size\": 0,\n        \"interior_intersection_size\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    \"scientia\": {\n      \"champ_eval_id\": 528,\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"1e-8\": { \"eval_ids\": [603], \"jaccard\": 0.80, \"missing_in_scientia\": [[0,\"xL\"],[4,\"yT\"],[20,\"xR\"],[24,\"yT\"]] },\n        \"2e-8\": { \"eval_ids\": [617], \"jaccard\": 1.0, \"log\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_boundary_jaccard_tol2e8.json\" }\n      },\n      \"topk_slack\": {\n        \"k25_1e9\": { \"eval_ids\": [598], \"jaccard\": 0.25, \"intersection\": 10, \"union\": 40 },\n        \"k15_1e8\": { \"eval_ids\": [598], \"jaccard\": 0.0714285714, \"intersection\": 2, \"union\": 28 }\n      },\n      \"gate_on_noesis\"\
    : {\n        \"eval_ids\": [605],\n        \"result\": \"UNSAT\",\n        \"dual_intersection_size\": 15,\n        \"interior_intersection_size\": 6,\n        \"log\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_dualtol_gate_on_noesis.json\"\n      },\n      \"gate_on_scientia\": { \"status\": \"pending_sets_only_report\" }\n    },\n    \"prometheus\": {\n      \"sota_refs\": \"Prometheus SOTA around eval 298/550 (per nmap files); boundary sets at 2e-8 pending request.\",\n      \"kkt_topk\": {\n        \"k25_1e9\": { \"eval_ids\": [574], \"jaccard\": 0.2083 },\n        \"k15_1e8\": { \"eval_ids\": [574], \"jaccard\": 0.2273 }\n      },\n      \"boundary\": { \"1e-8\": { \"status\": \"not_run_here\" }, \"2e-8\": { \"status\": \"requested\" } }\n    },\n    \"takeaways\": [\n      \"Boundary equalities align across SOTAs at tol=2e-8 (J~1.0), confirming stable boundary structure.\",\n      \"Interior Top-K overlaps are modest (J~0.07–0.25 across pairs/tols), reinforcing co-optimal interior\
    \ multiplicity.\",\n      \"Dual-tolerance crossing-quad gate remains UNSAT when projected onto Noesis geometry for Quest and Scientia sets.\"\n    ]\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E — Consolidated cross‑lineage summary (JSON index + eval IDs)\"\ncontent: |\n  For readers’ convenience, Appendix E now includes a single machine‑readable index of all sets‑only comparisons assembled so far:\n\n  JSON index:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json\n\n  Highlights (all with verifiable eval IDs):\n  - Quest (Eval 604): boundary@2e−8 J=1.0 (Eval 609); K15@1e−8 J=0.20; K25@1e−9 CSV was header‑only (Eval 613) → pending re‑export; dual‑tol gate on Noesis geometry: UNSAT (Evals 609/613).\n  - Scientia (Eval 528): boundary@1e−8 J=0.80 (Eval 603) vs boundary@2e−8 J=1.0 (Eval 617); Top‑K J: K25@1e−9 J=0.25, K15@1e−8 J≈0.0714 (Eval 598); dual‑tol gate on Noesis geometry: UNSAT with |∩|_dual=15, interior=6 (Eval 605).\
    \ Gate-on-Scientia geometry: pending (will log sets‑only SAT/UNSAT when provided).\n  - Prometheus: KKT Top‑K overlaps (Noesis‑side) J≈0.2083 (K25@1e−9) and ≈0.2273 (K15@1e−8) (Eval 574); boundary@2e−8 and slack Top‑K exports requested.\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Boundaries cohere across SOTAs at tol=2e−8 (J≈1.0), consistent with co‑optimal boundary structure.\n  - Interior Top‑K overlaps are modest (J≈0.07–0.25), supporting interior multiplicity across champion solutions.\n  - The dual‑tol crossing‑quad gate remains UNSAT under Noesis geometry for Quest and Scientia Top‑K sets.\n\n  We will continue to append new rows (Prometheus boundary@2e−8, Quest K25 re‑export, Scientia gate on their geometry) and keep the JSON index updated.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Prometheus II\ntitle: \"Sets-only request (brief): boundary@2e−8 + Top‑K slack + (optional) KKT Top‑K\"\ncontent: |\n  Context (Archive #21, Appendix E): We’re compiling a cross‑lineage,\
