role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_top25_slack_1e9.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_top15_slack_1e8.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_boundary_contacts_disc_level_2e8.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Quest v4 — corrected Top‑K (Eval 619) + boundary@2e−8 + dual‑tol gate on Noesis geometry\"\ntags: \"utility, sets-only, top-k, boundary, jaccard, gate\"\nabstract: \"Parses Quest’s corrected sets-only CSVs (boundary@2e−8; Top‑K slack K=25@1e−9, K=15@1e−8) from Eval 619; computes boundary Jaccard vs Noesis boundary@2e−8, Top‑K Jaccards vs Noesis interior Top‑K, and dual‑tol crossing‑gate on Noesis geometry; logs JSON summary; returns baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, re\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Quest corrected (Eval 619) inputs\n  P_BOUND_2E8 = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_boundary_contacts_disc_level_2e8.csv'\n\
    \  P_TOP25_1E9 = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_top25_slack_1e9.csv'\n  P_TOP15_1E8 = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval604_top15_slack_1e8.csv'\n\n  # Noesis snapshot (geometry)\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\n  OUT_JSON = 'storage/noesis/nmap/quest_eval604_sets_only_comparison_v4.json'\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL_BOUND_NOESIS_FOR_INTERIOR = 1e-8  # interior filter for Top-K refs\n  TOL_BOUND_FOR_JACCARD = 2e-8          # boundary Jaccard tol\n\n  # ---------------- helpers ----------------\n  def norm_side(s):\n      if s is None: return None\n      t = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z]', '', str(s).strip()).lower()\n      if t in ('xl','xmin','xleft','left','l'):  return 'xL'\n      if t in ('xr','xmax','xright','right','r'): return 'xR'\n      if t in ('yb','ymin','ybottom','bottom','b'): return 'yB'\n      if t in ('yt','ymax','ytop','top','t'):      return 'yT'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('min' in t or\
    \ 'left' in t): return 'xL'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('max' in t or 'right' in t): return 'xR'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('min' in t or 'bottom' in t): return 'yB'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('max' in t or 'top' in t):    return 'yT'\n      return None\n\n  def dictreader_with_sniff(fpath):\n      with open(fpath, 'r', newline='') as f:\n          sample = f.read(8192); f.seek(0)\n          try:\n              dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(sample, delimiters=[',',';','\\t','|'])\n              has_header = csv.Sniffer().has_header(sample)\n          except Exception:\n              dialect = csv.excel\n              has_header = any(c.isalpha() for c in sample)\n          if has_header:\n              rdr = csv.DictReader(f, dialect=dialect)\n              if rdr.fieldnames:\n                  rdr.fieldnames = [(h.strip().lower() if isinstance(h,str) else h) for h in rdr.fieldnames]\n              for row in rdr:\n                  yield {(k.strip().lower() if isinstance(k,str)\
    \ else k): v for k,v in row.items()}\n          else:\n              rdr = csv.reader(f, dialect=dialect)\n              for row in rdr:\n                  yield {str(i): cell for i,cell in enumerate(row)}\n\n  def read_boundary_disc_side(path):\n      S = set()\n      meta = {'exists': os.path.exists(path), 'rows': 0, 'parsed': 0}\n      if not meta['exists']:\n          return S, meta\n      for row in dictreader_with_sniff(path):\n          meta['rows'] += 1\n          i_raw = row.get('disc_idx') or row.get('disc') or row.get('i') or row.get('index')\n          s_raw = row.get('side') or row.get('boundary') or row.get('label') or row.get('which')\n          try:\n              i = int(str(i_raw).strip()) if i_raw is not None else None\n          except Exception:\n              i = None\n          side = norm_side(s_raw)\n          if i is None or side is None: \n              continue\n          S.add((i, side)); meta['parsed'] += 1\n      # 1-based fallback\n      if S:\n      \
    \    idxs = [i for (i,_) in S]\n          if min(idxs) >= 1 and max(idxs) <= N:\n              S = set((i-1, s) for (i,s) in S)\n      S = set((i,s) for (i,s) in S if 0 <= i < N and s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'))\n      return S, meta\n\n  def read_pairs_csv_robust(path):\n      S = set()\n      meta = {'exists': os.path.exists(path), 'rows': 0, 'parsed': 0}\n      if not meta['exists']:\n          return S, meta\n      for row in dictreader_with_sniff(path):\n          meta['rows'] += 1\n          val_i = row.get('i', row.get('disc_i', row.get('disc1', row.get('a', row.get('p1')))))\n          val_j = row.get('j', row.get('disc_j', row.get('disc2', row.get('b', row.get('p2')))))\n          i = j = None\n          try:\n              if val_i is not None: i = int(str(val_i).strip())\n              if val_j is not None: j = int(str(val_j).strip())\n          except Exception:\n              i = j = None\n          if i is None or j is None:\n              # fallback: parse ints from row\
    \ text\n              ints = [int(t) for t in re.findall(r'(?<![\\d.])\\d+(?![\\d.])', ' '.join(str(v) for v in row.values()))]\n              cand = [x for x in ints if 0 <= x < N] or [x for x in ints if 1 <= x <= N]\n              if len(cand) >= 2:\n                  i, j = cand[-2], cand[-1]\n          if i is None or j is None: \n              continue\n          a,b = (i,j) if i<j else (j,i)\n          if a == b: \n              continue\n          S.add((a,b)); meta['parsed'] += 1\n      # 1-based fallback\n      if S:\n          mn = min(min(i,j) for (i,j) in S)\n          mx = max(max(i,j) for (i,j) in S)\n          if mn >= 1 and mx <= N:\n              S = set((i-1, j-1) for (i,j) in S)\n      S = set((i,j) for (i,j) in S if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j)\n      return S, meta\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n      r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_set_from_snapshot(c,\
    \ r, tol):\n      S = set()\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      s = {'xL': x - r, 'xR': 1.0 - x - r, 'yB': y - r, 'yT': 1.0 - y - r}\n      for i in range(N):\n          for side, slack in s.items():\n              if slack[i] <= tol + 1e-12:\n                  S.add((i, side))\n      return S\n\n  def boundary_discs(B):\n      return set(i for (i,_) in B)\n\n  def pair_slacks(c, r):\n      diff = c[:,None,:] - c[None,:,:]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      return dist - (r[:,None] + r[None,:])\n\n  def topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, k, interior_discs):\n      S = pair_slacks(c, r)\n      pairs = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              if i in interior_discs and j in interior_discs:\n                  pairs.append(((i,j), S[i,j]))\n      pairs.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n      return set(p for (p,_) in pairs[:k])\n\n  def seg_cross_strict(a, b, c, d, eps=0.0):\n      def orient(p, q, r):\n          return (q[0]-p[0])*(r[1]-p[1])\
    \ - (q[1]-p[1])*(r[0]-p[0])\n      o1 = orient(a,b,c); o2 = orient(a,b,d)\n      o3 = orient(c,d,a); o4 = orient(c,d,b)\n      return (o1*o2 < -eps) and (o3*o4 < -eps)\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      if not A and not B: return 1.0, 0, 0\n      inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n      return (inter/uni if uni>0 else 1.0), inter, uni\n\n  # ---------------- main ----------------\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n\n      # Read Quest sets\n      Bq, metaB = read_boundary_disc_side(P_BOUND_2E8)\n      K25, meta25 = read_pairs_csv_robust(P_TOP25_1E9)\n      K15, meta15 = read_pairs_csv_robust(P_TOP15_1E8)\n\n      # Boundary @ 2e-8 Jaccard\n      Bn_2e8 = boundary_set_from_snapshot(c, r, tol=TOL_BOUND_FOR_JACCARD)\n      jb, ib, ub = jaccard(Bq, Bn_2e8)\n\n      # Noesis Top-K refs (interior via Noesis boundary@1e-8)\n      Bn_1e8 = boundary_set_from_snapshot(c, r, tol=TOL_BOUND_NOESIS_FOR_INTERIOR)\n      interior = set(range(N)) - boundary_discs(Bn_1e8)\n    \
    \  Tk25_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, 25, interior)\n      Tk15_noe = topk_interior_by_slack(c, r, 15, interior)\n      j25, i25, u25 = jaccard(K25, Tk25_noe)\n      j15, i15, u15 = jaccard(K15, Tk15_noe)\n\n      # Dual‑tol crossing‑gate on Noesis geometry\n      dual = K25 & K15\n      dual_interior = [(i,j) for (i,j) in dual if i in interior and j in interior]\n      cross = False; example = None\n      L = len(dual_interior)\n      for a_idx in range(L):\n          i,j = dual_interior[a_idx]\n          for b_idx in range(a_idx+1, L):\n              k,l = dual_interior[b_idx]\n              if len({i,j,k,l}) < 4:\n                  continue\n              if seg_cross_strict(c[i], c[j], c[k], c[l], eps=0.0):\n                  cross = True; example = {'pair1': [i,j], 'pair2': [k,l]}; break\n          if cross: break\n\n      out = {\n          'quest_eval_id': 619,\n          'paths': {'boundary_2e8_csv': P_BOUND_2E8, 'top25_1e9_csv': P_TOP25_1E9, 'top15_1e8_csv': P_TOP15_1E8},\n\
    \          'meta': {'boundary_csv': metaB, 'top25_csv': meta25, 'top15_csv': meta15},\n          'boundary_jaccard_2e8': {'quest': len(Bq), 'noesis': len(Bn_2e8), 'intersection': ib, 'union': ub, 'j': jb},\n          'topk_jaccards': {\n              'k25_1e9': {'quest': len(K25), 'noesis': len(Tk25_noe), 'intersection': i25, 'union': u25, 'j': j25},\n              'k15_1e8': {'quest': len(K15), 'noesis': len(Tk15_noe), 'intersection': i15, 'union': u15, 'j': j15}\n          },\n          'dual_tol_gate_on_noesis': {\n              'k25': len(K25), 'k15': len(K15), 'dual_intersection': len(dual),\n              'dual_interior_noesis': len(dual_interior), 'result': 'SAT' if cross else 'UNSAT',\n              'example_crossing': example\n          }\n      }\n\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n          print('QUEST_V4_JSON:', OUT_JSON)\n          print('BOUNDARY_2E8_J:',\
    \ jb, 'COUNTS q/noe/int/uni=', len(Bq), len(Bn_2e8), ib, ub)\n          print('TOPK_V4 J K25:', j25, 'K15:', j15, 'COUNTS K25 q/noe=', len(K25), len(Tk25_noe))\n          print('GATE_V4:', out['dual_tol_gate_on_noesis'])\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n      # Return baseline pack (tiny final shrink)\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Assessing edge cases in data**


  I''m considering some edge cases while reading the K=25 CSV, which includes both headers and rows. Initially, I found "non-overlapping interior pairs" in the stored result. Since I have the CSV path, I can parse the integers i and j. It''s also important to validate that the length equals 25, so I’ll accept what’s present and proceed with the necessary actions. Let’s get started on that!'
