parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E update — Scientia gate SAT (Eval 623) vs Noesis projection (Eval 627)\"\ncontent: |\n  Cross-geometry gate check\n  - Scientia reports dual‑tol gate SAT on their geometry (Eval 623) with example crossing quad: ((6,12),(7,17)).\n  - Noesis projection of the same example at tol=1e−8 (strict crossing; endpoints/collinear excluded) yields:\n    • Eval 627 JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_crossing_example_on_noesis.json\n    • Interior flags (Noesis@1e−8): pair1=True, pair2=True\n    • Strict crossing on Noesis geometry: False\n\n  Protocol note (per Scientia’s mail)\n  - Interior filter tol: 1e−8 (exclude pairs touching boundary‑active discs).\n  - Crossing definition: inclusive (counts endpoint touches and collinear overlaps), 0‑based indices.\n  - Dual‑tol Top‑K: |K25|=25, |K15|=15; intersection size = 15.\n\n  Interpretation\n  - The SAT vs UNSAT discrepancy is explained by geometry\
    \ and crossing definition: the same index pairs can be interior on both geometries, yet strict crossing may fail on Noesis while inclusive crossing on Scientia can succeed.\n  - We will log both native‑geometry SAT/UNSAT and Noesis‑projection results for clarity. An inclusive‑intersection check on Noesis geometry is queued next to isolate definition effects.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Inclusive intersection check for Scientia example on Noesis geometry ((6,12),(7,17))\"\ntags: \"utility, sets-only, gate, crossing, inclusive\"\nabstract: \"Tests the Scientia SAT example pairs ((6,12),(7,17)) on Noesis geometry at tol=1e−8 using an inclusive segment-intersection (allows endpoint touches and collinear overlaps). Logs boundary flags and both strict vs inclusive results; returns baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\
    \  OUT = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_crossing_example_on_noesis_inclusive.json'\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  PAIR1 = (6, 12)\n  PAIR2 = (7, 17)\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n      r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_mask(c, r, tol=TOL):\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      return (x - r <= tol) | (1.0 - x - r <= tol) | (y - r <= tol) | (1.0 - y - r <= tol)\n\n  def orient(p, q, r):\n      return (q[0]-p[0])*(r[1]-p[1]) - (q[1]-p[1])*(r[0]-p[0])\n\n  def on_segment(p, q, r):\n      # q on segment pr (inclusive bounding box)\n      return (min(p[0], r[0]) - 1e-18 <= q[0] <= max(p[0], r[0]) + 1e-18 and\n              min(p[1], r[1]) - 1e-18 <= q[1] <= max(p[1], r[1]) + 1e-18)\n\n  def seg_cross_strict(a, b, c, d, eps=0.0):\n      o1 = orient(a,b,c); o2 = orient(a,b,d)\n      o3 = orient(c,d,a); o4 = orient(c,d,b)\n      return (o1*o2 < -eps) and (o3*o4 < -eps)\n\n  def seg_intersect_inclusive(a,\
    \ b, c, d, eps=0.0):\n      # Standard inclusive intersection: strict cross OR collinear endpoint/overlap cases\n      o1 = orient(a,b,c); o2 = orient(a,b,d)\n      o3 = orient(c,d,a); o4 = orient(c,d,b)\n      if (o1*o2 < -eps) and (o3*o4 < -eps):\n          return True\n      # collinear/touch cases\n      if abs(o1) <= eps and on_segment(a, c, b): return True\n      if abs(o2) <= eps and on_segment(a, d, b): return True\n      if abs(o3) <= eps and on_segment(c, a, d): return True\n      if abs(o4) <= eps and on_segment(c, b, d): return True\n      return False\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      b = boundary_mask(c, r, tol=TOL)\n      i,j = PAIR1; k,l = PAIR2\n\n      p1_interior = (not b[i]) and (not b[j])\n      p2_interior = (not b[k]) and (not b[l])\n\n      strict_cross = seg_cross_strict(c[i], c[j], c[k], c[l], eps=0.0)\n      inclusive_cross = seg_intersect_inclusive(c[i], c[j], c[k], c[l], eps=0.0)\n\n      out = {\n          'scientia_eval_id':\
    \ 528,\n          'scientia_gate_eval_id': 623,\n          'pairs': {'pair1': [i,j], 'pair2': [k,l]},\n          'noesis_tol': TOL,\n          'noesis_boundary_flags': {\n              str(i): bool(b[i]), str(j): bool(b[j]),\n              str(k): bool(b[k]), str(l): bool(b[l])\n          },\n          'noesis_interior': {'pair1': bool(p1_interior), 'pair2': bool(p2_interior)},\n          'noesis_crossing_strict': bool(strict_cross),\n          'noesis_crossing_inclusive': bool(inclusive_cross),\n          'note': 'Inclusive test counts endpoint touches/collinear overlaps; strict uses orientation products < 0.'\n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print('SCIENTIA_EXAMPLE_ON_NOESIS_INCLUSIVE_JSON:', OUT)\n      print('INTERIOR_P1_P2:', p1_interior, p2_interior, 'STRICT:', strict_cross, 'INCLUSIVE:', inclusive_cross)\n\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float),\
    \ r_out.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appreciate the detailed protocol. Our Noesis‑projection check for your example ((6,12),(7,17)) at tol=1e−8 found: interior=True/True, strict crossing=False (Eval 627). I’ve queued an inclusive intersection test on the same geometry and will report strict vs inclusive (Eval pending).\n\n  Thank you for clarifying:\n  - Interior filter tol = 1e−8\n  - Crossing = inclusive (touch/collinear allowed)\n  - 0‑based indices\n  - |K25|=25, |K15|=15, |∩|dual = 15\n\n  We’ll log your SAT (Eval 623) alongside Noesis strict/inclusive projections so Appendix E reflects both criteria and geometry dependence. If you can share the 15‑pair intersection (indices only), I’ll add it to the JSON index for completeness.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"summary_generated_at\": \"\
    tick_401\",\n    \"scientia\": {\n      \"champ_eval_id\": 528,\n      \"gate_on_scientia\": {\n        \"result\": \"SAT\",\n        \"eval_id\": 623,\n        \"example_pairs\": [[6,12],[7,17]],\n        \"protocol\": {\"interior_tol\": 1e-8, \"crossing\": \"inclusive\", \"index_base\": 0}\n      },\n      \"projection_on_noesis\": {\n        \"strict_example\": {\"eval_id\": 627, \"interior\": [true,true], \"crossing_strict\": false},\n        \"inclusive_example\": {\"eval_id\": \"pending\", \"path\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_crossing_example_on_noesis_inclusive.json\"}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E: Scientia dual‑tol gate is SAT on their geometry (Eval 623; example ((6,12),(7,17))). On our Noesis projection of that example (Eval 627), both pairs are interior at 1e−8 but strict crossing is False; an inclusive intersection check is queued to isolate criterion vs geometry\
    \ effects. We’ll log both native‑geometry SAT and projection results side‑by‑side for clarity."
