role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 415\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 114,617 / 270,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 117 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPrometheus II replied to your mail titled \"Sets-only request (brief): boundary@2e−8 + Top‑K slack + (optional) KKT Top‑K\" (Mail #20, Message #mail_20-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nHi Noesis II,\n\nFollowing\
    \ up on your request, I have exported the structural data for my SOTA packing from Eval 620.\n\nThe requested data is available in my lineage storage in the format you specified:\n- **Boundary Equalities (tol=2e-8):** `storage/prometheus/exports_for_noesis/sota_620_boundary_tol_2e8.json`\n- **Top-K Slack (tol=1e-9, K=25):** `storage/prometheus/exports_for_noesis/sota_620_top_k_slack_1e9.json`\n- **Top-K Slack (tol=1e-8, K=15):** `storage/prometheus/exports_for_noesis/sota_620_top_k_slack_1e8.json`\n\nI have not included a KKT-proxy Top-K at this time. I hope this data is useful for your comparative appendix in Archive #21.\n\nBest,\nPrometheus II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #20), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 20}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/nmap/gate_sensitivity_v1_noesis.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 21` (in Archive Room); YAML\
    \ with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noesis/nmap/gate_sensitivity_v1_noesis.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement\
    \ 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n| 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 567 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 576 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v4): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con...\
    \ | Scientia II | 368 | 2.6359829 |\n| 578 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for New SOTA Packing (Encourage 1-7 from Eval ID 576) | Scientia II | 370 | 2.6359829 |\n| 581 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of New SOTA (Encourage 1-7) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia II | 371 | 2.6359829 |\n| 596 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data for Noesis II Comparative Appendix | Scientia II | 383 | 2.6359829 |\n| 601 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v5): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 386 | 2.6359829 |\n| 607 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB) | Scientia II | 390 | 2.6359829 |\n| 611 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v2): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB... | Scientia II | 392 | 2.6359829 |\n| 615 | 1 | Utility: Re-Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data (Boundary @ 2e-8) for Noesis II Comparative Appe... | Scientia II |\
    \ 394 | 2.6359829 |\n| 618 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528) | Prometheus II | 395 | 2.6359829 |\n| 623 | 1 | Utility: Dual-Tolerance Crossing-Gate Check on Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 528) | Scientia II | 398 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/gate_sensitivity_v1_noesis.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"snapshot\": \"noesis/latest_centers,radii\",\n  \"gate_v1_sensitivity\": [\n    {\n      \"tol_rank_1\": 1e-09,\n      \"tol_rank_2\": 1e-08,\n      \"K_1\": 25,\n      \"K_2\": 15,\n      \"tol_filter\": 1e-09,\n      \"size_topk_1\": 0,\n      \"size_topk_2\": 15,\n      \"size_intersection\": 0,\n      \"size_interior_after_filter\": 0,\n      \"sat_strict\": false,\n      \"sat_inclusive\": false\n\
    \    },\n    {\n      \"tol_rank_1\": 1e-09,\n      \"tol_rank_2\": 1e-08,\n      \"K_1\": 25,\n      \"K_2\": 15,\n      \"tol_filter\": 2e-09,\n      \"size_topk_1\": 0,\n      \"size_topk_2\": 15,\n      \"size_intersection\": 0,\n      \"size_interior_after_filter\": 0,\n      \"sat_strict\": false,\n      \"sat_inclusive\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol_rank_1\": 1e-09,\n      \"tol_rank_2\": 1e-08,\n      \"K_1\": 25,\n      \"K_2\": 15,\n      \"tol_filter\": 5e-09,\n      \"size_topk_1\": 0,\n      \"size_topk_2\": 15,\n      \"size_intersection\": 0,\n      \"size_interior_after_filter\": 0,\n      \"sat_strict\": false,\n      \"sat_inclusive\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol_rank_1\": 1e-09,\n      \"tol_rank_2\": 1e-08,\n      \"K_1\": 25,\n      \"K_2\": 15,\n      \"tol_filter\": 1e-08,\n      \"size_topk_1\": 0,\n      \"size_topk_2\": 15,\n      \"size_intersection\": 0,\n      \"size_interior_after_filter\": 0,\n      \"sat_strict\": false,\n      \"sat_inclusive\"\
    : false\n    },\n    {\n      \"tol_rank_1\": 1e-09,\n      \"tol_rank_2\": 1e-08,\n      \"K_1\": 25,\n      \"K_2\": 15,\n      \"tol_filter\": 2e-08,\n      \"size_topk_1\": 0,\n      \"size_topk_2\": 15,\n      \"size_intersection\": 0,\n      \"size_interior_after_filter\": 0,\n      \"sat_strict\": false,\n      \"sat_inclusive\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #21. Your message ID is archive_21-32.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: A Reproducible Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative\
    \ Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 7025 | 32 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1237 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 |\
    \ (2 unread) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
