tick: 425
role: model
parts:
- text: "Proceeding to integrate Scientia #23 via sets-only data and update Appendix E.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 596}`\n\n`/execute_action{review 615}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2: Scientia #23 sets-only integration — boundary@2e−8, Top‑K overlaps, Gate v1 on Noesis geometry\"\ntags: \"utility, sets-only, appendix-e, boundary, top-k, gate-v1, scientia\"\nabstract: \"Searches Scientia storage for boundary@2e−8 and Top‑K slack lists (K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8), computes boundary/Top‑K Jaccards vs Noesis, and runs Gate v1 (strict & inclusive) on Noesis geometry with interior filter@1e−8. Results saved to storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_* JSON files. Returns baseline packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # ---------------- Config and paths ----------------\n  N = 26\n  BASE_NOE = 'storage/noesis'\n  BASE_SCI = 'storage/Scientia'  # lineage directory\n  OUT_DIR  = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n\
    \  OUT_SUM  = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'scientia_23_sets_compare.json')\n  OUT_CX   = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'scientia_23_crossing_examples.json')\n\n  # Gate v1 parameters\n  TOL_INT   = 1e-8\n  K_1e9     = 25\n  K_1e8     = 15\n\n  # Noesis refs\n  SNAP_C = os.path.join(BASE_NOE, 'latest_centers.txt')\n  SNAP_R = os.path.join(BASE_NOE, 'latest_radii.txt')\n\n  # ---------------- Utilities ----------------\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      else:\n          centers = []\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < N:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          c = np.array(centers, float)\n          r = np.full(N, 0.08, float)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_set_from_pack(c, r, tol=TOL_INT):\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n\
    \      S = set()\n      if len(r) != N: return S\n      for i in range(N):\n          if x[i] - r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xL'))\n          if 1.0 - x[i] - r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xR'))\n          if y[i] - r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yB'))\n          if 1.0 - y[i] - r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yT'))\n      return S\n\n  def list_all_files(root):\n      for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(root):\n          for fn in filenames:\n              yield os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n\n  def looks_boundary_2e8(path):\n      t = path.lower()\n      return ('boundary' in t) and (('2e-8' in t) or ('2e8' in t))\n\n  def looks_topk_slack(path):\n      t = path.lower()\n      # heuristic: contains 'top' or 'k' or 'slack' and a tol tag\n      return ('slack' in t or 'top' in t or 'k' in t) and (('1e-9' in t) or ('1e9' in t) or ('1e-8' in t) or ('1e8' in t))\n\n  def norm_side(s):\n      if s is None: return None\n      t = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z]', '', str(s).strip()).lower()\n      if t in ('xl','xmin','xleft','left','l'):\
    \  return 'xL'\n      if t in ('xr','xmax','xright','right','r'): return 'xR'\n      if t in ('yb','ymin','ybottom','bottom','b'): return 'yB'\n      if t in ('yt','ymax','ytop','top','t'):      return 'yT'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('min' in t or 'left' in t): return 'xL'\n      if t.startswith('x') and ('max' in t or 'right' in t): return 'xR'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('min' in t or 'bottom' in t): return 'yB'\n      if t.startswith('y') and ('max' in t or 'top' in t):    return 'yT'\n      return None\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n              sample = f.read(4096); f.seek(0)\n              has_head = any(c.isalpha() for c in sample)\n              if has_head:\n                  reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n                  for row in reader:\n                      i = None\n                      for k in ('disc','disc_idx','discindex','i','index'):\n                          if k in\
    \ row and row[k] not in (None,''):\n                              try:\n                                  i = int(str(row[k]).strip()); break\n                              except Exception: pass\n                      side = None\n                      for k in ('side','boundary','label','which','wall'):\n                          if k in row and row[k] not in (None,''):\n                              side = norm_side(row[k]); \n                              if side: break\n                      if i is None or side is None: \n                          continue\n                      # assume 0-based if within [0,N-1]\n                      if 0 <= i < N: S.add((i, side))\n                      elif 1 <= i <= N: S.add((i-1, side))\n              else:\n                  reader = csv.reader(f)\n                  for r in reader:\n                      if not r: continue\n                      i = None; side = None\n                      for cell in r:\n                          if i\
    \ is None:\n                              try: i = int(str(cell).strip()); continue\n                              except Exception: pass\n                          if side is None:\n                              side = norm_side(cell)\n                      if i is None or side is None: continue\n                      if 0 <= i < N: S.add((i, side))\n                      elif 1 <= i <= N: S.add((i-1, side))\n      except Exception:\n          return set()\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv_or_json(path):\n      P = []\n      try:\n          if path.lower().endswith('.json'):\n              data = json.load(open(path,'r'))\n              # accept list [[i,j], ...] or dict with 'pairs'\n              if isinstance(data, list):\n                  for it in data:\n                      if isinstance(it, (list, tuple)) and len(it)==2:\n                          i,j = int(it[0]), int(it[1]); P.append((i,j))\n              elif isinstance(data, dict) and 'pairs' in data:\n          \
    \        for it in data['pairs']:\n                      i,j = int(it[0]), int(it[1]); P.append((i,j))\n          else:\n              with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n                  sample = f.read(4096); f.seek(0)\n                  has_head = any(c.isalpha() for c in sample)\n                  if has_head:\n                      reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n                      for row in reader:\n                          i=j=None\n                          for k in ('i','disc_i','a','p','u'):\n                              if k in row and row[k] not in (None,''):\n                                  try: i = int(str(row[k]).strip()); break\n                                  except Exception: pass\n                          for k in ('j','disc_j','b','q','v'):\n                              if k in row and row[k] not in (None,''):\n                                  try: j = int(str(row[k]).strip()); break\n                                  except Exception: pass\n       \
    \                   if i is None or j is None: \n                              # try generic parse from any cell \"(i,j)\"\n                              for v in row.values():\n                                  m = re.findall(r'\\d+', str(v))\n                                  if len(m)>=2:\n                                      i = int(m[0]); j = int(m[1]); break\n                          if i is None or j is None: \n                              continue\n                          P.append((i,j))\n                  else:\n                      reader = csv.reader(f)\n                      for r in reader:\n                          nums = [int(x) for x in re.findall(r'\\d+', ' '.join(map(str,r)))]\n                          if len(nums)>=2:\n                              P.append((nums[0], nums[1]))\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      # normalize 0/1-based\n      if P:\n          mn = min(min(i,j) for (i,j) in P)\n          mx = max(max(i,j) for (i,j) in P)\n   \
    \       if mn>=1 and mx<=N:\n              P = [(i-1,j-1) for (i,j) in P]\n      # clamp range\n      P = [(i,j) for (i,j) in P if 0<=i<N and 0<=j<N and i!=j]\n      # canonical order\n      P = [(min(i,j), max(i,j)) for (i,j) in P]\n      # dedup preserving order\n      seen=set(); out=[]\n      for pr in P:\n          if pr in seen: continue\n          seen.add(pr); out.append(pr)\n      return out\n\n  def jaccard(a_set, b_set):\n      if not a_set and not b_set: return 1.0, 0, 0\n      inter = len(a_set & b_set); uni = len(a_set | b_set)\n      return (inter/uni if uni>0 else 1.0), inter, uni\n\n  # geometry helpers\n  def boundary_mask(c, r, tol=TOL_INT):\n      x=c[:,0]; y=c[:,1]\n      return (x - r <= tol) | (1-x - r <= tol) | (y - r <= tol) | (1-y - r <= tol)\n\n  def seg_cross(p1,p2,p3,p4, inclusive=False):\n      def orient(a,b,c):\n          return np.cross(b-a, c-a)\n      a=p1; b=p2; c=p3; d=p4\n      o1 = orient(a,b,c); o2 = orient(a,b,d)\n      o3 = orient(c,d,a); o4\
    \ = orient(c,d,b)\n      if inclusive:\n          def sgn(x,eps=1e-15): \n              return 0 if abs(x)<=eps else (1 if x>0 else -1)\n          s1=sgn(o1); s2=sgn(o2); s3=sgn(o3); s4=sgn(o4)\n          return (s1*s2<=0) and (s3*s4<=0)\n      else:\n          return (o1*o2<0) and (o3*o4<0)\n\n  # compute slack and rank pairs by slack for our pack\n  def pair_slacks(c, r):\n      diff = c[:,None,:] - c[None,:,:]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      S = dist - (r[:,None] + r[None,:])\n      return S\n\n  # ---------------- Main workflow ----------------\n  def construct_packing():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      c_noe, r_noe = load_snapshot()\n\n      # 1) Locate Scientia boundary@2e-8 and Top-K files\n      sci_files = list(list_all_files(BASE_SCI)) if os.path.exists(BASE_SCI) else []\n      boundary_candidates = [p for p in sci_files if looks_boundary_2e8(p)]\n      topk_candidates     = [p for p in sci_files if looks_topk_slack(p)]\n\n      # choose\
    \ boundary file: prefer one with explicit '2e-8' or '2e8'\n      boundary_path = None\n      for p in boundary_candidates:\n          boundary_path = p; break\n\n      # choose Top-K files by tol tokens\n      def pick_topk(paths, tol_token):\n          # prefer filenames containing both 'slack' and tol token\n          for p in paths:\n              t = p.lower()\n              if 'slack' in t and tol_token in t:\n                  return p\n          for p in paths:\n              if tol_token in p.lower():\n                  return p\n          return None\n\n      topk_1e9_path = pick_topk(topk_candidates, '1e-9') or pick_topk(topk_candidates, '1e9')\n      topk_1e8_path = pick_topk(topk_candidates, '1e-8') or pick_topk(topk_candidates, '1e8')\n\n      # 2) Read Scientia sets\n      sci_boundary = read_boundary_csv(boundary_path) if boundary_path else set()\n      sci_k25 = set(read_pairs_csv_or_json(topk_1e9_path)[:K_1e9]) if topk_1e9_path else set()\n      sci_k15 = set(read_pairs_csv_or_json(topk_1e8_path)[:K_1e8])\
    \ if topk_1e8_path else set()\n\n      # 3) Build Noesis references\n      noe_boundary = boundary_set_from_pack(c_noe, r_noe, tol=2e-8)  # boundary@2e-8 per v2 reconciliation\n      S = pair_slacks(c_noe, r_noe)\n      pairs = [(i,j,S[i,j]) for i in range(N) for j in range(i+1,N)]\n      pairs.sort(key=lambda t: t[2])  # ascending by slack\n      noe_k25 = set((i,j) for (i,j,_) in pairs[:K_1e9])\n      # for 1e-8 K=15 we rank still by slack (same ordering), but report only top 15\n      noe_k15 = set((i,j) for (i,j,_) in pairs[:K_1e8])\n\n      # 4) Boundary/Top‑K Jaccards\n      jb, ib, ub = jaccard(sci_boundary, noe_boundary)\n      j25, i25, u25 = jaccard(sci_k25, noe_k25)\n      j15, i15, u15 = jaccard(sci_k15, noe_k15)\n\n      # 5) Gate v1 on Noesis geometry using Scientia Top‑K sets\n      # Intersection across tol for slack-based lists\n      dual = list((sci_k25 & sci_k15))\n      # Interior filter at tol=1e-8 on Noesis\n      bmask = boundary_mask(c_noe, r_noe, tol=TOL_INT)\n\
    \      dual_interior = [(i,j) for (i,j) in dual if (not bmask[i] and not bmask[j])]\n\n      # Crossing checks\n      def check_cross_list(pairs_list, inclusive=False):\n          cx = []\n          for a in range(len(pairs_list)):\n              i,j = pairs_list[a]\n              p1 = c_noe[i]; p2 = c_noe[j]\n              for b in range(a+1, len(pairs_list)):\n                  k,l = pairs_list[b]\n                  if len({i,j,k,l})<4: \n                      continue\n                  q1 = c_noe[k]; q2 = c_noe[l]\n                  if seg_cross(p1,p2,q1,q2, inclusive=inclusive):\n                      cx.append(((i,j),(k,l)))\n          return cx\n\n      cx_strict   = check_cross_list(dual_interior, inclusive=False)\n      cx_incl     = check_cross_list(dual_interior, inclusive=True)\n\n      gate_strict   = len(cx_strict) > 0\n      gate_incl     = len(cx_incl) > 0\n\n      # 6) Write outputs\n      compare = {\n          'source': 'Scientia_23',\n          'files': {\n      \
    \        'boundary_2e8': boundary_path,\n              'topk_1e9_k25': topk_1e9_path,\n              'topk_1e8_k15': topk_1e8_path\n          },\n          'counts': {\n              'sci_boundary': len(sci_boundary),\n              'noe_boundary': len(noe_boundary),\n              'sci_k25': len(sci_k25),\n              'noe_k25': len(noe_k25),\n              'sci_k15': len(sci_k15),\n              'noe_k15': len(noe_k15)\n          },\n          'jaccards': {\n              'boundary_2e8': {'J': jb, 'inter': ib, 'union': ub},\n              'k25_1e9': {'J': j25, 'inter': i25, 'union': u25},\n              'k15_1e8': {'J': j15, 'inter': i15, 'union': u15}\n          },\n          'gate_v1_noesis': {\n              'dual_size': len(dual),\n              'dual_interior_size@1e-8': len(dual_interior),\n              'strict': gate_strict,\n              'inclusive': gate_incl\n          }\n      }\n      cx_out = {\n          'source': 'Scientia_23',\n          'dual_interior_pairs@1e-8':\
    \ dual_interior,\n          'crossing_examples_strict': cx_strict[:10],\n          'crossing_examples_inclusive': cx_incl[:10]\n      }\n\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n          with open(OUT_SUM, 'w') as f: json.dump(compare, f, indent=2)\n          with open(OUT_CX, 'w') as f: json.dump(cx_out, f, indent=2)\n          print('SCI_23_COMPARE_JSON:', OUT_SUM)\n          print('SCI_23_CROSSING_JSON:', OUT_CX)\n          print('J_BOUNDARY_2e8:', jb, 'J_K25_1e9:', j25, 'J_K15_1e8:', j15)\n          print('GATE_V1(strict,inclusive):', gate_strict, gate_incl)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n      # 7) Return a valid packing (baseline snapshot with tiny final shrink)\n      r_out = np.maximum(r_noe - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c_noe.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2 — Scientia #23 sets-only integration queued\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  I have submitted an analysis-only utility to integrate Scientia #23 under Appendix E v2:\n  - Boundary@2e−8, Top‑K slack overlaps (K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8), and Gate v1 (strict & inclusive) run on my geometry with interior filter@1e−8.\n  - Outputs (JSON):\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_sets_compare.json\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_crossing_examples.json\n  - As with earlier entries, this is strictly sets-only (indices/tol/K), with full paths logged. I will summarize the results here once the eval finishes.\n```"
