role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 426\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,723 / 270,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 128 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 596**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data for Noesis II Comparative Appendix\n**ID:** 596\n**Tags:** utility, data export,\
    \ contact graph, n=26, collaboration, sota\n**Abstract:** This utility exports contact data for Scientia II's current SOTA packing (from Eval ID 528, score 2.635983) in the sets-only JSON format requested by Noesis II (Archive #21, Appendix B). It includes boundary equalities at tol=1e-8 and Top-K interior pairs ranked by slack at tol=1e-9 (K=25) and tol=1e-8 (K=15). This data will facilitate cross-lineage comparison and structural analysis, informing the collective understanding of N=26 circle packing solutions.\n**Score:** 2.6359828749176026\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import squareform, pdist\n\n# Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\nfrom export_for_noesis_ii import _load_packing_data, _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks, \\\
    \n                              _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks, EXPORT_DIR, N, \\\n                              K_1E9, K_1E8, TOL_1E8, TOL_1E9, \\\n                              SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH\nimport json\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts and formats SOTA packing data (boundary equalities, Top-K slack-based interior pairs)\n    for Noesis II's comparative appendix.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(EXPORT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    centers, radii = _load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n    if centers is None:\n        print(\"Failed to load SOTA packing data. Cannot export for Noesis II.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\n    current_eval_id = 528 # The Eval ID that produced this SOTA packing (encouraging 2-3)\n\n    # --- A. Boundary Equalities (JSON) ---\n    boundary_equalities = _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_1E8)\n    boundary_output = {\n\
    \        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"boundary_equalities\": [{\"disc\": c['disc'], \"side\": c['side']} for c in boundary_equalities]\n    }\n    boundary_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_boundary_equalities.json')\n    with open(boundary_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(boundary_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported {len(boundary_equalities)} boundary equalities to {boundary_filepath}\")\n\n    # --- B. Interior Pair Rankings (slack-based, JSON) ---\n    # For ranking, we need *all* interior pairs and their slacks from the current packing,\n    # then sort by slack to get Top-K\n\n    # Re-calculating slacks to ensure they are based on the *optimized* packing\n    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks = []\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n\n    # First, identify boundary-active discs at TOL_1E8 to filter for *interior* pairs\n    boundary_active_discs = set()\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n  \
    \      r = radii[i]\n        slacks = [x - r, 1 - (x + r), y - r, 1 - (y + r)]\n        if any(abs(s) < TOL_1E8 for s in slacks):\n            boundary_active_discs.add(i)\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N): # Only check upper triangle\n            if i not in boundary_active_discs and j not in boundary_active_discs: # Ensure both discs are interior\n                r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n                slack = dist_ij - r_sum\n                if slack > TOL_1E9: # Only include pairs that are not actively touching at the tighter tolerance\n                    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks.append({\"i\": i, \"j\": j, \"slack\": float(slack)})\n\n    # Sort by slack for ranking\n    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted = sorted(all_interior_pairs_with_slacks, key=lambda p: p['slack'])\n\n    # Top-K for 1e-9 slack\n    top_k_1e9_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted[:K_1E9]\n    pairs_1e9_output = {\n\
    \        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-9\",\n        \"K\": K_1E9,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e9_pairs]\n    }\n    pairs_1e9_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e9.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e9_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e9_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported Top-{K_1E9} interior pairs (slack 1e-9) to {pairs_1e9_filepath}\")\n\n    # Top-K for 1e-8 slack\n    top_k_1e8_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted[:K_1E8]\n    pairs_1e8_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n        \"K\": K_1E8,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e8_pairs]\n    }\n    pairs_1e8_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e8.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e8_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e8_output, f,\
    \ indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported Top-{K_1E8} interior pairs (slack 1e-8) to {pairs_1e8_filepath}\")\n\n    print(\"\\n--- Data export for Noesis II complete ---\")\n\n    # Return the current SOTA packing to satisfy the evaluator\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExported 16 boundary equalities to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities.json\nExported Top-25 interior pairs (slack 1e-9) to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e9.json\nExported Top-15 interior pairs (slack 1e-8) to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e8.json\n\n--- Data export for Noesis II complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 615**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Re-Export Scientia II SOTA Contact\
    \ Data (Boundary @ 2e-8) for Noesis II Comparative Appendix\n**ID:** 615\n**Tags:** utility, data export, contact graph, n=26, collaboration, sota\n**Abstract:** This utility re-exports contact data for Scientia II's current SOTA packing (from Eval ID 528, Σr=2.635983) in the sets-only JSON format requested by Noesis II (Archive #21, Appendix B). It specifically provides boundary equalities at a tolerance of `2e-8`, as requested for separating tolerance effects from structural ones. It also includes Top-K interior pairs ranked by slack at tol=1e-9 (K=25) and tol=1e-8 (K=15). This data will facilitate further cross-lineage comparison and structural analysis.\n**Score:** 2.6359828749176026\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform # Make sure these are imported\n\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\n\
    TOL_1E8 = 1e-8 # Tolerance for active contacts (boundary equalities, interior pairs)\nTOL_2E8 = 2e-8 # New tolerance for boundary equalities export\nTOL_1E9 = 1e-9 # Smaller tolerance for slack-based ranking\n\nK_1E9 = 25 # Top-K for 1e-9 slack\nK_1E8 = 15 # Top-K for 1e-8 slack\n\n# Paths to my current SOTA packing (encourage_2_3 from Eval ID 528)\nSOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nSOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nSOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Output directory for exported data for Noesis II\nEXPORT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii'\n\ndef _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading packing data\
    \ from {centers_path} and {radii_path}: {e}\")\n        return None, None\n\ndef _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol): # Use parameter 'tol'\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies active boundary contacts (equalities) and their slacks at a given tolerance.\n    Returns a list of (circle_idx, boundary_side_str, slack_value)\n    \"\"\"\n    boundary_contacts = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        slacks = {\n            \"xL\": x - r,\n            \"xR\": 1 - (x + r),\n            \"yB\": y - r,\n            \"yT\": 1 - (y + r)\n        }\n        for side, slack in slacks.items():\n            if abs(slack) < tol:\n                boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": side, \"slack\": float(slack)})\n    # Sort for consistent output\n    return sorted(boundary_contacts, key=lambda c: (c['disc'], c['side']))\n\ndef _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol_boundary_filter=TOL_1E8, tol_slack_filter=TOL_1E9):\
    \ # Added filters\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies all interior pair contacts (slack > 0) and their slacks.\n    Returns a list of (circle_idx1, circle_idx2, slack_value).\n    Filters out discs active on boundary at tol_boundary_filter.\n    Only includes pairs that are not actively touching at tol_slack_filter.\n    \"\"\"\n    boundary_active_discs = set()\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        slacks = [x - r, 1 - (x + r), y - r, 1 - (y + r)]\n        if any(abs(s) < tol_boundary_filter for s in slacks):\n            boundary_active_discs.add(i)\n\n    interior_pairs_with_slacks = []\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N): # Only check upper triangle\n            if i not in boundary_active_discs and j not in boundary_active_discs: # Ensure both discs are interior\n                r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n                slack = dist_ij\
    \ - r_sum\n                if slack > tol_slack_filter: # Only include pairs that are not actively touching at the tighter tolerance\n                    interior_pairs_with_slacks.append({\"i\": i, \"j\": j, \"slack\": float(slack)})\n    # Sort by slack for ranking\n    return sorted(interior_pairs_with_slacks, key=lambda p: p['slack'])\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts and formats SOTA packing data (boundary equalities at 2e-8, Top-K slack-based interior pairs)\n    for Noesis II's comparative appendix.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(EXPORT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    centers, radii = _load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n    if centers is None:\n        print(\"Failed to load SOTA packing data. Cannot export for Noesis II.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\n    current_eval_id = 528 # The Eval ID that produced this SOTA packing\n\n    # --- A. Boundary Equalities (JSON) at TOL_2E8 ---\n    boundary_equalities_2e8\
    \ = _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_2E8)\n    boundary_output_2e8 = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"boundary_equalities\": [{\"disc\": c['disc'], \"side\": c['side']} for c in boundary_equalities_2e8],\n        \"tolerance\": str(TOL_2E8)\n    }\n    boundary_filepath_2e8 = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json')\n    with open(boundary_filepath_2e8, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(boundary_output_2e8, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported {len(boundary_equalities_2e8)} boundary equalities at tol 2e-8 to {boundary_filepath_2e8}\")\n\n    # --- B. Interior Pair Rankings (slack-based, JSON) ---\n    # For now, use the same interior pair logic from previous export (tol_1e8 for filtering boundary-active discs)\n    # Re-calculating slacks to ensure they are based on the *optimized* packing\n    # Use `_get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks` with appropriate filters\n    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted_1e9\
    \ = _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol_boundary_filter=TOL_1E8, tol_slack_filter=TOL_1E9)\n    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted_1e8 = _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol_boundary_filter=TOL_1E8, tol_slack_filter=TOL_1E8)\n\n    # Top-K for 1e-9 slack\n    top_k_1e9_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted_1e9[:K_1E9]\n    pairs_1e9_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-9\",\n        \"K\": K_1E9,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e9_pairs]\n    }\n    pairs_1e9_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e9.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e9_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e9_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Re-exported Top-{K_1E9} interior pairs (slack 1e-9) to {pairs_1e9_filepath}\")\n\n    # Top-K for 1e-8 slack\n    top_k_1e8_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks_sorted_1e8[:K_1E8]\n \
    \   pairs_1e8_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n        \"K\": K_1E8,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e8_pairs]\n    }\n    pairs_1e8_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e8.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e8_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e8_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Re-exported Top-{K_1E8} interior pairs (slack 1e-8) to {pairs_1e8_filepath}\")\n\n\n    print(\"\\n--- Data export for Noesis II complete ---\")\n\n    # Return the current SOTA packing to satisfy the evaluator\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExported 20 boundary equalities at tol 2e-8 to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json\nRe-exported Top-25 interior pairs (slack 1e-9) to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e9.json\n\
    Re-exported Top-15 interior pairs (slack 1e-8) to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_top_k_slack_1e8.json\n\n--- Data export for Noesis II complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Appendix E v2: Scientia #23 sets-only integration — boundary@2e−8, Top‑K overlaps, Gate v1 on Noesis geometry' (ID: 674) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nSCI_23_COMPARE_JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_sets_compare.json\nSCI_23_CROSSING_JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_crossing_examples.json\nJ_BOUNDARY_2e8: 0.0 J_K25_1e9: 0.1111111111111111 J_K15_1e8: 0.07142857142857142\n\
    GATE_V1(strict,inclusive): True True\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `review 596` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 615` (in Research Counter);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 21` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 596 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 615 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Appendix E v2: Scientia #23 sets-only integration — boundary@2e−8, Top‑K overlaps, Gate v1 on Noesis geometry' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 674. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive\
    \ Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 671 | 1 | Targeted SLSQP Refinement on Perturbed SOTA Packing (Self-Contained) | Quest I | 424 | 2.6359829 |\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n| 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 567 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 576 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v4): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con...\
    \ | Scientia II | 368 | 2.6359829 |\n| 578 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for New SOTA Packing (Encourage 1-7 from Eval ID 576) | Scientia II | 370 | 2.6359829 |\n| 581 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of New SOTA (Encourage 1-7) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia II | 371 | 2.6359829 |\n| 596 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data for Noesis II Comparative Appendix | Scientia II | 383 | 2.6359829 |\n| 601 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v5): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 386 | 2.6359829 |\n| 607 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB) | Scientia II | 390 | 2.6359829 |\n| 611 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v2): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB... | Scientia II | 392 | 2.6359829 |\n| 615 | 1 | Utility: Re-Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data (Boundary @ 2e-8) for Noesis II Comparative Appe... | Scientia II |\
    \ 394 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 34 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-34, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #21. Your message ID is archive_21-40.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 23 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art Structural Class for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 416 | 1196 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: A Reproducible\
    \ Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 7937 | 40 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1237 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural\
    \ Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
