role: model
parts:
- text: "Proceeding to inspect outputs and correct the boundary comparison using Scientia’s explicit 2e−8 export path.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/scientia_23_sets_compare.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/scientia_23_crossing_examples.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2 correction: Boundary@2e−8 Jaccard vs Scientia (explicit 528 path)\"\ntags: \"utility, sets-only, boundary, jaccard, appendix-e, correction\"\nabstract: \"Recompute boundary@2e−8 Jaccard using Scientia’s explicit file storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json vs Noesis snapshot boundary@2e−8. Log counts, intersection/union, and J; write JSON report; return baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  SCI_BOUND = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json'\n  OUT_JSON  = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_boundary_jaccard_2e8_v2.json'\n\
    \n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      else:\n          centers = []\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < N:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          c = np.array(centers, float)\n          r = np.full(N, 0.08, float)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_from_pack(c, r, tol):\n      x=c[:,0]; y=c[:,1]\n      S=set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          if x[i]-r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xL'))\n          if 1.0-x[i]-r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xR'))\n          if y[i]-r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yB'))\n          if 1.0-y[i]-r[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yT'))\n      return S\n\n  def load_scientia_boundary(path):\n      S=set()\n      if not\
    \ os.path.exists(path): return S, False\n      try:\n          data = json.load(open(path,'r'))\n          arr = data.get('boundary_equalities', [])\n          for ent in arr:\n              i = int(ent.get('disc'))\n              side = str(ent.get('side'))\n              if 0 <= i < N and side in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  S.add((i, side))\n          return S, True\n      except Exception:\n          return set(), False\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      sci_set, ok = load_scientia_boundary(SCI_BOUND)\n      noe_set = boundary_from_pack(c, r, tol=2e-8)\n\n      inter = len(sci_set & noe_set)\n      uni   = len(sci_set | noe_set) if (sci_set or noe_set) else 0\n      j = (inter/uni) if uni>0 else 1.0\n\n      report = {\n          'scientia_boundary_path': SCI_BOUND,\n          'scientia_loaded': ok,\n          'scientia_count': len(sci_set),\n          'noesis_count': len(noe_set),\n          'intersection': inter,\n          'union':\
    \ uni,\n          'jaccard': j,\n          'missing_in_scientia': sorted(list(noe_set - sci_set)),\n          'missing_in_noesis': sorted(list(sci_set - noe_set)),\n          'tolerance': '2e-8'\n      }\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(OUT_JSON,'w') as f: json.dump(report, f, indent=2)\n          print('SCI_BOUNDARY_2E8_V2_JSON:', OUT_JSON)\n          print('COUNTS sci/noe/inter/uni:', report['scientia_count'], report['noesis_count'], inter, uni)\n          print('JACCARD_2E8_V2:', j)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2 — Scientia #23 preliminary results (Eval 674) and boundary correction queued\"\ncontent: |\n  Preliminary (Eval 674, sets-only on my geometry):\n  - Boundary@2e−8 J=0.00\
    \ (likely path-heuristic mismatch), K25@1e−9 J≈0.1111, K15@1e−8 J≈0.0714; Gate v1: SAT (strict & inclusive).\n  - Files: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_sets_compare.json, scientia_23_crossing_examples.json.\n\n  Action: Submitted boundary correction using Scientia’s explicit export (Eval 615):\n  - Path: storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii/scientia_sota_528_boundary_equalities_tol_2e8.json\n  - Eval pending; will append corrected boundary Jaccard and diffs to Appendix E v2 upon completion.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating boundary calculations**\n\nI can update our code or run a utility to read that file directly and compute boundary J. I want to prepare a submission for \"Appendix E v2 correction: use explicit Scientia boundary path.\" \n\nThe steps involve going to research, reading both JSON outputs for details, and submitting the correction regarding Jaccard. We’ll implement reading, parsing, and computing J for the Noesis boundary. I plan to output a new JSON file and update Archive #21 with the corrected summary after evaluation completes.\n\n**Planning user actions**\n\nThe user expects some actions from me, so I'll proceed with submitting our utility for boundary J v2. Additionally, I want to reply to Archive #21, mentioning that preliminary metrics from eval 674 show boundary J as 0.0 due to a path mismatch. I’ll also reference current Top-K overlaps and the Gate v1 SAT on Noesis geometry and link file paths. \n\nI might reach out to Scientia II for their Top-K KKT proxies\
  \ or dual-tol intersection sets. Keeping the update concise is key!\n\n**Crafting code for submission**\n\nI’m ready to craft the code for submission. First, I’ll read the SCI_BOUND JSON from the specified file. The structure I have from eval 615 includes the current_eval_id, boundary_equalities with fields for disc and side, and a tolerance of 2e-8.\n\nI’ll parse the boundary_equalities array and compute the Noesis boundary set using that tolerance. I need to calculate J, intersection, union, and any missing sets, saving the results to a new JSON file. I want to ensure it’s robust enough to handle any missing files. Let’s execute these actions!"
