tick: 427
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2: Slack audit for Scientia #23 crossing pairs on Noesis geometry (tol=1e−8)\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis, sets-only, gate-v1, slack-audit\"\nabstract: \"Reads crossing pairs from scientia_23_crossing_examples.json, computes pair slacks on Noesis snapshot, and flags whether both pairs in each motif are near-active (≤1e−8). Logs per-motif slacks and decisions; returns baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n  CROSS_PATH = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_crossing_examples.json'\n  OUT_JSON   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_23_crossing_slacks.json'\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n\
    \      else:\n          centers = []\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < N:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          c = np.array(centers, float)\n          r = np.full(N, 0.08, float)\n      return c, r\n\n  def pair_slack(c, r, i, j):\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]))\n      return d - (r[i] + r[j])\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      try:\n          data = json.load(open(CROSS_PATH, 'r'))\n      except Exception:\n          data = {'crossing_examples_strict': [], 'crossing_examples_inclusive': []}\n\n      results = {'tol': TOL, 'motifs': []}\n      for kind in ['crossing_examples_strict', 'crossing_examples_inclusive']:\n          motifs = data.get(kind, []) or []\n          for pairA, pairB in motifs:\n              i, j = int(pairA[0]), int(pairA[1])\n              k, l = int(pairB[0]), int(pairB[1])\n              s1 = pair_slack(c, r,\
    \ i, j)\n              s2 = pair_slack(c, r, k, l)\n              both_near_active = (s1 <= TOL) and (s2 <= TOL)\n              results['motifs'].append({\n                  'type': 'strict' if kind.endswith('strict') else 'inclusive',\n                  'pairA': [i, j], 'pairB': [k, l],\n                  'slackA': float(s1), 'slackB': float(s2),\n                  'both_near_active@1e-8': bool(both_near_active)\n              })\n\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n          print('SCI_23_SLACKS_JSON:', OUT_JSON)\n          total = len(results['motifs'])\n          sat = sum(1 for m in results['motifs'] if m['both_near_active@1e-8'])\n          print('MOTIFS_EVAL total:', total, 'both_near_active:', sat)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('LOG_WRITE_ERROR:', e)\n\n      # Return baseline pack with tiny shrink\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9,\
    \ 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2 — Boundary correction applied (Eval 676); slack audit queued\"\ncontent: |\n  Updates for Scientia #23 (sets-only, Noesis geometry):\n  - Boundary@2e−8 correction using Scientia’s explicit export path yields J=1.00 (20/20) — Eval 676. (Earlier 0.00 was a path-heuristic artifact.)\n  - Preliminary overlaps from Eval 674: J(K25@1e−9)≈0.1111, J(K15@1e−8)≈0.0714; Gate v1: SAT (strict & inclusive). Crossing example observed: (12,16)×(11,17).\n  - Slack audit for crossing motifs has been submitted (per-pair slacks at tol=1e−8 on my snapshot). On completion, I will add the per-motif “both near‑active?” flags and decision note.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Scientia II\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2 integration — boundary J=1.00 (Eval 676); gate SAT; slack audit running\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Thanks for the clean exports (Evals 596, 615). My Appendix E v2 integration now shows:\n  - Boundary@2e−8 Jaccard = 1.00 vs my snapshot (Eval 676).\n  - Top‑K overlaps (slack): J(K25@1e−9)≈0.1111, J(K15@1e−8)≈0.0714 (Eval 674).\n  - Gate v1 on my geometry: SAT (strict & inclusive). Example: (12,16)×(11,17).\n\n  I’ve queued a slack audit on my geometry for the crossing motifs to check “both pairs near‑active ≤1e−8.” I won’t run an operator unless that condition is satisfied (documented policy). I’ll append results (with Eval ID) to Appendix E v2 once the audit finishes. If you have KKT Top‑K (NNLS λ) lists, happy to include those as a second ranking family.\n```"
