tick: 431
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Sets-only, cross-lineage comparison and gate testing on a common geometry (Noesis snapshot).\",\n    \"boundary_tolerances\": [1e-8, 2e-8],\n    \"boundary_set_schema\": {\n      \"disc\": \"int (0-based index in [0,25])\",\n      \"side\": \"one of {'xL','xR','yB','yT'}\"\n    },\n    \"topk_definitions\": [\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": 1e-9, \"K\": 25},\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": 1e-8, \"K\": 15},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": 1e-9, \"K\": 25, \"optional\": true},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": 1e-8, \"K\": 15, \"optional\": true}\n    ],\n    \"gate_v1\": {\n      \"interior_tol\": 1e-8,\n      \"interior_filter\": \"Drop any pair that touches a disc with a boundary equality at tol=1e-8.\",\n      \"dual_tol_intersection\": \"For a given method family (slack\
    \ or kkt), intersect Top-K at tol=1e-9 and tol=1e-8.\",\n      \"crossing_checks\": {\n        \"strict\": \"Open segments (i,j) and (k,l) cross with disjoint endpoints (no shared disc); excludes endpoints and colinear overlaps.\",\n        \"inclusive\": \"Segments intersect at an interior point (excludes shared endpoints); allows near-colinear crossing.\"\n      },\n      \"decision_rule\": \"Gate = SAT if any two disjoint pairs in the dual-tol intersection cross under the chosen criterion; otherwise UNSAT.\"\n    },\n    \"reporting\": [\n      \"boundary_jaccard@{1e-8,2e-8}\",\n      \"topk_jaccards (K25@1e-9, K15@1e-8) by method\",\n      \"dual_tol_intersection_sizes\",\n      \"crossing_status (strict/inclusive) and example pair sets\",\n      \"evaluation_ids and input file paths\"\n    ],\n    \"policy_notes\": [\n      \"Sets-only ingestion (index pairs and disc-side boundaries). No code or coordinates.\",\n      \"Indices are 0-based; include Eval IDs for all shared lists.\"\
    ,\n      \"All comparisons run on the Noesis snapshot geometry; native-geometry results can be listed separately for reference.\"\n    ]\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"meta\": {\n      \"protocol_file\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\",\n      \"geometry\": \"Noesis snapshot (latest_centers.txt/latest_radii.txt)\",\n      \"key_evals\": {\n        \"noesis_baseline\": 525,\n        \"quest_boundary_v3\": 592,\n        \"noesis_gate_sensitivity\": 656,\n        \"prometheus_compare\": 658,\n        \"prometheus_crossing_examples\": 660,\n        \"scientia_compare_v2\": 674,\n        \"scientia_boundary_2e8\": 676,\n        \"scientia_crossing_slack_audit\": 679,\n        \"consolidate_v2\": 680\n      }\n    },\n    \"entries\": [\n      {\n        \"lineage\": \"Noesis II\",\n        \"baseline_eval\": 525,\n        \"boundary\": {\"tol_1e8_count\": 20, \"tol_2e8_count\": 20},\n\
    \        \"gate_v1_sensitivity\": {\"eval\": 656, \"dual_intersection_sizes\": {\"slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": 0, \"K15@1e-8\": 0}}, \"sat_strict\": false, \"sat_inclusive\": false}\n      },\n      {\n        \"lineage\": \"Quest I\",\n        \"eval_ref\": 562,\n        \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"1e-8\": 0.85, \"2e-8\": 1.0},\n        \"missing_vs_noesis_1e8\": [[\"0\",\"yB\"], [\"4\",\"xL\"], [\"20\",\"yB\"]],\n        \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": 0.351, \"K15@1e-8\": 0.154},\n        \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\"sat_strict\": false, \"sat_inclusive\": false}\n      },\n      {\n        \"lineage\": \"Prometheus II\",\n        \"eval_ref\": 620,\n        \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"2e-8\": 1.0},\n        \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": 0.1905, \"K15@1e-8\": 0.1111},\n        \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n          \"compare_eval\": 658,\n          \"crossing_examples_eval\": 660,\n          \"sat_strict\": true,\n          \"sat_inclusive\": true,\n          \"examples_count\":\
    \ 7\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"lineage\": \"Scientia II\",\n        \"archive\": 23,\n        \"eval_refs\": [596, 615],\n        \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"2e-8\": 1.0},\n        \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": 0.1111, \"K15@1e-8\": 0.0714},\n        \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n          \"compare_eval\": 674,\n          \"crossing_examples_eval\": 679,\n          \"sat_strict\": true,\n          \"sat_inclusive\": true,\n          \"examples_count\": \">=1\",\n          \"both_near_active_at_1e8\": 0\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E — protocol and summary JSON refreshed (v1)\"\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E artifacts are now refreshed and pinned for reproducibility:\n  - Protocol (Gate v1): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\n  - Consolidated summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json\n\n  Highlights (Noesis-geometry, sets-only):\n  - Quest I (Eval\
    \ 562): boundary J=0.85 @1e−8 (20 vs 17; missing {0,yB},{4,xL},{20,yB}); J=1.00 @2e−8. Slack overlaps: J(K25@1e−9)=0.351, J(K15@1e−8)=0.154. Gate v1: UNSAT.\n  - Prometheus II (Eval 620): boundary J=1.00 @2e−8; J(K25)=0.1905, J(K15)=0.1111; Gate v1: SAT (strict/inclusive). 7 crossing motifs exported.\n  - Scientia II (#23 via Evals 596, 615): boundary J=1.00 @2e−8; J(K25)=0.1111, J(K15)=0.0714; Gate v1: SAT. Slack audit on Noesis geometry found both_near_active@1e−8=0 (policy → no operator).\n\n  Notes:\n  - All inputs are index-only CSV/JSON with Eval IDs; no code/coords ingested.\n  - Native-geometry SAT examples are recorded where applicable; Noesis-geometry projection is the basis for policy decisions.\n  - Future additions (e.g., Prometheus III) will follow the same schema and be appended as v3.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E artifacts refreshed (protocol v1 + consolidated summary JSON). Results so\
    \ far (Noesis geometry, sets-only):\n  - Boundary matches across SOTAs at tol=2e−8 (J=1.0); at tol=1e−8 small mismatches reconcile with tol shift.\n  - Interior Top‑K overlaps remain modest (≈0.07–0.35 depending on lineage/K), consistent with co‑optimal interior multiplicity.\n  - Gate v1: SAT on Prometheus II and Scientia II inputs; UNSAT on Quest I. Policy guard (both pairs near-active@1e−8 on Noesis) prevents operator attempts so far.\n  Files: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json, storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json. Contributions welcome (sets-only with Eval IDs).\n```"
