role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Validate Appendix E artifacts and baseline boundary counts (logs to STDOUT)\"\ntags: \"utility, reproducibility, sets-only, appendix-e, validation\"\nabstract: \"Checks existence and basic consistency of Appendix E protocol/summary, Noesis snapshot files, and key sets-only inputs. Recomputes Noesis boundary counts at tol∈{1e−8,2e−8}; prints PASS/FAIL and metrics to STDOUT. Returns baseline pack (shrunk) for a valid evaluation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Paths\n  P_PROTO   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json'\n  P_SUMMARY = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json'\n  P_C       = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  P_R       = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  P_B_NOE   = 'storage/noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n  P_Q_BOUND = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/noesis_data/quest_eval562_boundary_contacts_disc_level.csv'\n \
    \ P_Q_J_V3  = 'storage/noesis/nmap/quest_eval562_boundary_jaccard_tol1e8_v3.json'\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def fexists(p): \n      ok = os.path.exists(p)\n      print(f'CHECK EXISTS: {p} -> {\"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\"}')\n      return ok\n\n  def read_json(p):\n      try:\n          with open(p,'r') as f:\n              return json.load(f)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('JSON_READ_ERROR:', p, e)\n          return None\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(P_C) and os.path.exists(P_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(P_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(P_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      # fallback grid (to keep eval valid if snapshot missing)\n      centers = []\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < N:\n                  centers.append([0.1+0.2*i, 0.1+0.15*j])\n      return np.array(centers,float), np.full(N,0.08,float)\n\n  def boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, tol):\n      S\
    \ = set()\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      slacks = {\n          'xL': x - r,\n          'xR': 1.0 - x - r,\n          'yB': y - r,\n          'yT': 1.0 - y - r\n      }\n      for i in range(N):\n          for side, arr in slacks.items():\n              if arr[i] <= tol + 1e-12:\n                  S.add((i, side))\n      return S\n\n  def read_noesis_boundary_csv(p_csv):\n      S = set(); cnt = 0\n      if not os.path.exists(p_csv):\n          return S, cnt\n      with open(p_csv, 'r', newline='') as f:\n          reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for row in reader:\n              try:\n                  i = int(str(row.get('i','')).strip())\n                  k = str(row.get('kind','')).strip()\n                  if k not in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'): \n                      continue\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      S.add((i,k)); cnt += 1\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return S, cnt\n\n  def construct_packing():\n   \
    \   # Existence checks\n      ok_proto   = fexists(P_PROTO)\n      ok_summary = fexists(P_SUMMARY)\n      ok_c       = fexists(P_C)\n      ok_r       = fexists(P_R)\n      ok_bnoe    = fexists(P_B_NOE)\n      ok_qb      = fexists(P_Q_BOUND)\n      ok_qv3     = fexists(P_Q_J_V3)\n\n      # Parse JSONs if present\n      proto   = read_json(P_PROTO)   if ok_proto   else None\n      summary = read_json(P_SUMMARY) if ok_summary else None\n      if proto is not None:\n          print('PROTO_VERSION:', proto.get('version'))\n          print('PROTO_GATE_INTERIOR_TOL:', proto.get('gate_v1',{}).get('interior_tol'))\n      if summary is not None:\n          meta = summary.get('meta', {})\n          entries = summary.get('entries', [])\n          print('SUMMARY_META_KEYS:', sorted(list(meta.keys())))\n          print('SUMMARY_ENTRIES_COUNT:', len(entries))\n\n      # Boundary counts (Noesis)\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      S_1e8 = boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, tol=1e-8)\n      S_2e8 = boundary_from_snapshot(c,\
    \ r, tol=2e-8)\n      print('NOESIS_BOUNDARY_COUNTS snapshot: tol=1e-8 ->', len(S_1e8), '; tol=2e-8 ->', len(S_2e8))\n\n      # Compare exported Noesis CSV vs computed set at tol=1e-8\n      S_csv, csv_rows = read_noesis_boundary_csv(P_B_NOE)\n      inter = len(S_csv & S_1e8)\n      uni   = len(S_csv | S_1e8) if (S_csv or S_1e8) else 0\n      j     = (inter/uni) if uni>0 else 1.0\n      print('NOESIS_EXPORT_CSV_ROWS:', csv_rows)\n      print('NOESIS_EXPORT_VS_COMPUTED@1e-8: inter/union/J =', inter, '/', uni, '/', j)\n\n      # Quest artifacts quick check (boundary CSV present and jaccard v3 JSON present)\n      if ok_qb:\n          with open(P_Q_BOUND,'r') as f:\n              head = f.readline().strip()\n              print('QUEST_BOUNDARY_CSV_HEADER:', head)\n      if ok_qv3:\n          qv3 = read_json(P_Q_J_V3)\n          if qv3 is not None:\n              print('QUEST_V3_COUNTS inter/union/J:', qv3.get('intersection'), qv3.get('union'), qv3.get('jaccard'))\n\n      # Return baseline\
    \ pack\n      r_out = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      print('VALIDATION_DONE:', 'OK')\n      return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```"
