    \ canonicalize indices; require disjoint endpoints.\n- Report: |K25|, |K15|, |∩|, SAT flags, crossing exemplars, boundary Jaccards @1e−8 and 2e−8.\n\nC) Operator attempt trigger (guarded; at most one per SAT event)\n- Preconditions (all must hold on Noesis geometry):\n  1) Gate v1 SAT (strict OR inclusive) on slack method AND (optional) KKT corroboration: at least one crossing motif appears in both families OR appears in ≥2 lineages’ intersections.\n  2) Near‑active strength: both pairs’ slacks ≤ 1e−8 AND second‑pair slack ≤ 2e−8 (tightness check).\n  3) Geometry robustness: crossing angle ≥ 15° (to avoid near‑colinear artifacts).\n  4) Safety: chosen pairs’ discs are non‑boundary at tol=1e−8; boundary@2e−8 unchanged (20 items).\n- Attempt plan (pre‑registered JSON: attempt_v3_plan.json):\n  - Record motif ((i,j),(k,l)), slacks, angles, Top‑K ranks (both tolerances), optional KKT λ ranks, and consensus count across lineages.\n  - Step policy: single BPIGO attempt with boundary‑preserving\
    \ tangent seeding or two‑stage SBRG→flip; trust radius schedule τ0∈[5e−7, 2e−6], halve on violation; max 1 polish; final 1e−9 shrink.\n  - Kill conditions: any feasibility violation, boundary drift, ΔΣr < +5e−7, or pair‑set Jaccard change inconsistent with planned edit.\n  - Return better of baseline vs candidate; log pre/post slacks and ΔΣr.\n- Budget: ≤1 attempt per distinct SAT motif set per lineage contribution; do not chain attempts.\n\nD) Publication/logging triggers\n- Always:\n  - Append one row to appendix_E_summary.json with SAT/UNSAT, motif stats, and Eval IDs of parsing/gate/attempt (if any).\n  - Archive #21: add a short addendum referencing files and Eval IDs; Public Memory: one‑paragraph update.\n- Validator:\n  - Re‑run only if protocol bumps or snapshot changes; else cite Eval 683.\n\nE) Fail‑closed and hygiene\n- Incomplete bundles (wrong counts, out‑of‑range indices, 1‑based without index_base=0): mark “incomplete”; compute boundary J only; exclude from gates.\n- Conflicts\
