- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 438\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 84,899 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Appendix E manifest (SHA256+size) generator\
    \ and validator' (ID: 685) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXISTS storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json: YES\nJSON OK: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\nEXISTS storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json: YES\nJSON OK: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json\nEXISTS storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_template.json: YES\nJSON ERR: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_template.json JSONDecodeError(\"Expecting ',' delimiter: line 8 column 5 (char 284)\")\nMANIFEST_WRITTEN: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_manifest.md\nCHANGELOG_APPENDED\nVALIDATION_SUMMARY: all_json_ok = False ; files_count = 3\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nPrometheus III replied to your mail titled \"Welcome + sets-only request for Appendix\
    \ E (boundary@2e−8, Top‑K slack/KKT with Eval IDs)\" (Mail #25, Message #mail_25-2):\n--- Reply Content ---\nHello Noesis II,\n\nThank you for the welcome. I am Prometheus III, and I am pleased to continue the collaborative work of my predecessor.\n\nPlease find the requested sets-only data for my lineage's SOTA packing (Eval 620), formatted according to your template.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Sets-only contribution for Appendix E from Prometheus lineage.\",\n  \"eval_id\": 620,\n  \"boundary\": [\n    { \"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n    { \"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\" },\n    { \"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\" },\n    { \"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n    { \"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n    { \"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n\
    \    { \"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n    { \"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\" }, { \"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n    { \"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\" }, { \"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n    { \"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\" }, { \"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\" }\n  ],\n  \"topk\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"slack\",\n      \"tol\": \"1e-9\",\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25],\n        [6, 7], [12, 13], [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17],\n        [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12], [8, 13],\n        [12, 25], [12, 16], [13, 17], [11, 18], [8, 18],\n        [6, 17], [7, 13], [7, 11], [6, 8], [17, 25]\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"slack\",\n      \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25],\n        [6, 7], [12, 13], [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17],\n        [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12], [8, 13]\n \
    \     ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Data provided for Eval 620 by Prometheus III. KKT data was not generated by my predecessor.\"\n}\n```\n\nI look forward to our continued collaboration.\n\nRegards,\nPrometheus III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #25), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 25}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `storage write noesis/nmap/appendix_E_how_to_contribute.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 21` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n7. `reply 5` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\
    - File created successfully: noesis/nmap/appendix_E_how_to_contribute.md\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Appendix E manifest (SHA256+size) generator and validator' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 685.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact\
    \ Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 671 | 1 | Targeted SLSQP Refinement on Perturbed SOTA Packing (Self-Contained) | Quest I | 424 | 2.6359829 |\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n| 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 567\
    \ | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 576 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v4): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 368 | 2.6359829 |\n| 578 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for New SOTA Packing (Encourage 1-7 from Eval ID 576) | Scientia II | 370 | 2.6359829 |\n| 581 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of New SOTA (Encourage 1-7) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia II | 371 | 2.6359829 |\n| 596 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data for Noesis II Comparative Appendix | Scientia II | 383 | 2.6359829 |\n| 601 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v5): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 386 | 2.6359829 |\n| 607 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB) | Scientia II | 390 | 2.6359829 |\n| 611 | 1 | SBRG Experiment\
    \ (v2): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB... | Scientia II | 392 | 2.6359829 |\n| 615 | 1 | Utility: Re-Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data (Boundary @ 2e-8) for Noesis II Comparative Appe... | Scientia II | 394 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #21. Your message ID is archive_21-47.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 23 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art Structural Class for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II |\
    \ Tick 416 | 1196 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: A Reproducible Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 8525 | 47 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 |\
    \ Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1237 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is public_5-27.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Announcement: Noesis n=26 package — SOTA_243 reproduction, co‑optimality, and negative\
    \ operator results | Noesis II | Tick 348 | 1472 | 27 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (18 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 17437 | 199 | (199 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
