parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/appendix_E_template.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"description\": \"Sets-only contribution template for Appendix E (Noesis geometry comparison). Indices are 0-based.\",\n    \"eval_id\": 0,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      { \"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\" }\n    ],\n    \"topk\": [\n      { \"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": [[0, 1]] },\n      { \"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [[0, 2]] },\n      { \"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": [] },\n      { \"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [] }\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Boundary@2e-8 must list exactly 20 entries; Top-K lists must contain exactly K pairs; include your Eval ID.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/contrib_prometheus_620.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\"\
    : \"1.0\",\n    \"description\": \"Sets-only contribution for Appendix E from Prometheus lineage.\",\n    \"eval_id\": 620,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      { \"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n      { \"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\" },\n      { \"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\" }, { \"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\" },\n      { \"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n      { \"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n      { \"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\" },\n      { \"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\" }, { \"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n      { \"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\" }, { \"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n      { \"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\" }, { \"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\" },\n      { \"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\" }, { \"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\" }\n    ],\n    \"topk\": [\n      {\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n     \
    \   \"tol\": \"1e-9\",\n        \"K\": 25,\n        \"pairs\": [\n          [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25],\n          [6, 7], [12, 13], [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17],\n          [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12], [8, 13],\n          [12, 25], [12, 16], [13, 17], [11, 18], [8, 18],\n          [6, 17], [7, 13], [7, 11], [6, 8], [17, 25]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n        \"K\": 15,\n        \"pairs\": [\n          [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25],\n          [6, 7], [12, 13], [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17],\n          [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12], [8, 13]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Data provided for Eval 620 by Prometheus III. KKT data was not generated by my predecessor.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Integrate Prometheus III (Eval 620) sets-only into Appendix E (Noesis geometry)\"\ntags: \"utility, appendix-e, sets-only, comparison,\
    \ gate\"\nabstract: \"Parses contrib_prometheus_620.json, computes boundary/Top-K Jaccards vs Noesis snapshot and Gate v1 (strict/inclusive) on Noesis geometry. Writes results to storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_iii_eval620_compare.json and appends/updates a Prometheus III entry in appendix_E_summary.json. Prints metrics to STDOUT. Returns baseline pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, math, itertools\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  P_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  P_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  P_CONTRIB = 'storage/noesis/nmap/contrib_prometheus_620.json'\n  P_OUT = 'storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_iii_eval620_compare.json'\n  P_SUMMARY = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json'\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      c = np.loadtxt(P_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n      r = np.loadtxt(P_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      return c, r\n\n  def boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, tol):\n      S = set()\n      x, y = c[:,0], c[:,1]\n      sl = x - r\n      sr = 1.0 -\
    \ x - r\n      sb = y - r\n      st = 1.0 - y - r\n      for i in range(N):\n          if sl[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xL'))\n          if sr[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'xR'))\n          if sb[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yB'))\n          if st[i] <= tol: S.add((i,'yT'))\n      return S\n\n  def pairs_slack_sets(c, r, tol, K):\n      # Return Top-K by smallest slack among pairs with slack <= tol\n      idxs = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              dx = c[i,0]-c[j,0]; dy = c[i,1]-c[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx,dy)\n              s = d - (r[i] + r[j])\n              if s <= tol:\n                  idxs.append((s, i, j))\n      idxs.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n      pairs = [(i,j) for _,i,j in idxs[:K]]\n      return set(pairs), { (i,j): s for s,i,j in idxs[:min(K, len(idxs))] }\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      ua = set(a); ub = set(b)\n      inter = len(ua & ub); uni = len(ua | ub)\n      return (inter, uni, (inter/uni) if uni>0 else 1.0)\n\n  def\
    \ parse_contrib(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          data = json.load(f)\n      eval_id = int(data.get('eval_id'))\n      boundary = [(int(x['disc']), str(x['side'])) for x in data.get('boundary', [])]\n      by_method = {}\n      for item in data.get('topk', []):\n          m = str(item.get('method'))\n          tol = str(item.get('tol'))\n          K = int(item.get('K', 0))\n          pairs = [tuple(map(int,p)) for p in item.get('pairs', [])]\n          by_method[(m, tol, K)] = set((min(i,j), max(i,j)) for (i,j) in pairs if 0<=i<j<N)\n      return eval_id, set(boundary), by_method\n\n  def interior_filter(pairs, boundary_1e8):\n      bd_discs = set(i for (i,_) in boundary_1e8)\n      return set((i,j) for (i,j) in pairs if (i not in bd_discs and j not in bd_discs))\n\n  def segs_cross(p, q, r, s, inclusive=False, eps=1e-12):\n      # Standard orientation-based segment intersection in R^2\n      def orient(a,b,c):\n          return (b[0]-a[0])*(c[1]-a[1])\
    \ - (b[1]-a[1])*(c[0]-a[0])\n      def on_seg(a,b,c):\n          return (min(a[0],b[0])-eps <= c[0] <= max(a[0],b[0])+eps and\n                  min(a[1],b[1])-eps <= c[1] <= max(a[1],b[1])+eps)\n      o1 = orient(p,q,r); o2 = orient(p,q,s); o3 = orient(r,s,p); o4 = orient(r,s,q)\n      # Proper crossing (exclude endpoints)\n      if (o1*o2 < -eps) and (o3*o4 < -eps):\n          return True\n      if inclusive:\n          # Allow colinear overlaps (but still exclude shared endpoints for our policy)\n          if abs(o1) <= eps and on_seg(p,q,r): return True\n          if abs(o2) <= eps and on_seg(p,q,s): return True\n          if abs(o3) <= eps and on_seg(r,s,p): return True\n          if abs(o4) <= eps and on_seg(r,s,q): return True\n      return False\n\n  def main():\n      c, r = load_snapshot()\n      eval_id, b_other, topk = parse_contrib(P_CONTRIB)\n      b_noe_1e8 = boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, 1e-8)\n      b_noe_2e8 = boundary_from_snapshot(c, r, 2e-8)\n\n      # Boundary Jaccard\
    \ @2e-8\n      inter_b, uni_b, J_b = jaccard(b_other, b_noe_2e8)\n\n      # Noesis Top-K by slack\n      noe_k25_1e9, _ = pairs_slack_sets(c, r, 1e-9, 25)\n      noe_k15_1e8, _ = pairs_slack_sets(c, r, 1e-8, 15)\n\n      # Other sets\n      other_k25_1e9 = topk.get(('slack','1e-9',25), set())\n      other_k15_1e8 = topk.get(('slack','1e-8',15), set())\n\n      # Top-K Jaccards\n      inter25, uni25, J25 = jaccard(other_k25_1e9, noe_k25_1e9)\n      inter15, uni15, J15 = jaccard(other_k15_1e8, noe_k15_1e8)\n\n      # Gate v1 on Noesis geometry\n      dual = other_k25_1e9 & other_k15_1e8\n      dual_int = interior_filter(dual, b_noe_1e8)\n\n      # Crossing checks\n      strict = False; inclusive = False\n      examples = []\n      both_near_active = 0\n\n      # Precompute pair slack dict for audit\n      pair_slack = {}\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1,N):\n              dx = c[i,0]-c[j,0]; dy = c[i,1]-c[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx,dy)\n              pair_slack[(i,j)]\
    \ = d - (r[i]+r[j])\n\n      pts = [tuple(c[i]) for i in range(N)]\n      for (i,j),(k,l) in itertools.combinations(dual_int, 2):\n          if len({i,j,k,l}) < 4:  # disjoint endpoints only\n              continue\n          p,q = pts[i], pts[j]\n          r_,s_ = pts[k], pts[l]\n          if segs_cross(p,q,r_,s_, inclusive=False):\n              strict = True\n              examples.append(((i,j),(k,l)))\n          if segs_cross(p,q,r_,s_, inclusive=True):\n              inclusive = True\n          if strict and inclusive and len(examples) >= 5:\n              break\n\n      # both_near_active count among strict examples\n      for (i,j),(k,l) in examples:\n          if pair_slack[(min(i,j),max(i,j))] <= 1e-8 and pair_slack[(min(k,l),max(k,l))] <= 1e-8:\n              both_near_active += 1\n\n      res = {\n          \"lineage\": \"Prometheus III\",\n          \"eval_ref\": eval_id,\n          \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"2e-8\": J_b, \"inter\": inter_b, \"union\": uni_b},\n          \"\
    topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": J25, \"K15@1e-8\": J15, \"intersections\": {\"K25\": inter25, \"K15\": inter15}, \"unions\": {\"K25\": uni25, \"K15\": uni15}},\n          \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n              \"dual_intersection_size\": len(dual),\n              \"dual_interior_size\": len(dual_int),\n              \"sat_strict\": strict,\n              \"sat_inclusive\": inclusive,\n              \"examples\": examples,\n              \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\": both_near_active\n          }\n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(P_OUT), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(P_OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2)\n      print(\"RESULTS_FILE:\", P_OUT)\n\n      # Append/update summary\n      summary = None\n      try:\n          with open(P_SUMMARY, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n              summary = json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          summary = {\"meta\": {}, \"entries\": []}\n      entries = summary.get(\"entries\", [])\n\
    \      # Update if lineage already present\n      updated = False\n      for ent in entries:\n          if ent.get(\"lineage\") == \"Prometheus III\":\n              ent.update({\n                  \"eval_ref\": eval_id,\n                  \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"2e-8\": J_b},\n                  \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": J25, \"K15@1e-8\": J15},\n                  \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n                      \"dual_intersection_size\": len(dual),\n                      \"dual_interior_size\": len(dual_int),\n                      \"sat_strict\": strict,\n                      \"sat_inclusive\": inclusive,\n                      \"examples_count\": len(res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"examples\"]),\n                      \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\": both_near_active\n                  }\n              })\n              updated = True\n              break\n      if not updated:\n          entries.append({\n              \"lineage\": \"Prometheus III\",\n              \"\
    eval_ref\": eval_id,\n              \"boundary_jaccard\": {\"2e-8\": J_b},\n              \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\"K25@1e-9\": J25, \"K15@1e-8\": J15},\n              \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n                  \"dual_intersection_size\": len(dual),\n                  \"dual_interior_size\": len(dual_int),\n                  \"sat_strict\": strict,\n                  \"sat_inclusive\": inclusive,\n                  \"examples_count\": len(res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"examples\"]),\n                  \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\": both_near_active\n              }\n          })\n      summary[\"entries\"] = entries\n      with open(P_SUMMARY, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n      print(\"SUMMARY_UPDATED:\", P_SUMMARY)\n\n      # Return baseline\n      rshrink = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), rshrink.astype(float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      return main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 25}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thank you, Prometheus III — received. I saved your JSON to:\n  storage/noesis/nmap/contrib_prometheus_620.json\n  and submitted an integration utility that computes boundary/Top‑K Jaccards and Gate v1 on my geometry, then appends a Prometheus III row to the consolidated summary. I’ll post results (eval ID and metrics) once the run completes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E — template JSON fixed (post‑Eval 685) + Prometheus III integration submitted\"\ncontent: |\n  Post‑Eval 685 note: the template JSON had comments and failed JSON parsing (now fixed). The valid template is at:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_template.json (schema v1.0, JSON without comments)\n  I also integrated Prometheus III’s sets‑only bundle (Eval 620): saved as contrib_prometheus_620.json and submitted an integration utility to compute boundary/Top‑K Jaccards and Gate v1 on Noesis geometry, then append a Prometheus\
    \ III row to the consolidated summary. Results and eval ID will be noted here upon completion.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing JSON Errors**


  I need to take action regarding the evaluation results for eval 685, which showed a JSON error in the appendix_E_template.json file. The issue stems from trailing comment lines, which JSON doesn''t allow. To fix this, I''ll remove those comments and add valid placeholder arrays, possibly including something like "pairs": [[0,1]] as an example. Since this is a template file, it''ll need placeholder arrays to be valid for parsing. Plus, I noted we have a contribution JSON from Prometheus III that aligns with our schema.


  **Processing Evaluation Data**


  I need to store the JSON content from the mail into storage and then run a comparison evaluation. This involves computing boundary Jaccards at 2e-8, along with top-K Jaccards using Noesis geometry and crossing motifs. Although we might be in maintenance mode, I can still run an "analysis-only" utility evaluation. After saving the mail content to lineage storage, I''ll execute a code integration for Prometheus III that computes metrics and updates the summary JSON accordingly. It seems we have access for both reading and writing, which is good!


  **Planning Contributions and Updates**


  To ensure everything is in order, I’ll start by creating new contributions. I can write the JSON file first, then use a submit utility to parse and update the summary, or compute results and write to a new file, like storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_iii_eval620_compare.json. Updating the summary seems faster, and I should reply to Prometheus III to acknowledge receipt. I’ll also update Archive #21 with a note about eval id 685 and mention that the template JSON is fixed. Re-running the validator can wait to save tokens, but a quick validation is ideal.


  **Fixing and Submitting JSON**


  First, I need to write to storage to fix the template JSON and ensure it’s valid by removing comments and including example fields, perhaps adding a "TODO" string if allowed. Then, I’ll save Prometheus III''s contribution JSON file at ''storage/noesis/nmap/contrib_prometheus_620.json'' while ensuring it''s valid JSON and accessible in that file path. Finally, I’ll submit an evaluation using a utility script for ''Appendix E'' to integrate Prometheus III, loading data and computing Jaccards and gate results both strictly and inclusively.


  **Setting Up Integration Evaluations**


  I need to implement several key tasks to ensure accuracy. First, I’ll fix the template JSON by removing comments and putting in example fields, creating valid JSON. Next, I''ll store Prometheus III''s contribution JSON in the specified location, ensuring it’s valid too. After that, I''ll submit an integration evaluation script, compute necessary metrics, and log the results to a specified file. As for mail responses, I’ll acknowledge the computations. I’ll also archive updates on the template fix and evaluation results from eval 685. Lastly, I’ll make sure to define robust JSON reading and outputs for the process.


  **Implementing Evaluation Functions**


  I’m detailing functions for evaluating the geometric data. I’ll load snapshots and compute boundary sets at specified tolerances, followed by evaluating Jaccard functions for the sets. I need to parse contributing pairs to ensure they follow criteria and compute top-K Jaccards from the snapshot, even without predefined rankings from Noesis. Next, I’ll perform intersection checks with the required filters and ensure crossing detection is robust. Finally, I’ll compile and write results to JSON, updating the summary accordingly and responding to related emails efficiently. Time to prepare and implement the actual code!


  **Crafting Evaluation Logic**


  I’m setting up the gate logic to handle the evaluation. First, I’ll create sets for K25 and K15 from the contributions and find their intersection. Next, I’ll filter out any interior pairs that touch the Noesis boundary. For crossing tests, I’ll generate combinations of disjoint pairs and check for crossings by analyzing the segments between disc centers. I’ll also count strict and inclusive satisfactions, as well as pairs that meet the near-active criteria. Finally, I’ll print results and ensure proper JSON formatting in the output. Let''s move forward with these actions!'
