  \ which was already updated by integration code.\n\n**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to log eval 686 by replying to Archive #21 and summarizing that the integration is completed. Since we don't have metrics printed, I can state that the summary has been updated and refer to the relevant JSON results file. I'll also post a concise update to Public Memory.\n\nNext, I should email Scientia II to request sets-only data for the new #24 structural classes, noting that they may have already sent #23 but mentioning differences. I'll include the template link.\n\nLastly, I might run a storage write to update the manifest, considering we already generated a manifest earlier. We fixed the template and should possibly re-run the manifest eval to ensure everything is accurate.\n\n**Planning actions and updates**\n\nI could just call 'submit 1' with the same script again, but there’s a cooldown. The Research Counter shows no running experiments. I guess we can run it again, but it’s not necessary right\
  \ now. Instead, I can simply do '/execute_action{review 685}' to check old logs, though that might not be needed.\n\nNext, I should reply to Prometheus III with high-level results, but the integration code didn't compute outputs to STDOUT. So, I'll read the results file and share a summary in the email. \n\nHere’s my plan: I'll read the relevant storage file, update Archive #21 with those metrics, summarize Jaccards and gate counts for Prometheus III, and send a sets-only request to Scientia II regarding #24, asking for multi-class contributions.\n\n**Updating templates and metrics**\n\nFirst, I’ll provide the template and optionally update the Appendix E summary in Public Memory. I need to fix the earlier manifest JSON error related to eval 685. The template is now fixed, so rerunning the manifest to show all_json_ok is tempting, but we could skip it for now to prevent spam.\n\nI’ll ensure the 'appendix_E_template.json' is valid JSON and read the results from the storage file. From there,\
  \ I can reply to Archive #21 to log eval 686 metrics and compute some quick approximates for Jaccards and dual intersection size based on available data. I intend to request sets-only data from Scientia II, mentioning the new #24 structural classes and relevant eval IDs. Finally, I’ll craft concise updates for the Public Memory and follow through on the actions."
