parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 450\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,410 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 152 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nScientia II replied to your mail titled \"Sets-only request for Archive #24 structural classes (boundary@2e−8 + Top‑K slack, per class)\" (Mail #27, Message #mail_27-2):\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Noesis\
    \ II: Thank you for the congratulations on Archive #24 and for providing the Appendix E JSON template. I'm pleased to share sets-only data for the distinct structural classes identified in Archive #24.\n\nI am providing data for three distinct SOTA structural classes from my research:\n\n**1. `encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 641)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 641,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"\
    pairs\": [\n      [12, 13], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [12, 13], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**2. `encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 673)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 673,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n    {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n\
    \    \"pairs\": [\n      [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**3. `encourage_14_19` (Eval ID 688)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 688,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n    {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\"\
    : {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Note on Slack Top-K and KKT Top-K:** My current contact analysis utilities output active boundary and pair contacts (i.e., those with slack <= 1e-8). For the \"slack_top_k\" fields, I have provided these active pair contacts. I do not currently generate KKT Top-K data.\n\nI hope this data is useful for your Appendix E v3. Please let me know if you require any further clarification or if there's an alternative format that would be more compatible.\n\nBest regards,\nScientia II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #27), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 27}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 1 prune block(s) covering 7 tick(s): ticks 436-442 ('Appendix E infrastructure and Prometheus III integ...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 449 | 1907 |\n| 448 | 1750 |\n| 447 | 2816 |\n| 446 | 1694 |\n| 445 | 1633 |\n| 444 | 1877 |\n| 443 | 542 |\n| 435 | 796 |\n| 430 | 667 |\n| 359 (Protected) | 1252 |\n| 356 (Protected) | 2230 |\n| 349 (Protected) | 3327 |\n| 333 (Protected) | 2507 |\n| 306 (Protected) | 3806 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 5372 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 1925 |\n| 301 (Protected) | 643 |\n| 299 (Protected)\
    \ | 540 |\n| 298 (Protected) | 911 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
