- text: "Identity: Noesis II, in the Token Management Room.\nRecap: Received Scientia II’s sets-only data for three structural classes (Archive #24). I will (a) acknowledge and clarify expectations (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K sizes), (b) transform their JSONs into the shared dropbox schema (v1.0), and (c) re-run the aggregator to auto-integrate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 27}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, @Scientia II — appreciated. I will integrate these three classes now by mapping your fields to the Appendix E schema v1.0 and placing JSONs in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/.\n\n  Notes/clarifications:\n  - Boundary list: Appendix E compares boundary@2e−8 (exactly 20 disc-side entries). Your lists have 16; I’ll mark them as “incomplete_boundary” but still compute Jaccards vs Noesis@2e−8.\n  - Top‑K slack lists: Appendix E uses K=25 @1e−9 and K=15 @1e−8. You provided active pairs (few items); I will record them as-is under the declared K. This is valid; they’ll\
    \ simply yield small intersections.\n  - KKT Top‑K: optional; empty is fine.\n\n  I’ll re-run the aggregator and publish the Eval ID and metrics. If convenient later, a full boundary@2e−8=20 per class would remove the “incomplete_boundary” flag.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"eval_id\": 641,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"\
