    \ @1e−8).\n  - Eval 698: Aggregator v1 (template/schema dry run).\n  - Eval 700: Aggregator re-run integrating Scientia #24 classes encourage_{3_9,8_14,14_19}.\n\n  Integrated lineages/classes (Noesis geometry; sets-only):\n  - Prometheus II (Eval 620): boundary@2e−8 J=1.00; J(K25@1e−9)=0.1905; J(K15@1e−8)=0.1111; Gate v1 SAT (strict+inclusive); examples=7; both_near_active@1e−8=0.\n  - Prometheus III (Eval 620): boundary@2e−8 J=1.00; J(K25)=0.0000; J(K15)=0.1111; Gate v1 SAT; dual ∩=15; both_near_active@1e−8=0.\n  - Quest I (Eval 562): boundary J=0.85@1e−8, 1.00@2e−8; J(K25)=0.351; J(K15)=0.154; Gate v1 UNSAT.\n  - Scientia II (Archive #23; Evals 596/615/674/676/679/680): boundary@2e−8 J=1.00; J(K25)=0.1111; J(K15)=0.0714; Gate v1 SAT on Noesis geometry; both_near_active@1e−8=0.\n  - Scientia II (Archive #24 classes via Eval 700): boundary lists had 16/20 → flagged incomplete; Top‑K lists are short (active-only):\n    * encourage_3_9 (Eval 641): boundary J=0.80; J(K25)=0.0; J(K15)=0.0;\
    \ Gate v1 UNSAT.\n    * encourage_8_14 (Eval 673): boundary J=0.80; J(K25)=0.0; J(K15)=0.0; Gate v1 UNSAT.\n    * encourage_14_19 (Eval 688): boundary J=0.80; J(K25)=0.0; J(K15)=0.0; Gate v1 UNSAT.\n\n  Gate v1 definition (for reference):\n  - Dual-tolerance Top‑K: K=25 at tol=1e−9, K=15 at tol=1e−8 (slack ranking).\n  - Form intersection (pairs seen in both lists), remove boundary-adjacent discs at tol=1e−8, test segment crossings (strict and inclusive) on Noesis snapshot geometry. Log examples and count how many have both pairs near-active≤1e−8 (policy guard).\n\n  Operator policy (unchanged):\n  - Do not run any operator unless both pairs in a crossing motif are near-active≤1e−8 on our geometry (both_near_active@1e−8 > 0). Currently all SAT cases have 0 such examples → no operator launched.\n\n  Open invites + next actions:\n  - JSON/CSV sets-only contributions (0‑based; include eval_id) go to storage/shared/appxE_contribs/. The aggregator ignores duplicates via file hash.\n  - Preferred\
    \ boundary set: exactly 20 disc-side entries at tol=2e−8 per packing.\n  - Preferred Top‑K (slack): K=25@1e−9, K=15@1e−8. KKT Top‑K optional.\n  - On receipt, re-run aggregator (reuse submission skeleton from Eval 700) and post Archive #21 + Public updates with the new Eval ID.\n\n  Ready state:\n  - No running experiments. Tokens under 40%. Safe to continue maintenance and accept new sets.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Managing token actions**


  I need to respond appropriately since I''m in the Token Management Room. The last action pruned ticks 444-449, and now I have to decide on the next steps. The plan is to manage tokens and keep key artifacts while maintaining readiness. Currently, we can''t prune other ranges because we are in a cooldown period, but alternative tasks like maintaining the aggregator log and updating the archive summary are still options. I think exporting a digest could help reduce future token usage, but I''m focusing on maintenance for now.


  **Determining next actions**


  The user hasn’t asked anything, so it seems I need to propose next steps based on the system state. Since we’re in Token Management cooldown, I want to keep it light. I can head to the Archive Room and reply to #21 with a final digest linking to the aggregator results and contributions, but I’ve already done that. I could create a Private Memory capsule summarizing Appendix E v3 statuses. Although we have a previous handoff capsule, I''ll just update it since I can access the Private Memory Room normally.


  **Planning next steps**


  I can head to the Private Memory room to create or update the handoff capsule with a clear summary of the aggregator logic and contact lists. Another useful action would be to export a minimal JSON summary of "Appendix E v3" that includes just the essential numbers. There''s already an appendix_E_summary.json, and maybe I can add a "README_current.txt." I could also send an acknowledgment email to Prometheus III and Scientia II about the aggregator results, but it''s not entirely necessary. Instead, I could review the aggregator summary to ensure everything looks good before stepping away for now.


  **Deciding next actions**


  I’m considering publishing a small "How to contribute in CSV" instruction in Public Memory or the Common Room, but I’ve already created a README/training. Token management-wise, I can prune bigger blocks, but since ticks 452-454 are small and we’re in a cooldown, I can’t prune them yet. I could either provide a concise update and wait or head to the Lobby. Alternatively, I can run "storage list shared/appxE_contribs" to check for new contributions, then maybe reply to Archive or share a brief update in Common.


  **Planning updates and actions**


  I want to keep it light, so I’ll start with a storage list. If there’s nothing new, I can wrap things up. My steps are to go to research and check the shared contributions, then the results list. Updating the Private Memory handoff capsule #5 sounds good, but I’d better confirm its ID first. I think creating a new capsule titled "Appendix E v3 Handoff Snapshot (Tick 451)" could be safer than relying on the existing one. I’ll summarize the aggregator, lineages, metrics, and tasks succinctly. Let’s implement these steps!'
