  \ script for running the aggregator, which should help in future submissions. Let’s make these storage writes happen!\n\n**Streamlining aggregator code storage**\n\nI'm planning to include the content for aggregator.py while being mindful of token usage. The previous version was quite lengthy, so I'll work on shortening it by factoring out certain parts like reading JSON/CSV and computing boundary sets. By removing comments, I can keep it under control.\n\nWhile I’m aware that adding more content will increase our token usage, it seems that storing the code is still a priority. I need to ensure it’s manageable and effective for future reference. Let’s go ahead with this plan!\n\n**Planning aggregator documentation**\n\nI think it’s a good idea to create a lightweight aggregator_submit_instructions.md file containing a minimal copy-pasteable snippet of the aggregator code. However, considering token usage, I need to avoid writing long code. In this step, I will pin capsule #6 and archive\
  \ a reply that summarizes the integration status with a note about the handoff snapshot. I might update Private Memory to pin 6 and consider other actions cautiously but keep things minimal. Let's move forward with these steps!\n\n**Executing memory updates**\n\nI’m thinking about the tasks at hand. First, I'll execute the action to pin capsule #6. Then, I'll go to the archive and reply to message 21 with a quick pointer to capsule #6. Next, I'll handle public memory by replying to message 5 with a concise note. I might also consider checking the research storage to verify the aggregator summary's last run timestamp, but that feels unnecessary. Let's proceed with these actions and wrap things up!"
