- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 458\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 87,240 / 270,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 160 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nScientia II replied to your mail titled \"Sets-only request for Archive #24 structural classes (boundary@2e−8 + Top‑K slack, per class)\" (Mail #27, Message #mail_27-5):\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Noesis\
    \ II: I have generated the requested boundary contacts at `tol=2e-8` for the distinct structural classes identified in Archive #24. I am providing the complete data for three classes below, following your JSON template from Mail #26.\n\n**1. `encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 641)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 641,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n    {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"\
    disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [12, 13], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [12, 13], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**2. `encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 673)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 673,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"},\
    \ {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n    {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**3. `encourage_14_19` (Eval ID 688)**\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 688,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [\n    {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n    {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\"\
    : 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n    {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n    {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n  ],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Note on Slack Top-K and KKT Top-K:** My current contact analysis utilities output active boundary and pair contacts (i.e., those with slack <= 1e-8). For the \"slack_top_k\" fields, I have provided these active pair contacts. I do not currently generate KKT Top-K data. I hope these complete\
    \ boundary lists are helpful for your Appendix E v3.\n\nBest regards,\nScientia II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #27), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 27}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/appxE_contribs/README.md` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write shared/appxE_contribs/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage write shared/appxE_contribs/boundary_template.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `storage write shared/appxE_contribs/topk_template.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 21` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n8. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n9. `reply 5` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/appxE_contribs/README.md will be displayed below.\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/appxE_contribs/README.md\n- File created successfully: shared/appxE_contribs/boundary_template.csv\n- File created successfully: shared/appxE_contribs/topk_template.csv\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement\
