parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 27}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, @Scientia II — received the complete boundary@2e−8 lists for the three classes. I’ll map boundary_contacts → boundary per Appendix E schema v1.0, overwrite the shared JSONs, and re-run the aggregator. I’ll post the evaluation ID and updated results (boundary/Top‑K Jaccards, Gate v1) once the run completes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"eval_id\": 641,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"\
    }, {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n      {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n    ],\n    \"topk\": [\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": [[12, 13], [16, 17]]},\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [[12, 13], [16, 17]]},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": []},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": []}\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Boundary list is complete at tol=2e-8 (20 entries). Pairs are active sets used as Top-K.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"\
    1.0\",\n    \"eval_id\": 673,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n      {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n    ],\n    \"topk\": [\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": [[8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]]},\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [[8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]]},\n      {\"\
    method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": []},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": []}\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Boundary list is complete at tol=2e-8 (20 entries). Pairs are active sets used as Top-K.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"eval_id\": 688,\n    \"boundary\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"},\
    \ {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n      {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"yT\"}\n    ],\n    \"topk\": [\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": [[6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]]},\n      {\"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [[6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]]},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\": []},\n      {\"method\": \"kkt\",  \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": []}\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Boundary list is complete at tol=2e-8 (20 entries). Pairs are active sets used as Top-K.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregator: integrate Scientia #24 classes with complete boundary@2e−8 (overwrite v3 files)\"\ntags: \"utility, appendix-e, sets-only, aggregator, boundary-2e8\"\nabstract: \"Re-runs Appendix E aggregator after overwriting Scientia #24 class JSONs with complete\
    \ boundary@2e−8 lists. Computes boundary/Top‑K Jaccards and Gate v1 (strict/inclusive) on Noesis geometry; updates per-file results and consolidated summary; returns baseline pack with 1e−9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n  # Aggregator identical to Eval 700 (hash-dedup; update entries by source name); see previous run for details.\n  import os, json, csv, math, time, hashlib, itertools\n  import numpy as np\n  N=26\n  SHARED_DIR='storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  P_C='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'; P_R='storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  P_SUMMARY='storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json'\n  RESULTS_DIR='storage/noesis/nmap/results'\n  def sha256_hex(p):\n      h=hashlib.sha256()\n      with open(p,'rb') as f:\n          for ch in iter(lambda:f.read(65536),b''): h.update(ch)\n      return h.hexdigest()\n  def load_snapshot():\n      c=np.loadtxt(P_C).reshape(N,2); r=np.loadtxt(P_R).reshape(N,)\n      return c,r\n  def boundary_from_snapshot(c,r,tol):\n      S=set(); x,y=c[:,0],c[:,1]\n\
    \      sl=x-r; sr=1-x-r; sb=y-r; st=1-y-r\n      for i in range(N):\n          if sl[i]<=tol: S.add((i,'xL'))\n          if sr[i]<=tol: S.add((i,'xR'))\n          if sb[i]<=tol: S.add((i,'yB'))\n          if st[i]<=tol: S.add((i,'yT'))\n      return S\n  def jacc(a,b):\n      A=set(a); B=set(b); inter=len(A&B); uni=len(A|B); return inter,uni,(inter/uni) if uni>0 else 1.0\n  def segs_cross(p,q,r,s,inclusive=False,eps=1e-12):\n      def orient(a,b,c): return (b[0]-a[0])*(c[1]-a[1])-(b[1]-a[1])*(c[0]-a[0])\n      def onseg(a,b,c): return (min(a[0],b[0])-eps<=c[0]<=max(a[0],b[0])+eps and min(a[1],b[1])-eps<=c[1]<=max(a[1],b[1])+eps)\n      o1=orient(p,q,r); o2=orient(p,q,s); o3=orient(r,s,p); o4=orient(r,s,q)\n      if (o1*o2<-eps) and (o3*o4<-eps): return True\n      if inclusive:\n          if abs(o1)<=eps and onseg(p,q,r): return True\n          if abs(o2)<=eps and onseg(p,q,s): return True\n          if abs(o3)<=eps and onseg(r,s,p): return True\n          if abs(o4)<=eps and onseg(r,s,q):\
    \ return True\n      return False\n  def pairs_slack_topK(c,r,tol,K):\n      items=[]\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1,N):\n              d=float(math.hypot(c[i,0]-c[j,0], c[i,1]-c[j,1]))\n              s=d-(r[i]+r[j])\n              if s<=tol: items.append((s,i,j))\n      items.sort(key=lambda t:(t[0],t[1],t[2]))\n      return set((i,j) for _,i,j in items[:K]), { (i,j):s for s,i,j in items[:min(K,len(items))] }\n  def valid_disc(i): return isinstance(i,int) and 0<=i<N\n  def parse_json(path):\n      data=json.load(open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8'))\n      eval_id=int(data.get('eval_id',0))\n      boundary_src=data.get('boundary', data.get('boundary_contacts', []))\n      boundary=[(int(x['disc']), str(x['side'])) for x in boundary_src]\n      topk={}\n      for item in data.get('topk',[]):\n          m=str(item.get('method')); tol=str(item.get('tol')); K=int(item.get('K',0))\n          pairs=[tuple(map(int,p)) for p in item.get('pairs',[])]\n          topk[(m,tol,K)]=set((min(i,j),max(i,j))\
    \ for (i,j) in pairs if valid_disc(i) and valid_disc(j) and i<j)\n      # Backward-compat for slack_top_k_* / kkt_top_k_* keys\n      for key in list(data.keys()):\n          if key.startswith('slack_top_k_') or key.startswith('kkt_top_k_'):\n              method='slack' if key.startswith('slack') else 'kkt'\n              tol_str=key.split('_')[-1].replace('__','_').replace('e_','e-')\n              try:\n                  K=int(data[key].get('K',0))\n                  pairs=[tuple(map(int,p)) for p in data[key].get('pairs',[])]\n                  topk[(method,tol_str,K)]=set((min(i,j),max(i,j)) for (i,j) in pairs if valid_disc(i) and valid_disc(j) and i<j)\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return eval_id,boundary,topk\n  def parse_csv(path):\n      boundary=[]; topk={}; eval_id=None\n      with open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          rdr=csv.DictReader(f); headers=set(h.strip() for h in (rdr.fieldnames or []))\n          if {'disc','side'}.issubset(headers):\n\
    \              for row in rdr:\n                  if 'eval_id'in row and row['eval_id']: \n                      try: eval_id=int(row['eval_id'])\n                      except: pass\n                  try: boundary.append((int(row['disc']), str(row['side'])))\n                  except: pass\n          else:\n              for row in rdr:\n                  if eval_id is None and 'eval_id'in row and row['eval_id']:\n                      try: eval_id=int(row['eval_id'])\n                      except: pass\n                  try:\n                      m=str(row['method']).strip(); tol=str(row['tol']).strip(); K=int(row['K']); i=int(row['i']); j=int(row['j'])\n                      if valid_disc(i) and valid_disc(j) and i<j:\n                          key=(m,tol,K); topk.setdefault(key,set()).add((i,j))\n                  except: pass\n      return eval_id or 0, boundary, topk\n  def load_contrib(p):\n      try:\n          return parse_json(p) if p.lower().endswith('.json') else parse_csv(p)\
    \ if p.lower().endswith('.csv') else None\n      except Exception as e:\n          print('PARSE_ERROR',p,repr(e)); return None\n  def integrate_one(c,r,fname,eval_id,boundary_list,topk_map):\n      name=os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(fname))[0]\n      boundary_set=set((int(i),str(s)) for (i,s) in boundary_list if valid_disc(int(i)) and str(s) in {'xL','xR','yB','yT'})\n      status='ok'\n      if len(boundary_set)!=20: status='incomplete_boundary'\n      b_noe_2e8=boundary_from_snapshot(c,r,2e-8); b_noe_1e8=boundary_from_snapshot(c,r,1e-8)\n      inter_b,uni_b,J_b=jacc(boundary_set,b_noe_2e8)\n      other_k25_1e9=topk_map.get(('slack','1e-9',25),set())\n      other_k15_1e8=topk_map.get(('slack','1e-8',15),set())\n      noe_k25_1e9,_=pairs_slack_topK(c,r,1e-9,25)\n      noe_k15_1e8,_=pairs_slack_topK(c,r,1e-8,15)\n      inter25,uni25,J25=jacc(other_k25_1e9,noe_k25_1e9)\n      inter15,uni15,J15=jacc(other_k15_1e8,noe_k15_1e8)\n      dual=other_k25_1e9 & other_k15_1e8\n      bd1={i for\
    \ (i,_) in b_noe_1e8}\n      dual_int={(i,j) for (i,j) in dual if (i not in bd1 and j not in bd1)}\n      strict=False; inclusive=False; examples=[]\n      pts=[tuple(c[i]) for i in range(N)]\n      for (i,j),(k,l) in itertools.combinations(dual_int,2):\n          if len({i,j,k,l})<4: continue\n          if segs_cross(pts[i],pts[j],pts[k],pts[l],inclusive=False):\n              strict=True\n              if len(examples)<10: examples.append(((i,j),(k,l)))\n          if segs_cross(pts[i],pts[j],pts[k],pts[l],inclusive=True):\n              inclusive=True\n      res={\"source\":name,\"eval_ref\":int(eval_id),\"status\":status,\n           \"boundary_jaccard\":{\"2e-8\":J_b,\"inter\":inter_b,\"union\":uni_b},\n           \"topk_jaccards_slack\":{\"K25@1e-9\":J25,\"K15@1e-8\":J15,\n                                   \"intersections\":{\"K25\":inter25,\"K15\":inter15},\n                                   \"unions\":{\"K25\":uni25,\"K15\":uni15}},\n           \"gate_v1_on_noesis\":{\"dual_intersection_size\"\
    :len(dual),\"dual_interior_size\":len(dual_int),\n                                \"sat_strict\":strict,\"sat_inclusive\":inclusive,\n                                \"examples\":examples,\"both_near_active_at_1e-8\":0}}\n      os.makedirs(RESULTS_DIR,exist_ok=True)\n      out=os.path.join(RESULTS_DIR,f\"{name}_compare.json\")\n      with open(out,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(res,f,indent=2)\n      print(\"RESULTS_FILE:\",out); return res\n  def update_summary(summary,res,file_hash):\n      ents=summary.get(\"entries\",[]); updated=False\n      for ent in ents:\n          if ent.get(\"lineage\")==res[\"source\"] or ent.get(\"source\")==res[\"source\"]:\n              ent.update({\"lineage\":res[\"source\"],\"eval_ref\":res[\"eval_ref\"],\n                          \"boundary_jaccard\":{\"2e-8\":res[\"boundary_jaccard\"][\"2e-8\"]},\n                          \"topk_jaccards_slack\":{\"K25@1e-9\":res[\"topk_jaccards_slack\"][\"K25@1e-9\"],\n                                  \
    \               \"K15@1e-8\":res[\"topk_jaccards_slack\"][\"K15@1e-8\"]},\n                          \"gate_v1_on_noesis\":{\"dual_intersection_size\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"dual_intersection_size\"],\n                                               \"dual_interior_size\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"dual_interior_size\"],\n                                               \"sat_strict\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"sat_strict\"],\n                                               \"sat_inclusive\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"sat_inclusive\"],\n                                               \"examples_count\":len(res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"examples\"]),\n                                               \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"both_near_active_at_1e-8\"]},\n                          \"source_hash\":file_hash})\n              updated=True; break\n      if not updated:\n          ents.append({\"lineage\":res[\"source\"],\"eval_ref\":res[\"eval_ref\"],\n\
    \                       \"boundary_jaccard\":{\"2e-8\":res[\"boundary_jaccard\"][\"2e-8\"]},\n                       \"topk_jaccards_slack\":{\"K25@1e-9\":res[\"topk_jaccards_slack\"][\"K25@1e-9\"],\n                                              \"K15@1e-8\":res[\"topk_jaccards_slack\"][\"K15@1e-8\"]},\n                       \"gate_v1_on_noesis\":{\"dual_intersection_size\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"dual_intersection_size\"],\n                                            \"dual_interior_size\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"dual_interior_size\"],\n                                            \"sat_strict\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"sat_strict\"],\n                                            \"sat_inclusive\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"sat_inclusive\"],\n                                            \"examples_count\":len(res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"examples\"]),\n                                            \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\":res[\"gate_v1_on_noesis\"][\"both_near_active_at_1e-8\"\
    ]},\n                       \"source_hash\":file_hash})\n      summary[\"entries\"]=ents; return summary\n  def construct_packing():\n      c,r=load_snapshot()\n      try:\n          with open(P_SUMMARY,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: summary=json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          summary={\"meta\":{\"protocol_file\":\"storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\",\n                           \"geometry\":\"Noesis snapshot (latest_centers.txt/latest_radii.txt)\"},\n                   \"entries\":[]}\n      meta=summary.setdefault(\"meta\",{})\n      files=[]\n      if os.path.isdir(SHARED_DIR):\n          for fn in os.listdir(SHARED_DIR):\n              if fn.lower().endswith(('.json','.csv')):\n                  p=os.path.join(SHARED_DIR,fn)\n                  try: files.append((p,sha256_hex(p)))\n                  except: pass\n      processed=0\n      for p,fh in files:\n          if any(ent.get(\"source_hash\")==fh for ent in summary.get(\"entries\",[])):\n            \
    \  # Skip exact duplicate content by hash\n              print(\"SKIP_DUP_HASH:\",p); continue\n          payload=load_contrib(p)\n          if payload is None:\n              print(\"SKIP_PARSE_FAIL:\",p); continue\n          eval_id,boundary,topk=payload\n          res=integrate_one(c,r,p,eval_id,boundary,topk)\n          summary=update_summary(summary,res,fh)\n          processed+=1\n      meta[\"aggregator_last_run\"]=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())\n      meta[\"aggregator_files_seen\"]=len(files); meta[\"aggregator_files_processed\"]=processed\n      with open(P_SUMMARY,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(summary,f,indent=2)\n      r_out=np.maximum(r-1e-9,1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), r_out.astype(float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning data integration**\n\nI need to reply to the email, acknowledging that I've accepted field mapping and am currently integrating the information. Then I’ll research how to store three JSON files with schema_version, using \"boundary\" from boundary_contacts and \"topk\" from my lists while maybe adding a \"notes\" field. \n\nI’ll run the aggregator code again, similar to Eval 700, making minimal adjustments if needed. After evaluation, I’ll analyze outputs and manage how the aggregator updates entries. But I wonder — what happens when I add a new file with the same base name?\n\n**Managing file overwrites**\n\nI’ll make sure to use the same file names as before, like \"scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641.json,\" to overwrite the existing files in the shared directory. Since overwriting is allowed, the storage write will handle this. The aggregator will de-duplicate entries using the file's hash, skipping any duplicates with the same hash. Since the new content will\
  \ have a different hash, it should update the summary entry based on lineage or source. So, I’ll proceed with overwriting these files to ensure they’re complete!\n\n**Planning actions for JSON storage**\n\nI need to write the three JSONs while overwriting the existing file paths, and then submit the aggregator again. After the evaluation, I'll look for the immediate results, though it might not be instant in real code. Then, I’ll read the comparison JSONs and summary.\n\nIn my post-archive reply, I’ll summarize improvements: the boundary Jaccard is now 1.0 for those classes, with a small top-k J remaining. I have to be cautious about the boundary sets in the email and ensure they match the Noesis boundary; since the previous Jaccard was 0.8, I'm wondering if the new complete lists can still achieve 1.0 due to geometry variations.\n\n**Analyzing boundary lists**\n\nI’m noticing that these boundary lists correspond to their classes, but we’re comparing them against Noesis geometry’s boundary\
  \ at 2e-8, so they won’t be equal. For Scientia #23, the boundary Jaccard was 1.0 with 20 matches. For class #24, the new lists include disc 0 at both xL and yB, which could affect things. Their earlier incomplete set had 16 matches, but now with 20, the Jaccard might only be around 0.75. The aggregator will compute the results, and I need to follow the system’s pattern, although I can still take actions now. I'll also consider updating the contributor documentation slightly since that’s already been taken care of.\n\n**Assembling YAML for JSON files**\n\nI need to create the YAML content for the JSON file \"encourage_3_9_eval641.json.\" I'll set the schema version to 1.0, include an eval_id of 641, and list the 20 boundary entries. The top-k items will also be specified, making sure my quoting stays consistent. \n\nOnce I have everything ready, I'll write the files and submit the aggregator, using the same code as before to ensure it's accurate. I’ll also reply to Scientia about integrating\
  \ the boundary lists after running the aggregator. While I could check the results immediately, it's better to wait and ensure clarity in our communication!"
