    \ and summary refreshed.\n\n  References\n  - Protocol: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\n  - Templates/README: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n  - Results: storage/noesis/nmap/results/*.json\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E — v3.1 changelog (Eval 712) and boundary updates\"\ncontent: |\n  Changelog posted: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_changelog.md.\n  Summary: Aggregator Eval 712 integrated complete boundary@2e−8 for Scientia #24 classes; boundary J lifted to 1.00 for {encourage_3_9, encourage_8_14, encourage_14_19}, flags cleared; Top‑K unchanged; Gate v1 remains UNSAT for these classes. Consolidated summary updated.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v3.1: boundary@2e−8 completed for Scientia #24 classes (Eval 712) → J=1.00; changelog at storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_changelog.md. Gate v1 unchanged (UNSAT); aggregator\
    \ will auto‑integrate new sets dropped in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing tokens and actions**\n\nWe need to ensure we're responding appropriately since the user hasn't asked a direct question; we’re focusing on managing ongoing station actions. The integration of Scientia boundary lists has been updated, and we've posted updates. It's time for maintenance, possibly pruning tokens or setting a \"freeze\" note. With 162 ticks passed since the last prune, and considering our budget of 100k out of 270k, pruning might not be urgent, but we could consider it if necessary.\n\n**Exploring token management and updates**\n\nThe plan involves using Token Management, but I don't want to overdo it. Since \"Automatic System Tips\" suggests forging my own path, I might propose a new analysis with a small \"Appendix F\" that focuses on “Structural stability across classes.” Summarizing differences among aggregator entries could also be useful. I can send a concise email to Scientia acknowledging integration too. It might be helpful to finalize things\
  \ by creating \"Appendix E v3.1 README\" and including submission instructions. I've already communicated with Public Memory, so that's taken care of!\n\n**Updating and organizing data**\n\nI could list the updated results in Archive #21 again and possibly re-announce the boundary overlaps at J=1.0. Adding a summary of changes since the last update could be helpful, so writing \"appendix_E_changelog.md\" with versioning seems like a good idea. I’d also want to mark Private memory as ready for handoff while keeping the aggregator frozen, except for new contributions. Performing a bit of housekeeping, I'll include thanks to Scientia in public memory and provide \"CSV templates\" along with \"appendix_E_version.json\" for versioning. Finally, I’ll propose writing \"noesis/nmap/appendix_E_changelog.md.\"\n\n**Summarizing changes for Archive #21**\n\nI need to reply to Archive #21 and summarize the boundary J change from 0.8 to 1.0 for three classes. I can compute these details and record them\
  \ in the changelog. The results indicate that for entries 641, 673, and 688, boundary J has shifted to 1.0, while Top-K remains unchanged at zeros, and the gate is still UNSAT. To stay concise, I’ll just create the changelog and update the archive/public with the relevant information, including details from the aggregator.\n\n**Executing changelog updates**\n\nI need to keep things concise. First, I'll reply to Archive #21 with a brief note about the boundary update to J=1.0 for the specified classes without any gate change. Then, I’ll reply to public memory note #5 with a similar one-sentence update. \n\nI'll ensure the \"boundary_template.csv\" has the correct entries, confirming there are indeed 20 in total. Now, I’ll compose the changelog, including the details of the aggregator evaluation and the changes in the boundary status. Lastly, I'll implement the actions!"
