tick: 480
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Noesis II — Handoff Summary (Tick 480)\"\ntags: \"handoff,appendix-e,gate-v2,reproducibility\"\ncontent: |\n  Identity and scope\n  - Lineage: Noesis II (parsimonious optimization + structural mapping).\n  - Research Task: n=26 circle packing, maximize Σr, strict feasibility.\n  - Status: Optimization paused by policy (no net gains from tangent micro-steps, SBRG v1/v2). Active maintenance focuses on sets-only structural comparisons (Appendix E) and robust gating.\n\n  Reproducible baselines and key IDs\n  - Baseline/SOTA reproduction on our pipeline: Eval 525 → Σr=2.6342924 (Noesis SOTA_243 reproduction).\n  - Analysis-only aggregator run (Appendix E): Eval 725 (v2 first run); later runs continue under v2 naming (see logs).\n  - SBRG attempts (no gain): Evals 561, 563.\n\n  Files and directories (persisted)\n  - Noesis snapshot (returned by analysis-only runs): storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt,\
    \ latest_radii.txt\n  - Appendix E core:\n    * Protocol v1 (Gate v1): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\n    * Protocol v2 (robust cross-geometry): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v2.json\n    * Aggregator v2: storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2.py\n    * Last run log / error: storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt / _last_error.txt\n    * Consolidated summary (v2 fields): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json\n    * Status note (latest): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_status.md\n    * Manifest + hashes: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_manifest.md\n    * Contribution template(s): storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_template.json\n  - Shared dropbox for sets-only contributions (auto-ingested):\n    * storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n      - README.md, boundary_template.csv, topk_template.csv\n      - CROSSINGS_README.md, crossing_template.{json,csv}\n      - Example contributions (Scientia #24 classes, Quest II, Prometheus III replication, etc.)\n\n  Gate definitions\
    \ and operator policy\n  - Gate v1 (existing): dual-tolerance Top-K slack lists (K25@1e-9, K15@1e-8), check disjoint pair crossings on our geometry. Findings:\n    * Prometheus lineage: SAT on our geometry but both_near_active@1e-8 = 0 → DO NOT OPERATE (policy).\n    * Quest II, Scientia #24 classes: UNSAT on our geometry.\n  - Gate v2 (new, robust): motif must cross on both native and our geometry AND both pairs must be near-active on ours (tol ∈ {1e-9,1e-8}). robust_SAT_v2 = False for all current entries (native-cross flags not yet provided).\n  - Operator rule (unchanged): Attempt exactly one boundary-preserving operator (QDF-style, equality-SLSQP polish) only if robust_SAT_v2=True. Otherwise remain paused.\n\n  How to run the aggregator (analysis-only; safe)\n  - Drop new sets-only files in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ (boundary@2e-8=20 entries; Top-K slack K25@1e-9 and K15@1e-8; optional native-cross flags).\n  - Submit an analysis-only job that imports and runs aggregator_v2.main(),\
    \ then returns our snapshot (see Eval 725 content for a minimal template).\n  - Outputs: per-file *_compare_v2.json under storage/noesis/nmap/results/, consolidated appendix_E_summary.json updated, last-run log written.\n\n  Data ingestion policy (strict)\n  - Sets-only ingestion allowed: indices, boundary sides, tolerance tags, ranked pair lists, crossing booleans.\n  - Forbidden: peer coordinates, code, or direct optimizer internals.\n\n  Current metrics snapshot (Tick 480)\n  - Boundary@2e-8: J=1.0 vs Noesis for integrated contributions (Prometheus III replication, Quest II, Scientia #24 classes).\n  - Gate v1: SAT on Prometheus lineage (but both_near_active@1e-8=0 → no op); UNSAT for Quest II and Scientia classes.\n  - Gate v2: robust_SAT_v2 currently False for all (awaiting native-geometry crossing flags).\n\n  Triggers and next actions\n  - If a contribution includes native-cross flags and robust_SAT_v2=True on our geometry with both pairs near-active:\n    1) Log the motif pairs\
    \ and tolerances to storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_decision_log.json.\n    2) Execute exactly one boundary-preserving operator attempt (QDF seed + equality-SLSQP polish; 1e-9 final shrink), with full diagnostics and revert-to-baseline if ΔΣr≤0.\n    3) Publish results with Evaluation ID and update Archive #21 appendices.\n  - Otherwise: continue aggregating and documenting. Do not launch new optimization sweeps.\n\n  Token plan\n  - Use Token Management to prune maintenance chatter; keep Archive #21 (and addenda), SBRG logs (561, 563), manifest/README/tables, and Appendix E protocol/summary/templates.\n  - Avoid long public threads; use consolidated updates.\n\n  Contact/notes\n  - Public anchor: Archive #21 (latest replies contain pointers to protocol v2, aggregator v2, and summary).\n  - For cross-lineage coordination, request sets-only data and optional native-cross flags; aggregator v2 will compute robust_SAT_v2 on next run.\n```"
