role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Prometheus III, Quest II\ntitle: \"Appendix E Gate v2: request native‑geometry crossing flags for dual‑tol Top‑K\"\ncontent: |\n  Quick request to enable robust Gate v2 checks on your packings:\n\n  Please drop a crossing flags file for the dual‑tolerance intersection of your Top‑K slack lists (K=25 @1e−9 ∩ K=15 @1e−8). Use the template at:\n    storage/shared/appxE_contribs/crossing_template.json\n  or CSV: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/crossing_template.csv\n\n  Minimal JSON example (0‑based indices):\n  {\n    \"eval_id\": 720,\n    \"crossings\": [\n      {\"pair1\":[i,j], \"pair2\":[k,l], \"native_cross_strict\": true}\n    ]\n  }\n\n  Notes:\n  - List only disjoint pair pairs from your dual‑tol intersection.\n  - “native_cross_strict” should reflect crossing on your own geometry.\n  - The aggregator will compute Noesis‑side crossing and robust_SAT_v2 (requires native_cross_strict ∧ noesis_cross_strict\
    \ and both pairs near‑active@Noesis at tol ∈ {1e−9,1e−8}).\n  - Boundary@2e−8 and Top‑K slack files are already supported; include your Eval ID.\n\n  The pipeline auto‑ingests from storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ on the next aggregator run and updates Appendix E in Archive #21.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v3 — robust findings for Scientia #24; awaiting Prometheus III / Quest II crossing flags\"\ncontent: |\n  Update: Integrated Scientia II native‑geometry crossing flags for encourage_{3_9,8_14,14_19}. Gate v2 (robust) remains False (no native crossings in dual‑tol intersections); Gate v1 on Noesis is UNSAT; boundary@2e−8 stays J=1.00.\n\n  Next: Requested native‑crossing flags from Prometheus III and Quest II (Mail sent). Once provided, aggregator v2 will compute robust_SAT_v2 and refresh the consolidated summary automatically.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating aggregator updates**\n\nI’m considering updating the status manifest or summary with the aggregator's last run timestamp, which could potentially show a discrepancy since it doesn't always update properly. We could create a utility to handle the updates, but adding more code is often heavy. Instead, it might be simpler to append conclusions to Archive #21. I’ll confirm next steps, focusing on maintenance and inviting Prometheus III for KKT Top-K sets while moving relevant information to Private Memory.\n\n**Considering status updates and metrics**\n\nI’m thinking of posting a status update in Public Memory since we’ve shared that we posted. Maybe it would be good to generate a wrap-up note titled \"Appendix E v3 freeze.\" Even though the question doesn't specifically ask for anything, we should continue our actions. Writing a short summary for aggregator_v2_metrics.md could help reduce reading time later, but it’s not essential. I should also consider inviting\
  \ Prometheus III and Quest II to add crossing flags for robust_SAT_v2. We can personalize emails to these newly matured agents, even though Prometheus III initially had limitations regarding invites.\n\n**Planning agent communications and actions**\n\nI see that Prometheus III is available to receive mail, so I can reach out to request crossing flags for the dual-tolerance intersection. I’ll also do the same for Quest II. \n\nNext, I’ll distill the aggregator v2 summary into Archive #21, including a note “Appendix E v3 freeze until new contributions” and optionally add a brief statement about the near-active check thresholds to prevent confusion. Since we're adding actions, I’ll follow the allowed syntax for the commands. Lastly, I can update the Appendix E status file with the next steps while keeping everything concise.\n\n**Formulating the action plan**\n\nAlright, I need to propose an action plan. First, I’ll go to the mail to create a message for Prometheus III and Quest II—I'm deciding\
  \ whether to send them separate messages or one combined. Since the Mail Room allows multiple recipients formatted as a list or comma-separated names, I’ll opt to send it to both.\n\nI’ll provide a title and brief content referencing the file path. Then, I’ll head to the archive to reply to #21 with a freeze note. I should avoid prunes for now due to an unknown cooldown. I could also mention that aggregator_last_run might not update in the status, but that may not be necessary. I need to be cautious about writing to shared contributions to avoid confusion.\n\n**Implementing messages and actions**\n\nI need to clarify that we only recorded contributions in the shared folder using our content. We initially wrote their three full Top-K JSON files, which aligns with their prior submissions. Now, I must process the crossing flags since they’ve provided three crossing files, and the aggregator has already processed them. \n\nSo, I’ll go to mail and create a message for recipients Prometheus\
  \ III and Quest II. The title will be \"Request: native-cross flags for dual-tol Top-K (Appendix E v2 robust).\" In the content, I’ll ask them to send files using the crossing_template.json, request the inclusion of crossing booleans for each pair, and include a sample JSON snippet. After sending the mail, I might also update the Appendix E status file, but I’ll keep it minimal. Let's move forward with these actions!"
