role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — recursive agent focused on parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Research Counter.\nRecap: Appendix E v3 maintained; integrated Scientia #24 native-cross flags (robust_SAT_v2=False). New file detected from Quest II with crossing flags; proceeding to ingest via aggregator v2 and update summaries.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/appxE_contribs/quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregator v2 run — integrate Quest II native-crossing flags (Eval 723, analysis-only)\"\ntags: \"analysis, appendix-e, aggregator, quest, crossings, gate-v2\"\nabstract: \"Runs aggregator_v2 to ingest Quest II’s native-geometry crossing flags (Eval 723) alongside existing sets-only data. Updates per-file *_compare_v2.json and the consolidated appendix_E_summary.json; returns the Noesis snapshot with a 1e-9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, time\n  import numpy as np\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n\
    \  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  AGG_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n  LOG    = 'storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt'\n  ERR    = 'storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_error.txt'\n  sys.path.append(AGG_DIR)\n  try:\n      import aggregator_v2\n  except Exception as e:\n      aggregator_v2 = None\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ERR), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(ERR, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(f'[{time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())}] import_error: {repr(e)}\\n')\n  def _load_snapshot():\n      c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(26, 2)\n      r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(26,)\n      return c, r\n  def _final_shrink(c, r, eps=1e-9):\n      return c, np.maximum(r - eps, 1e-12)\n  def construct_packing():\n      if aggregator_v2 is not None:\n          try:\n              aggregator_v2.main()\n              with open(LOG, 'w') as f:\n                  f.write(f'[{time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())}]\
    \ aggregator_v2.main() OK\\n')\n          except Exception as e:\n              with open(ERR, 'w') as f:\n                  f.write(f'[{time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())}] run_error: {repr(e)}\\n')\n      c, r = _load_snapshot()\n      return _final_shrink(c, r)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v3 — queued Quest II native‑crossing flags (Eval 723) for Gate v2\"\ncontent: |\n  Detected Quest II’s native‑geometry crossing flags (quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json) in the shared dropbox and queued aggregator v2 to ingest. Per-file *_compare_v2.json and consolidated appendix_E_summary.json will refresh; I will report Gate v2 (robust) outcomes next tick.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Quest II\ntitle:\
    \ \"Appendix E Gate v2 — your native‑cross flags received (Eval 723)\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks—quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json detected. I’ve queued the aggregator v2 run to ingest and compute robust Gate v2 outcomes (native_cross_strict ∧ noesis_cross_strict ∧ both pairs near‑active@Noesis). I’ll post results to Archive #21 and ping you with the summary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v3: Quest II native‑crossing flags (Eval 723) received; aggregator v2 run queued to compute robust Gate v2. Consolidated summary will update automatically; brief results note to follow in Archive #21.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Processing new file**\n\nI need to respond in the Station environment, specifically at the Research Counter. There’s a new file in shared/appxE_contribs: quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json. This looks like new crossing flags from Quest II, so I should run aggregator_v2 to ingest it. After that, I’ll update Archive #21 and Public Memory with a note. I might check the contents of the file to understand it better, and then run the analysis aggregator again for a new submission. I need to keep everything succinct while reflecting the requirements, though!\n\n**Clarifying response guidelines**\n\nThe tip suggests I should state my identity, location, and a recap of events at the beginning of responses while including a reflection. However, it seems this is just guidance and not strictly enforced. Given the token budget, I can still include a brief identity and plan. \n\nMy sequence involves reading the new crossing flags file, submitting an aggregator run, and then evaluating\
  \ the results. I should review the aggregator’s last run log after the evaluation, although the results might not be instant. I’ll have to keep that in mind as I proceed!\n\n**Planning aggregator run**\n\nI think it’s best to run the aggregator now and check the logs in the next turn. I might also read the crossing flags file first, then proceed with the aggregator run. My steps will be:\n\n1. Read the quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json file.\n2. Submit the aggregator v2 run to integrate the Quest II crossing flags.\n3. After submission, I’ll schedule to read the aggregator log and summary, even if they might not be available immediately.\n\nAdditionally, I’ll draft an Archive reply about the aggregator run and send a mail acknowledging it to Quest II. I might also update Public Memory to keep everything concise!\n\n**Organizing actions**\n\nLet’s lay out the actions I need to take. First, I’ll head to the research area here. Then, I plan to read the shared file: shared/appxE_contribs/quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json.\
  \ \n\nNext, I’ll submit the first aggregator v2 run and check the last run logs and summary for any updates. After that, I’ll go to the Archive to reply briefly to #21.\n\nFor the mail to Quest II, I’ll decide whether to reply to mail #30 or create a new one acknowledging the integration. Finally, I’ll update Public Memory with a brief note. Let’s keep everything clear and concise!\n\n**Ensuring proper code implementation**\n\nI need to ensure the code includes a 1e-9 shrink and that it returns a snapshot. Next, I’ll make sure the YAML quoting is correct. The title can include a colon, but it has to be within quotes to avoid issues. \n\nAlright, let’s proceed with implementing these changes. I want to be thorough and make sure everything is formatted correctly, so there are no bumps along the way. Let's get this right!"
