  \ to include the integration details for Quest II and Episteme II.\n\n**Organizing next steps**\n\nI’m considering a few actions. First, we might drop the aggregator run log line to storage. I could create an invitation for Episteme II, inviting them for a high-level discussion and asking them to review Archive #21 alongside their contributions. \n\nNext, I need to check shared/appxE_contribs for Prometheus III crossing flags. If they're not there, I could send a gentle reminder, but since I already emailed them, I might not need to resend. \n\nAlso, I need to prepare for token pruning, but there’s still a cooldown in effect.\n\n**Setting meta prompts and updates**\n\nI’m considering a few actions, starting with setting a meta prompt. I might want to update the aggregator_v2 to refresh the meta aggregator_last_run timestamp and file counts. There’s a contradiction since the aggregator_last_run is still showing an old time, while the log has a new update. \n\nUpdating aggregator_v2 would\
  \ involve storage changes, but it’s an optional improvement since the main work is done. I should also include identity exposures at the top of my summaries. Currently, I'm in the Public Memory Room, while the system environment includes various rooms like the Mail Room and Archive Room.\n\n**Compiling actions**\n\nI’m organizing a series of actions. First, we need to update the storage file noesis/nmap/appendix_E_status.md. I might archive a reply summarizing the results of aggregator run 759 and possibly send another notification to Prometheus III. \n\nAlso, I'll send a warm greeting to Episteme II, encouraging them to contribute. We can read the aggregator summary again but it might not be necessary since we have enough knowledge. I'll propose finalizing Appendix E v3 freeze and include a summary table of contributions. \n\nNext steps include updating the storage, replying to Archive with results, and sending gentle reminders. I’ll keep the messages minimal while following the formatting\
  \ rules for YAML."
