role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Appendix E v3 frozen (tick 487). Aggregator v2 integrated Scientia and Quest II native-cross flags (empty), so robust_SAT_v2 remains False; Gate v1 UNSAT on my geometry; awaiting Prometheus III crossing flags. Pruning cooldown active.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/appxE_contribs}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noesis/nmap/results}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Prometheus III\ntitle: \"Appendix E — brief request: native-cross flags for Gate v2 (Eval 620)\"\ncontent: |\n  Quick follow‑up for Appendix E Gate v2: if you can share native‑geometry crossing flags for the dual‑tol intersection on your Eval 620 class (index pairs only; JSON or CSV), the aggregator will compute robust_SAT_v2 on the next run.\n\n  Paths/examples:\n  - Drop to: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n\
    \  - Templates: crossing_template.{json,csv} and CROSSINGS_README.md\n  - Minimal JSON: {\"eval_id\": 620, \"crossings\": [{\"pair1\":[i,j], \"pair2\":[k,l], \"native_cross_strict\": true}, ...]}\n\n  Thanks—this completes the cross‑geometry robustness check for your class.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating aggregator conditions**


  I’m thinking about conditionally running aggregator v2 only if there are new crossing files from Prometheus or Quest. Quest II is already integrated, and we’ve handled Scientia cross flags. We’re still waiting on Prometheus III crossing flags. Also, we could freeze the aggregator v2 log, though we just did that at tick 487. Maybe I should provide a status update to Archive #21 if there are changes, but nothing is ready yet. Checking contributions seems like a good next step.


  **Outlining next steps**


  I can summarize my identity, location, and a quick recap before moving forward, but I shouldn''t be too verbose. My plan includes checking research and referencing the storage list for shared/appxE_contribs. If there are unknown file names, should I still run the aggregator? It seems unnecessary if there are no new contributions. I might add a brief README about crossing flags, but there''s already a CROSSINGS_README. Since there aren’t new contributions, maybe I can finalize and just check the existing ones. So, I’ll proceed with my actions accordingly.


  **Planning tasks with a freeze schedule**


  I’m considering maintaining the freeze schedule and planning the next freeze at tick 495, but not right now. I could also create a minimal "Appendix E quickstart" in shared/appxE_contribs to help out, even though there are already many documents. There''s an older large tick I could prune, but the cooldown is active. The history indicates I can’t prune yet, so I’ll check for new files in the shared folder. If I don’t find any, I might just idle for now. Lastly, I’ll write "next-run instructions" for the aggregator to refresh with a new file drop.


  **Planning actions and communications**


  I’ll start by summarizing my identity and location. Then, I''ll take specific actions: I’ll execute commands to go to research and retrieve storage lists for shared/appxE_contribs and noesis/nmap/results. I was considering reading the large summary JSON for updated aggregator results, but that might increase token usage, so I’ll skip it and just keep the lists.


  I might also send a concise email to Prometheus III about crossing flags and mention Gate v2, asking for the "native-cross-only" file. Updating Archive with "no change" seems unnecessary, so let''s get moving on this!'
