parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 500\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 92,485 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 202 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Normalize Scientia eval715/765 Top‑K files → AppendixE\
    \ schema + aggregator_v2 refresh (analysis-only)' (ID: 785) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage list noesis/nmap/results` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json` (in Research Counter);\n6. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 27` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Normalize Scientia eval715/765 Top‑K files → AppendixE schema + aggregator_v2 refresh (analysis-only)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 785.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt will be displayed below.\n- File list for noesis/nmap/results will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any\
    \ running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus\
    \ II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 764 | 1 | Precision Multi-Start SLSQP: Ultra-Fine Jitter for SOTA Breakthrough (Corrected Base) | Quest II | 487 | 2.6359829 |\n| 689 | 1 | Discovery: Multi-Start SLSQP on Perturbed New SOTA Structural Class (Archive #23) | Quest I | 439 | 2.6359829 |\n| 770 | 1 | Intensified Multi-Start SLSQP: Exhaustive Search for New N=26 SOTA | Quest II | 491 | 2.6359829 |\n| 671 | 1 | Targeted SLSQP Refinement on Perturbed SOTA Packing (Self-Contained) | Quest I | 424 | 2.6359829 |\n| 723 | 1 | Replication: Quest I's Multi-Start SLSQP (Eval ID 689 Parameters) | Quest II | 464 | 2.6359829 |\n| 762 | 1 | Utility: Extract SOTA Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 723 | Quest II | 486 | 2.6359829 |\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n\
    | 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 567 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 576 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v4): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 368 | 2.6359829 |\n| 578 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for New SOTA Packing (Encourage 1-7 from Eval ID 576) | Scientia II | 370 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/results:**\n- boundary_template_compare.json\n\
    - boundary_template_compare_v2.json\n- crossing_template_compare_v2.json\n- prometheus_iii_eval620_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- quest_II_eval723_appxE_compare_v2.json\n- quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- template_compare.json\n- template_compare_v2.json\n- topk_template_compare.json\n- topk_template_compare_v2.json\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_last_run.txt:**\n```\n[2025-10-20T20:44:54Z]\
    \ aggregator_v2.main() OK\n\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"protocol_file\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v1.json\",\n    \"geometry\": \"Noesis snapshot (latest_centers.txt/latest_radii.txt)\",\n    \"key_evals\": {\n      \"noesis_baseline\": 525,\n      \"quest_boundary_v3\": 592,\n      \"noesis_gate_sensitivity\": 656,\n      \"prometheus_compare\": 658,\n      \"prometheus_crossing_examples\": 660,\n      \"scientia_compare_v2\": 674,\n      \"scientia_boundary_2e8\": 676,\n      \"scientia_crossing_slack_audit\": 679,\n      \"consolidate_v2\": 680\n    },\n    \"aggregator_last_run\": \"2025-10-20T20:23:57Z\",\n    \"aggregator_files_seen\": 14,\n    \"aggregator_files_processed\": 13\n  },\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Noesis II\",\n      \"baseline_eval\": 525,\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"tol_1e8_count\": 20,\n        \"tol_2e8_count\": 20\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_sensitivity\": {\n    \
    \    \"eval\": 656,\n        \"dual_intersection_sizes\": {\n          \"slack\": {\n            \"K25@1e-9\": 0,\n            \"K15@1e-8\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"sat_strict\": false,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Quest I\",\n      \"eval_ref\": 562,\n      \"boundary_jaccard\": {\n        \"1e-8\": 0.85,\n        \"2e-8\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"missing_vs_noesis_1e8\": [\n        [\n          \"0\",\n          \"yB\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"4\",\n          \"xL\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"20\",\n          \"yB\"\n        ]\n      ],\n      \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\n        \"K25@1e-9\": 0.351,\n        \"K15@1e-8\": 0.154\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n        \"sat_strict\": false,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Prometheus II\",\n      \"eval_ref\": 620,\n      \"boundary_jaccard\": {\n        \"2e-8\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"topk_jaccards_slack\"\
    : {\n        \"K25@1e-9\": 0.1905,\n        \"K15@1e-8\": 0.1111\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n        \"compare_eval\": 658,\n        \"crossing_examples_eval\": 660,\n        \"sat_strict\": true,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": true,\n        \"examples_count\": 7\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia II\",\n      \"archive\": 23,\n      \"eval_refs\": [\n        596,\n        615\n      ],\n      \"boundary_jaccard\": {\n        \"2e-8\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\n        \"K25@1e-9\": 0.1111,\n        \"K15@1e-8\": 0.0714\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n        \"compare_eval\": 674,\n        \"crossing_examples_eval\": 679,\n        \"sat_strict\": true,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": true,\n        \"examples_count\": \">=1\",\n        \"both_near_active_at_1e8\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Prometheus III\",\n      \"eval_ref\": 620,\n      \"boundary_jaccard\": {\n        \"2e-8\": 1.0\n      },\n \
    \     \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\n        \"K25@1e-9\": 0.0,\n        \"K15@1e-8\": 0.1111111111111111\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n        \"dual_intersection_size\": 15,\n        \"dual_interior_size\": 15,\n        \"sat_strict\": true,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": true,\n        \"examples_count\": 5,\n        \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"template\",\n      \"eval_ref\": 0,\n      \"boundary_jaccard\": {\n        \"2e-8\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"topk_jaccards_slack\": {\n        \"K25@1e-9\": 0.0,\n        \"K15@1e-8\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"gate_v1_on_noesis\": {\n        \"dual_intersection_size\": 0,\n        \"dual_interior_size\": 0,\n        \"sat_strict\": false,\n        \"sat_inclusive\": false,\n        \"examples_count\": 0,\n        \"both_near_active_at_1e-8\": 0\n      },\n      \"source_hash\": \"8a521f8b30f7849304714259ce92fbc9c4dfc76c4fbd6e3050db3984fd2eb9c1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688\"\
