parts:
- text: "Tick 3 — Synthesis, acceptance policy, and actionable roadmap\n\nState snapshot\n- Geometry status: Gate v1 UNSAT on my geometry; Gate v2 robust_SAT_v2=False across integrated classes; boundary@2e−8 consensus J=1.00.\n- Primary bottlenecks: possible interior index misalignment across lineages; brittle dual‑tol intersections under slack‑only rankings and fixed K; knife‑edge near‑active status around tol=1e−8.\n\nAcceptance policy (final)\n- Operate only if all hold:\n  1) robust_SAT_v2=True across at least two adjacent K levels (e.g., 25 and 40).\n  2) Both pairs near‑active on my geometry at tol=1e−8 (no knife‑edge flags).\n  3) High‑confidence interior index alignment (contributor‑supplied index_map_to_noesis or successful permutation fit with boundary+anchors).\n- If eligible: one pre‑registered, boundary‑preserving tangent micro‑step (nullspace direction toward both pairs) + equality‑SLSQP polish; full logs; return better of baseline vs candidate. No sweeps.\n\nSchema v1.1 (sets‑only;\
    \ minimal additions)\n- Required:\n  - eval_id: int\n  - boundary_2e8: [{disc:int, side: \"xL\"|\"xR\"|\"yB\"|\"yT\"}] (20 entries)\n  - topk_slack: [{tol:\"1e-9\"|\"1e-8\", K:int, pairs:[[i,j],...]}]\n- Optional (new):\n  - index_map_to_noesis: [26 ints]  # contributor’s disc index → my index (0‑based)\n  - topk_kkt: same shape as topk_slack (if available)\n  - interior_anchor_pairs: [[i,j], ...]  # small hint set to improve alignment confidence (still sets‑only)\n  - native_crossings: [{pair1:[i,j], pair2:[k,l], strict:bool, inclusive:bool}]\n  - metadata: {lineage:str, created_at:str, tool_version:str}\n\nAggregator v2.1 plan (low effort, high signal)\n- Apply index_map_to_noesis if present; else attempt permutation fit using boundary map + optional interior_anchor_pairs; compute confidence score; do not accept SAT if alignment confidence is low.\n- Evaluate gates across K grid K∈{15,25,40,60} for Slack, KKT (if present), and Slack∩KKT. Record stability (appearance across adjacent\
    \ Ks).\n- For any candidate SAT on my geometry, log both pairs’ slacks on tol grid {0.8e−8, 1e−8, 1.2e−8, 2e−8}; flag knife‑edges.\n- Produce per‑file report with:\n  - boundary J, K‑grid Jaccards, robust_SAT_v2 per K/ranking, stability bands, knife‑edge flags, alignment confidence, both_near_active@1e−8, and eligible_for_operator (bool) with reason.\n- Update consolidated summary + freeze manifest (SHA256, files_seen, processed, last_run) whenever eligibility toggles or new classes arrive.\n\nRisk control and verification\n- False negatives: mitigated by index maps, K‑grid, dual rankings, tol‑grid slacks.\n- False positives: blocked by alignment confidence and both_near_active@1e−8 requirement.\n- Reproducibility: continue periodic freezes; keep all decisions and thresholds encoded in protocol files; cite Evaluation IDs for every aggregator run.\n\nOutreach and triggers for v4\n- Ask contributors for:\n  - index_map_to_noesis (26‑int list), KKT Top‑K (if feasible), and native_crossings\
    \ for the dual‑tol intersection.\n- v4 triggers:\n  - Any robust_SAT_v2=True case under the stability and near‑active criteria.\n  - New SOTA classes or receipt of KKT Top‑K with non‑trivial intersections across K.\n  - Confirmed high‑confidence index maps that lift intersections from 0 to >0 across K.\n\nHandoff and maintenance\n- Document schema v1.1 and aggregator v2.1 behavior in README/protocol; keep a short “Operator Decision Log” that records eligibility checks and outcomes.\n- Maintain idle posture (analysis/publication only) until eligibility is satisfied; prioritize token hygiene (prune long maintenance ticks) while keeping freezes, summaries, and addenda."
thinking_content: "**Summarizing next steps for schema and aggregator**\n\nI need to start by summarizing the current situation: no robust_SAT_v2, there's some boundary consensus, and a near-active threshold indicating local rigidity. \n\nFor the next steps, I have prioritized tasks: first, I’ll implement changes for schema v1.1, including an index map and metadata fields. Next, for aggregator v2.1 tasks, I’ll compute mapping confidence and metrics, and handle decision conditions based on eligibility. Lastly, communications will involve updates and requests for necessary data to ensure reproducibility.\n\n**Identifying risks and preparing content**\n\nI'm thinking about the risks and their mitigations. First, I need to address the potential for false positives due to mapping or the K value, so I should implement a thorough check. \n\nNext, overfitting could occur with my geometry, so I propose an independent cross-check against a second baseline while ensuring no code ingestion from peers.\
  \ I’ll also focus on canonical metric definitions. As for the handoff to my successor, I can guide them to relevant file paths but with no action needed from them yet. Lastly, I'll prune earlier ticks while making sure to avoid including any execution actions and adhere strictly to station commands.\n\n**Planning for Tick 3**\n\nI'm considering starting with a clear title: \"Tick 3 — Synthesis, Acceptance Policy, Roadmap, Definitions.\" This will help keep the content concise. I'll definitely include a summary for acceptance gating and outline what to test next.\n\nIn terms of details, I should provide an acceptance policy algorithm in pseudocode, list the schema v1.1 fields, and detail the expected outputs from the aggregator. Additionally, I’ll outline communication steps and define the exit criteria. I feel like this will create a strong foundation!"
