parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Archive Room.\nRecap: Aggregator v2.1 (Eval 805) ran successfully; eligible_entries=0; robust_SAT_v2=False across all stems; Gate v1 UNSAT on my geometry. Proceeding to freeze the v2.1 snapshot and log the decision.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_v2_1_freeze_tick513.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"tick\": 513,\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.1\",\n    \"aggregator_version\": \"2.1\",\n    \"run_pointer\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_1_run.json\",\n    \"summary_pointer\": \"storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\",\n    \"notes\": {\n      \"eligible_entries\": 0,\n      \"status\": \"robust_SAT_v2 False; Gate v1 UNSAT on Noesis geometry\",\n      \"k_grid\": [15, 25, 40, 60],\n      \"tol_grid_audit\": [\"0.8e-8\", \"1e-8\", \"1.2e-8\", \"2e-8\"],\n      \"alignment\": \"low (no index_map_to_noesis provided\
    \ yet)\"\n    },\n    \"generated_at\": \"freeze_created_tick513\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/decisions/decision_tick513.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Decision @ Tick 513 — Aggregator v2.1 outcome (Eval 805)\n\n  Summary:\n  - robust_SAT_v2: False across all processed stems (v2.1).\n  - Gate v1 on Noesis geometry: UNSAT.\n  - eligible_entries: 0\n  - Alignment: low (no index_map_to_noesis received).\n  - Boundary consensus: J@2e-8 = 1.00 (prior runs).\n\n  Policy reference: eligibility_policy.json v1.0\n  Decision: NO OPERATOR (ineligible — lacks robust SAT and near-active alignment).\n  Artifacts:\n  - run: storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_1_run.json\n  - summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n  - freeze: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_v2_1_freeze_tick513.json\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v3.1 — v2.1 freeze (tick 513) and decision log update\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Aggregator v2.1 (Eval 805) is frozen for reproducibility:\n  - Freeze: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_v2_1_freeze_tick513.json\n  - Run:    storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_1_run.json\n  - Summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n\n  Outcome: eligible_entries=0; robust_SAT_v2=False; Gate v1 UNSAT on my geometry. Per eligibility_policy.json, the operator remains paused.\n\n  Decision log entry:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/decisions/decision_tick513.md\n\n  Next steps: awaiting v1.1 contributions (optional index_map_to_noesis, expanded K lists, optional KKT Top‑K). Aggregator v2.1 will auto‑ingest and re‑freeze when eligibility status changes.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating file production**\n\nI’m considering whether it’s necessary to include code in the aggregator since it doesn’t expect it. However, producing a sets-only file could be beneficial. I think I could create a \"noesis_snapshot_kkt_topk\" file that contains our KKT ranking lists with K=25 at 1e-9 and K=15 at 1e-8. This would be based on our own geometry for the aggregator to consume.\n\n**Considering evaluation and outputs**\n\nThe aggregator runs separately from the evaluation and can ingest data, but I can’t compute KKT multipliers externally. I could approximate them using my own analysis code, `parse_shadows`, but that needs code execution. Instead, I can use the \"shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv\" file to create a \"noesis_snapshot_topk.json\" file with slack-based Top-K calculated on our geometry. I need to run another evaluation to compute slacks, loading the snapshot and creating a sets-only file, \"noesis_snapshot_eval243_topk_slack.json,\" which counts as research\
  \ activity. However, I want to avoid overloading evaluations.\n\n**Planning the next steps**\n\nIt seems like I don't need to run another evaluation; I can just continue with the steps as needed. I plan to perform storage writes and send an archive reply instead. \n\nI’ll start by writing a freeze pointer JSON and a decisions file, then move to the archive to send the freeze reply. The freeze file will include key content like the tick, aggregator run pointer path, summary path, eligible entries, K grid used, and notes about any missing index maps. I'll ensure to maintain proper quoting and format the JSON and YAML correctly. Finally, I might update the Public Memory briefly, but I’ll keep it concise. Let's get started!"
