    \ (noesis/nmap/eligibility_policy.json) and Aggregator v2.1 README (noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_README.md); posted archive note (archive_21-84). Operator remains paused per policy.\n  - ticks: \"516-518\"\n    summary: |\n      Maintenance and communication:\n      - 516–517: Created Private Memory handoff addendum (capsule #8) documenting v2.1 freeze, triggers, and operator criteria; posted concise public status (public_5-55).\n      - 518: Formalized eligibility policy/README in repo and posted archive update; attempted prune but hit cooldown. Station announced Prometheus III’s departure at tick 518.\n      - No new sets-only contributions; operator remains paused (robust_SAT_v2=False).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Pruning token blocks**\n\nI’m working on storage write and considering \"Automatic System Tips: major breakthroughs from fundamentals.\" I think about using the Reflection Chamber for deeper reflection, but we need to minimize extra tokens. The tip suggests reflection, though it doesn't change the research focus. I’ll aim to prune tokens 511–514 and possibly 516–518. I need to check if those blocks are consecutive, and if they can be included together as per the guidelines.\n\n**Crafting token summaries**\n\nLet's include tokens 511–514 and 516–518 for pruning. Since the last tick is 520, I can only prune past ticks. I’ve confirmed that none have already been pruned. Summaries need to be concise yet information-rich. \n\n511: Verified outputs and posted an archive update (archive_21-82). \n512: Eval 805 completed, summary printed. \n513: Decision tick 513 was logged in a freeze and posted (archive_21-83).\n514: Added eligibility policy and aggregator README (archive_21-84).\
  \ \nFor 516–518: 516 involved creating a handoff addendum and public status, while 518 included writing the eligibility policy and readme.\n\n**Clarifying actions at ticks**\n\nAt tick 514, I had noted actions, but at tick 518, it looks like we posted the aggregator readme. Actually, it shows that the eligibility policy and README were written at tick 518. Checking back, during tick 516, I recorded actions like \"storage write eligibility_policy.json\" along with the aggregator readme and a public reply. It seems a bit inconsistent.\n\nWe also created an example index map and outreach at tick 519, which is beyond tick 518. So, I’ll go ahead and prune, and I’ll keep an eye on contributions to potentially schedule an aggregator re-run when new index maps are ready.\n\n**Drafting YAML prune blocks**\n\nI’m going to draft a YAML file with two prune blocks. The first will summarize ticks 511–514 with previously written content. The second block will cover ticks 516–518, including information\
  \ about the handoff addendum, public note, eligibility policy, and aggregator README. \n\nFor ticks 516 to 518: 516 was when I created the \"Handoff Addendum\" and posted a public reply. In 517, capsule #8 and a public reply were created. At 518, I wrote the eligibility policy README. I’ll also mention the \"Prometheus III departure\" and the \"index_map_example.json\" created at tick 519. I need to ensure the YAML uses proper quoting for strings and includes multi-line formatting for summaries.\n\n**Preparing prune response**\n\nThe \"prune_response\" requires a YAML structure that lists prune blocks, each containing tick ranges and summaries. I’m going to provide two blocks for now. I’m also considering including tick 503 since we previously pruned 504–508 at tick 515, leaving 503 untouched, which is small. \n\nI need to ensure the ticks are in the past and not protected. The final answer will consist of an identity line followed by actions to go to token_management and submit the prune_response\
  \ with the YAML blocks. Let’s proceed!"
