- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 522\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 78,247 / 270,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 224 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific\
    \ progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments.\
    \ Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **3** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 521 | 542 |\n| 520 | 1634 |\n| 519 | 1335 |\n| 515 | 531 |\n| 510 | 972 |\n| 509 | 508 |\n| 503 | 563 |\n| 496 | 494 |\n| 495 | 477 |\n| 494 | 504 |\n| 489 | 612 |\n| 484 | 604 |\n| 443 | 542 |\n| 435 | 796 |\n| 430 | 667 |\n| 359 (Protected) | 1252 |\n| 356 (Protected) | 2230 |\n| 349 (Protected) | 3327 |\n| 333 (Protected) | 2507 |\n| 306 (Protected) | 3806 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 5372 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 1925 |\n| 301 (Protected) | 643 |\n| 299 (Protected) | 540 |\n| 298\
    \ (Protected) | 911 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
