tick: 527
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Completed internal audits (Eval 826 slack Top‑K; Eval 831 KKT‑proxy Top‑K) and published addenda. Detected a new sets‑only file from Quest II (quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json) in shared/appxE_contribs; I will ingest it with an analysis-only aggregator run and return the baseline pack.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregator v2.1 (targeted): Ingest quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json vs Noesis audits\"\ntags: \"analysis-only, appendix-E, sets-only, top-k, boundary, v2.1\"\nabstract: \"Ingests Quest II v3.1 sets-only file (quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json) from shared/appxE_contribs/, applies optional index_map_to_noesis, computes boundary@2e−8 Jaccard and Top‑K slack overlaps for tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60}, plus optional KKT overlaps if provided. Writes per-file result JSON under storage/noesis/nmap/results/.\
    \ Returns the baseline packing (1e−9 shrink) for evaluation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  SHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  TARGET_FILE = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json')\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results'\n  NOESIS_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  NOESIS_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  AUDIT_SLACK = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_topk_audit.json'\n  AUDIT_KKT   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit.json'\n\n  K_GRID = [15, 25, 40, 60]\n  TOLS = [1e-9, 1e-8]\n  BOUNDARY_TOL = 2e-8\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(NOESIS_C) and os.path.exists(NOESIS_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_C, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      # Fallback: feasible grid+hole (conservative)\n      centers = []\n      radius = 0.08\n      for i in range(5):\n\
    \          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < 26:\n                  x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                  y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                  centers.append([x, y])\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.full(N, radius, float)\n\n  def slacks(c, r):\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      s_xL = x - r\n      s_xR = 1.0 - x - r\n      s_yB = y - r\n      s_yT = 1.0 - y - r\n      return s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT\n\n  def boundary_set(c, r, tol):\n      s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = slacks(c, r)\n      out = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          if s_xL[i] <= tol: out.add((i, 'xL'))\n          if s_xR[i] <= tol: out.add((i, 'xR'))\n          if s_yB[i] <= tol: out.add((i, 'yB'))\n          if s_yT[i] <= tol: out.add((i, 'yT'))\n      return out\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      if not A and not B: return 1.0\n      if not A or not B: return 0.0\n      inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n      return inter/uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n\n  def load_json(path):\n      with open(path,\
    \ 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def norm_tol(t):\n      if isinstance(t, (int, float)): return float(t)\n      if isinstance(t, str):\n          t = t.replace('−','-').strip()\n          try: return float(t)\n          except: pass\n      return None\n\n  def get_index_map(data):\n      # schema v1.1: 26-int list mapping contributor index -> noesis index\n      im = data.get('index_map_to_noesis')\n      if isinstance(im, list) and len(im) == 26 and all(isinstance(x, int) for x in im):\n          return im\n      return None\n\n  def remap_pair(p, idx_map):\n      if idx_map is None: return (int(p[0]), int(p[1]))\n      i = idx_map[int(p[0])]\n      j = idx_map[int(p[1])]\n      return (int(i), int(j))\n\n  def remap_boundary_entry(e, idx_map):\n      disc = int(e['disc'])\n      side = str(e['side'])\n      if idx_map is not None:\n          disc = idx_map[disc]\n      return (disc, side)\n\n  def load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map):\n      b = data.get('boundary',\
    \ [])\n      out = set()\n      for e in b:\n          try:\n              out.add(remap_boundary_entry(e, idx_map))\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return out\n\n  def load_contrib_topk(data, method_key):\n      # Accept consolidated 'topk': [{method, tol, K, pairs}] or separate keys like 'slack_top_k_1e_9'\n      entries = []\n      if 'topk' in data and isinstance(data['topk'], list):\n          for ent in data['topk']:\n              m = ent.get('method')\n              if (method_key == 'slack' and str(m).lower().startswith('slack')) or \\\n                 (method_key == 'kkt' and str(m).lower().startswith('kkt')):\n                  entries.append(ent)\n      else:\n          # separate keys pattern for slack only\n          for key in list(data.keys()):\n              if method_key == 'slack' and key.startswith('slack_top_k_'):\n                  tol_str = key.replace('slack_top_k_','').replace('_','.')\n                  entries.append({'method':'slack',\
    \ 'tol': tol_str, 'K': len(data[key]), 'pairs': data[key]})\n      return entries\n\n  def pairs_to_set(pairs, idx_map):\n      S = set()\n      for p in pairs:\n          try:\n              i, j = remap_pair(p, idx_map)\n              if i == j: continue\n              if i > j: i, j = j, i\n              S.add((i, j))\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return S\n\n  def main():\n      c0, r0 = load_snapshot()\n      results = {\n          'source_file': os.path.basename(TARGET_FILE),\n          'generated_at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime()),\n          'notes': [],\n          'boundary': {},\n          'topk_slack': {},\n          'topk_kkt': {},\n      }\n\n      if not os.path.exists(TARGET_FILE):\n          results['notes'].append('target_file_missing')\n          os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n          with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3_1_compare_v2_1.json'), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(results,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n          # Return baseline\n          r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n          return c0.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n\n      data = load_json(TARGET_FILE)\n      idx_map = get_index_map(data)\n\n      # Boundary Jaccard @ 2e-8\n      B_noe = boundary_set(c0, r0, tol=BOUNDARY_TOL)\n      B_contrib = load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map)\n      results['boundary'] = {\n          'tol': BOUNDARY_TOL,\n          'noesis_count': len(B_noe),\n          'contrib_count': len(B_contrib),\n          'jaccard': jaccard(B_noe, B_contrib)\n      }\n\n      # Load Noesis audits\n      slack_audit = load_json(AUDIT_SLACK) if os.path.exists(AUDIT_SLACK) else None\n      kkt_audit   = load_json(AUDIT_KKT)   if os.path.exists(AUDIT_KKT)   else None\n\n      # Slack overlaps\n      results['topk_slack'] = {'entries': []}\n      slack_entries = load_contrib_topk(data, 'slack')\n      # Normalize contrib entries by tol and K and compute overlaps against Noesis slack audit\n      for\
    \ ent in slack_entries:\n          t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n          K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs', []))))\n          if t not in TOLS or K not in K_GRID: \n              continue\n          S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs', []), idx_map)\n          S_noe = set()\n          try:\n              noe_list = slack_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n              S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_list, None)  # already in Noesis index\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n          results['topk_slack']['entries'].append({\n              'tol': t, 'K': K,\n              'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n              'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n              'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n          })\n\n      # KKT overlaps (optional)\n      results['topk_kkt'] = {'entries': []}\n      kkt_entries = load_contrib_topk(data, 'kkt')\n      for ent in kkt_entries:\n          t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n          K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs',\
    \ []))))\n          if t not in TOLS or K not in K_GRID:\n              continue\n          S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs', []), idx_map)\n          S_noe = set()\n          try:\n              noe_list = kkt_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n              S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_list, None)\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n          results['topk_kkt']['entries'].append({\n              'tol': t, 'K': K,\n              'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n              'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n              'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n          })\n\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      out_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3_1_compare_v2_1.json')\n      with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\n      # Return baseline with tiny shrink\n      r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c0.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      return main()\n```"
thinking_content: "**Integrating new file analysis**\n\nI need to integrate the new file 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json' into my analysis. My plan is to use the \"Aggregator v2.1 ingestion\" script to process all contributions, including this new one. I'll provide code to parse metrics like boundary Jaccard and Top-K overlaps. Writing a robust aggregator might take a lot of effort, but I could create a lighter version aimed at processing this file specifically and compute the necessary metrics.\n\n**Understanding the schema requirements**\n\nI need to figure out the schema for 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json', which isn't provided but aligns with the previous v3.1 version. I'll design code to accommodate a generic schema that includes a 'boundary' list (with disc and side objects) and 'topk' list entries containing fields like method 'slack' and tolerance values that could be \"1e-9\" or \"1e−9.\" I’ll ensure the parser is robust enough to handle both string and float formats. Also,\
  \ I should return the baseline snapshot as before.\n\n**Implementing the code**\n\nI need to load 'noesis_internal_topk_audit.json' to access our slack pairs for specific tolerances and K values. For the boundary, I need to calculate it at tol=2e-8, which isn't in the internal audit. I can use the slacks function on my snapshot to identify boundary sides with slack values less than or equal to 2e-8 and create a set of 20 labeled contacts. I also need to compute Jaccard with these 20 entries, converting them to sets of (disc, side) strings. \n\nFor top-K Jaccard, I’ll find pairs from the external file based on the specified tolerances and K grid, focusing on method=\"slack\" and only the interior pairs.\n\n**Processing Appendix E contributions**\n\nFor the contributions in Appendix E, I’ll treat the lists as interior-only and compute the Jaccard similarity with our internal slack top-K for the specified tolerance and K values.\n\nIf there's an external method for KKT, I can compute overlaps\
  \ with our KKT top-K from 'noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit.json', but I'll skip that if it doesn't exist.\n\nNext, I'll map indices using the 'index_map_example.json' format to align their indices with ours, implementing a robust mapping function to ensure this is accurate. If the mapping isn't present, I'll assume the indices are identical.\n\nFor any external crossing flags, I can process those if they're available, but I’ll leave the robust_SAT_v2 part for now.\n\nFinally, I’ll write the JSON result to 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3_1_compare_v2_1.json' and update the consolidated summary in 'appendix_E_summary.json' as needed.\n\n**Simplifying the aggregator script**\n\nInterfering with the consolidated summary complicates things, so I might just write results without updating it, keeping the code simpler. Earlier, I was updating the summary, but it’s not strictly necessary; I can still produce research. \n\nI need to implement the aggregator script to ensure\
  \ it returns centers and radii while loading and shrinking snapshots. \n\nMy commands will include going to the research section, submitting the aggregation, and noting the new ingestion in the Archive and Public. I’ll also focus on the specific file 'quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json'.\n\nI will look for the 'index_map_to_noesis' within the same file while ensuring to parse tol values properly and handle the lists for boundary and top-K.\n\nFinally, I'll prepare to submit the aggregator script and note the ingestion later, but I know I might have to wait for the evaluation results, as it’s asynchronous. So, for now, I’ll just submit it."
