tick: 531
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 531\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nToken plan:\n- Use Token Management tools to prune nonessential logs and previews.\n- Keep: archive capsule #21 and addenda, SBRG logs (Evals 561, 563), manifest/README/tables.\n- Optional: compress long private capsule #1 by summarizing and pruning early drafting ticks if supported.\n- Maintain readiness; no new optimizations planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,796 / 270,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 233 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aggregator v2.1 refresh: scan shared/appxE_contribs and update consolidated summary (v1.1 schema)' (ID: 837) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 837\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed AttributeError by adding type checking for JSON data structures. The code now runs to completion with a score of 2.63.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code assumed all JSON files in `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/` would contain dictionary objects at the top level. However, some files contain arrays instead. When the code attempted to call `.get('index_map_to_noesis')` on a list object, it crashed with:\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nThis occurred in the `get_index_map()` function when processing files, which then propagated through `process_file()` → `load_contrib_boundary()` → `load_contrib_topk()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded defensive type checking in three key functions to handle both dict and non-dict JSON data:\n\n1. **`get_index_map(data)`** - Added check at\
    \ start:\n   ```python\n   if not isinstance(data, dict):\n       return None\n   ```\n\n2. **`load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map)`** - Added check:\n   ```python\n   if not isinstance(data, dict):\n       return set()\n   ```\n\n3. **`load_contrib_topk(data, method_key)`** - Added check:\n   ```python\n   if not isinstance(data, dict):\n       return []\n   ```\n\n4. **`process_file(fname, c0, r0, slack_audit, kkt_audit)`** - Added early validation:\n   ```python\n   if not isinstance(data, dict):\n       return {'file': fname, 'error': 'json_not_dict'}\n   ```\n\nThese changes allow the aggregator to gracefully skip or handle malformed JSON files while continuing to process valid contribution files.\n\n## Result\nThe submission completed successfully with a score of **2.63**, generating the consolidated summary file at `storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json` and creating a timestamped freeze in the freezes directory.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files\
    \ in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, json, time\nimport numpy as np\n\nN = 26\nSHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\nOUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results'\nSUMMARY_PATH = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json'\nFREEZE_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/freezes'\n\nNOESIS_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\nNOESIS_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\nAUDIT_SLACK = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_topk_audit.json'        # Eval 826\nAUDIT_KKT   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit.json'    # Eval 831\n\nK_GRID = [15, 25, 40, 60]\nTOLS = [1e-9, 1e-8]\nBOUNDARY_TOL = 2e-8\n\ndef load_snapshot():\n    if os.path.exists(NOESIS_C) and os.path.exists(NOESIS_R):\n        c = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_C, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n        r = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n        return c, r\n    centers\
    \ = []\n    radius = 0.08\n    for i in range(5):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if len(centers) < 26:\n                centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n    return np.array(centers, float), np.full(N, radius, float)\n\ndef slacks(c, r):\n    x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n    return x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r\n\ndef boundary_set(c, r, tol):\n    s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = slacks(c, r)\n    out = set()\n    for i in range(N):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'xL'))\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'xR'))\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'yB'))\n        if s_yT[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'yT'))\n    return out\n\ndef jaccard(A, B):\n    if not A and not B: return 1.0\n    if not A or not B: return 0.0\n    inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n    return inter/uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n\ndef load_json(path):\n    with open(path, 'r') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef norm_tol(t):\n    if isinstance(t, (int,float)): return float(t)\n    if isinstance(t,\
    \ str):\n        t = t.replace('−','-').strip()\n        try: return float(t)\n        except: return None\n    return None\n\ndef get_index_map(data):\n    # FIX: Handle case where data is a list instead of dict\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return None\n    im = data.get('index_map_to_noesis')\n    if isinstance(im, list) and len(im) == 26 and all(isinstance(x,int) for x in im):\n        return im\n    return None\n\ndef remap_pair(p, idx_map):\n    i, j = int(p[0]), int(p[1])\n    if idx_map is not None:\n        i, j = idx_map[i], idx_map[j]\n    if i == j: return None\n    if i > j: i, j = j, i\n    return (i, j)\n\ndef remap_boundary_entry(e, idx_map):\n    disc = int(e['disc']); side = str(e['side'])\n    if idx_map is not None:\n        disc = idx_map[disc]\n    return (disc, side)\n\ndef load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map):\n    # FIX: Handle case where data is not a dict\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return set()\n    b = data.get('boundary',\
    \ [])\n    S = set()\n    for e in b:\n        try: S.add(remap_boundary_entry(e, idx_map))\n        except: pass\n    return S\n\ndef pairs_to_set(pairs, idx_map):\n    S = set()\n    for p in pairs:\n        try:\n            q = remap_pair(p, idx_map)\n            if q is not None: S.add(q)\n        except: pass\n    return S\n\ndef load_contrib_topk(data, method_key):\n    # FIX: Handle case where data is not a dict\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return []\n    entries = []\n    if 'topk' in data and isinstance(data['topk'], list):\n        for ent in data['topk']:\n            m = str(ent.get('method','')).lower()\n            if (method_key == 'slack' and m.startswith('slack')) or \\\n               (method_key == 'kkt'   and m.startswith('kkt')):\n                entries.append(ent)\n    else:\n        if method_key == 'slack':\n            for key in list(data.keys()):\n                if key.startswith('slack_top_k_'):\n                    tol_str = key.replace('slack_top_k_','').replace('_','.')\n\
    \                    entries.append({'method':'slack','tol':tol_str,'K':len(data[key]),'pairs':data[key]})\n    return entries\n\ndef process_file(fname, c0, r0, slack_audit, kkt_audit):\n    path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, fname)\n    try:\n        data = load_json(path)\n    except Exception:\n        return {'file': fname, 'error': 'json_load_failed'}\n\n    # FIX: Handle case where JSON contains a list at top level\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return {'file': fname, 'error': 'json_not_dict'}\n\n    idx_map = get_index_map(data)\n\n    B_noe = boundary_set(c0, r0, tol=BOUNDARY_TOL)\n    B_contrib = load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map)\n    boundary = {\n        'tol': BOUNDARY_TOL,\n        'noesis_count': len(B_noe),\n        'contrib_count': len(B_contrib),\n        'jaccard': jaccard(B_noe, B_contrib)\n    }\n\n    entries_slack = []\n    if slack_audit:\n        for ent in load_contrib_topk(data, 'slack'):\n            t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n           \
    \ K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs',[]))))\n            if t in TOLS and K in K_GRID:\n                S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs',[]), idx_map)\n                try:\n                    noe_list = slack_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n                except Exception:\n                    noe_list = []\n                S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_list, None)\n                entries_slack.append({\n                    'tol': t, 'K': K,\n                    'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n                    'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n                    'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n                })\n\n    entries_kkt = []\n    if kkt_audit:\n        for ent in load_contrib_topk(data, 'kkt'):\n            t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n            K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs',[]))))\n            if t in TOLS and K in K_GRID:\n                S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs',[]), idx_map)\n                try:\n                  \
    \  noe_list = kkt_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n                except Exception:\n                    noe_list = []\n                S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_list, None)\n                entries_kkt.append({\n                    'tol': t, 'K': K,\n                    'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n                    'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n                    'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n                })\n\n    res = {\n        'file': fname,\n        'index_map_present': (get_index_map(data) is not None),\n        'boundary': boundary,\n        'topk_slack': {'entries': entries_slack},\n        'topk_kkt':   {'entries': entries_kkt},\n    }\n    return res\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    c0, r0 = load_snapshot()\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    files = [f for f in os.listdir(SHARED_DIR) if f.endswith('.json')]\n    # Load Noesis audits if present\n    slack_audit = load_json(AUDIT_SLACK) if os.path.exists(AUDIT_SLACK) else None\n    kkt_audit\
    \   = load_json(AUDIT_KKT)   if os.path.exists(AUDIT_KKT)   else None\n\n    results = []\n    for f in sorted(files):\n        # skip templates\n        if 'template' in f.lower() or f.endswith('_example.json'):\n            continue\n        # crossing-only files are handled in Gate v2 runs; include basic presence note\n        if 'crossing' in f.lower():\n            results.append({'file': f, 'note': 'crossings_only'})\n            continue\n        results.append(process_file(f, c0, r0, slack_audit, kkt_audit))\n\n    summary = {\n        'generated_at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime()),\n        'files_seen': len(files),\n        'processed': len(results),\n        'k_grid': K_GRID,\n        'tols': TOLS,\n        'boundary_tol': BOUNDARY_TOL,\n        'results': results\n    }\n    with open(SUMMARY_PATH, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n    os.makedirs(FREEZE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(os.path.join(FREEZE_DIR, f'appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_{summary[\"\
    generated_at\"]}.json'), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\n    r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n    return c0.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage list noesis/nmap` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list noesis/nmap/freezes` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n6. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File list for noesis/nmap will be displayed below.\n- File list for noesis/nmap/freezes will be displayed\
