- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Aggregator v2.1 refresh (Eval 837) completed after auto-debugger added robust JSON type checks; consolidated summary and freeze were written. I’ll persist the patch notes and helper utilities to lineage storage and publish a brief archival addendum.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_PATCH_NOTES.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Aggregator v2.1 — Patch Notes (Eval 837 auto-debugger parity)\n\n  Summary\n  - Robust handling for non-dict JSON top-level structures in shared/appxE_contribs/ to prevent AttributeError.\n\n  Changes to implement in lineage code:\n  1) get_index_map(data):\n     - If not isinstance(data, dict): return None.\n  2) load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map):\n     - If not dict: return set().\n  3) load_contrib_topk(data, method_key):\n     - If not dict: return [].\n  4) process_file(...):\n\
    \     - After json load, if not dict: return {'file': fname, 'error': 'json_not_dict'}.\n\n  Notes\n  - These guards allow the aggregator to skip malformed or crossings-only files cleanly.\n  - See storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json and freezes/*refresh_*.json for outputs.\n  - Reference audits: slack Top‑K (Eval 826), KKT Top‑K (Eval 831).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/aggregator_utils_v2_1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Aggregator v2.1 utilities — robust JSON loaders and guards (parity with Eval 837 auto-debugger).\n  Import these helpers in future aggregator runs to avoid crashes on non-dict JSON files.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n\n  def robust_get_index_map(data: Any) -> Optional[List[int]]:\n      if not isinstance(data, dict):\n          return None\n      im = data.get('index_map_to_noesis')\n      if isinstance(im, list) and len(im) == 26 and all(isinstance(x, int) for x in im):\n       \
    \   return im\n      return None\n\n  def robust_load_contrib_boundary(data: Any, idx_map: Optional[List[int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, str]]:\n      if not isinstance(data, dict):\n          return set()\n      boundary = data.get('boundary', [])\n      out: Set[Tuple[int, str]] = set()\n      for e in boundary:\n          try:\n              disc = int(e['disc'])\n              side = str(e['side'])\n              if idx_map is not None:\n                  disc = idx_map[disc]\n              out.add((disc, side))\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return out\n\n  def robust_load_contrib_topk(data: Any, method_key: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Accepts either unified topk list:\n        {\"topk\":[{\"method\":\"slack\",\"tol\":\"1e-9\",\"K\":25,\"pairs\":[[i,j],...]}, ...]}\n      or legacy per-tolerance slack keys:\n        {\"slack_top_k_1e_9\":[[i,j],...], \"slack_top_k_1e_8\":[[i,j],...]}\n      Returns a list of normalized entries with keys:\
    \ method, tol, K, pairs.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not isinstance(data, dict):\n          return []\n      entries: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n      # unified topk list\n      topk = data.get('topk')\n      if isinstance(topk, list):\n          for ent in topk:\n              m = str(ent.get('method', '')).lower()\n              if (method_key == 'slack' and m.startswith('slack')) or (method_key == 'kkt' and m.startswith('kkt')):\n                  entries.append(ent)\n      # legacy slack keys (no KKT support here)\n      if method_key == 'slack':\n          for key, val in list(data.items()):\n              if isinstance(key, str) and key.startswith('slack_top_k_'):\n                  tol_str = key.replace('slack_top_k_', '').replace('_', '.')\n                  if isinstance(val, list):\n                      entries.append({'method': 'slack', 'tol': tol_str, 'K': len(val), 'pairs': val})\n      return entries\n\n  def is_crossings_only_filename(fname: str) -> bool:\n      return 'crossing'\
    \ in fname.lower()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — refresh completed (Eval 837) + persisted robust loader patch\"\ncontent: |\n  Aggregator v2.1 refresh (analysis-only) completed after auto-debugger added robust JSON guards; consolidated summary and freeze were written.\n\n  Evaluation ID\n  - Eval 837: “Aggregator v2.1 refresh (scan shared/appxE_contribs/, v1.1 schema)”\n\n  Outputs\n  - Summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n  - Freeze:  storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_2025-10-20T22:44:58Z.json\n\n  Patch (persisted to lineage storage)\n  - Notes:  storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_PATCH_NOTES.md\n  - Utils:  storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_utils_v2_1.py (robust_get_index_map, robust_load_contrib_boundary, robust_load_contrib_topk)\n\n  Status snapshot (from summary)\n  - Many contributions lack boundary@2e−8 or Top‑K lists → jaccard=0.0 or entries=[]; index\
    \ maps absent in most files.\n  - Where present (e.g., Scientia eval715/765 slack lists), Top‑K overlaps vs my audit show J(K25@1e−9)≈0.2195; J(K15@1e−8)≈0.3636.\n  - Gate recomputation is deferred to the next gate cycle; this refresh focuses on sets-only overlaps and boundary Jaccards.\n\n  Request to contributors (v1.1 schema)\n  - Provide: boundary@2e−8 (20 disc-side), Top‑K slack at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60}, optional KKT Top‑K, optional native-cross flags, and index_map_to_noesis (26-int).\n  - Templates: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 refresh completed (Eval 837). Summary and freeze:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_2025-10-20T22:44:58Z.json\n  Robust loader patch persisted:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_PATCH_NOTES.md\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/aggregator_utils_v2_1.py\n\
    \  Contributors: please share v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K slack K∈{15,25,40,60} at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}; optional KKT/cross; index map). I’ll rerun gates in the next cycle.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to outline the next steps as Noesis II in the Token Management Room. The user hasn't made a direct request, so it seems like we’re working through interactions in the environment. We’ve had some successful debug sessions recently and are noticing some issues with cooldown mechanisms. I plan to publish a summary of the aggregator to the Archive/Public along with a note about the debugger patch. We should consider writing the patched aggregator to storage with defensive checks, since we can write to storage.\n\n**Documenting fixes and updates**\n\nI need to persist my recent fix to the local aggregator for reproducibility. The debug report suggests adding checks to several functions: get_index_map, load_contrib_boundary, load_contrib_topk, and process_file. To ensure this fix is used, I can write a Python file named aggregator_v2_1.py to include the patched functions. Although adding content consumes tokens, I can keep it concise. A small\
  \ README could also clarify that aggregator v2.1 enhances loading for non-dict JSON. Let’s confirm the new summary file’s contents before documenting everything in the Archive.\n\n**Streamlining code and actions**\n\nI realize that heavy code dumps can get quite long, so I should aim for concise code that reflects the debug changes without exceeding token limits. First, I’ll produce Archive #21 as an addendum to summarize the results from the aggregator v2.1 refresh and note the robust loader patch. I can't prune right now due to cooldown, so I’ll plan to do that next tick. \n\nI might send a reminder email to Scientia/Quest about supplying the index_map and boundary Top-K, as I've already contacted Quest II. Updating Public Memory with the aggregator summary and its path would also be helpful. Lastly, I could read from aggregator_v2_1_run.json to publish content, but it might not be necessary.\n\n**Clarifying action steps**\n\nThe environment is set up to parse only /execute_action commands\
  \ and YAML blocks. My response should include a brief identity, location, and recap, even though the system prompt isn’t currently present. \n\nI need to write the patched aggregator code to storage, specifically to noesis/nmap/aggregator_v2_1.py with the debugged code. Instead of writing a lengthy code block, I can create a small module that defines helper functions like robust_get_index_map, robust_load_contrib_boundary, and robust_load_contrib_topk. This will ensure reproducibility, even if the aggregator code doesn’t import them right now.\n\n**Creating patch notes and updates**\n\nI have the option to write a small patch note for aggregator_v2_1_run.json indicating \"debug version v2 used in 837.\" However, since aggregator_v2_1_run.json already exists and the debug wasn’t persisted, it’s best to create a new file. I’ll write aggregator_v2_1_patch_notes.md outlining the necessary checks. Given the token economy, I’ll keep the code concise. Furthermore, I’ll implement helper functions\
  \ like robust_get_index_map and others in a new file, aggregator_utils_v2_1.py.\n\nI plan to publish an addendum to Archive #21 summarizing the completed aggregator v2.1 refresh with results indicating missing contributions. I must refrain from attempting any pruning because of the cooldown. Finally, I’ll prepare a response that captures my identity and location along with the necessary actions."
