tick: 535
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Research Counter.\nRecap: Quest II provided a “complete” v3.1 sets-only file. I will run an incremental Aggregator v2.1 analysis-only refresh to integrate all current v1.1 files (including Quest II’s complete file), update the consolidated summary and freeze, and return the baseline pack.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregator v2.1 incremental refresh: integrate current v1.1 sets-only files (incl. Quest II v3.1 complete)\"\ntags: \"analysis-only, reproducibility, sets-only, appendix-E, aggregator\"\nabstract: \"Processes all JSON files under shared/appxE_contribs with schema v1.1 guards; integrates boundary@2e−8 and Top‑K slack/KKT vs internal audits (Evals 826, 831). Writes per-file results, consolidated summary_v2_1.json, and a timestamped freeze. Returns the Noesis baseline with 1e−9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time, sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Import\
    \ robust helpers persisted earlier\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/nmap')\n  try:\n      from aggregator_utils_v2_1 import (\n          robust_get_index_map, robust_load_contrib_boundary,\n          robust_load_contrib_topk, is_crossings_only_filename\n      )\n  except Exception:\n      # Minimal fallbacks if helper module not found\n      def robust_get_index_map(data): \n          return data.get('index_map_to_noesis') if isinstance(data, dict) else None\n      def robust_load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map):\n          if not isinstance(data, dict): return set()\n          out = set()\n          for e in data.get('boundary', []):\n              try:\n                  d = int(e['disc']); s = str(e['side'])\n                  if idx_map: d = idx_map[d]\n                  out.add((d, s))\n              except Exception: pass\n          return out\n      def robust_load_contrib_topk(data, method_key):\n          if not isinstance(data, dict): return []\n          ents = []\n    \
    \      tk = data.get('topk')\n          if isinstance(tk, list):\n              for ent in tk:\n                  m = str(ent.get('method','')).lower()\n                  if (method_key=='slack' and m.startswith('slack')) or (method_key=='kkt' and m.startswith('kkt')):\n                      ents.append(ent)\n          if method_key=='slack':\n              for k,v in list(data.items()):\n                  if isinstance(k,str) and k.startswith('slack_top_k_') and isinstance(v,list):\n                      ents.append({'method':'slack','tol':k.replace('slack_top_k_','').replace('_','.'),'K':len(v),'pairs':v})\n          return ents\n      def is_crossings_only_filename(fname): return 'crossing' in fname.lower()\n\n  # Constants and paths\n  N = 26\n  SHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  OUT_DIR    = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results'\n  SUM_PATH   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json'\n  FREEZE_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/freezes'\n  AUDIT_SLACK = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_topk_audit.json'\
    \   # Eval 826\n  AUDIT_KKT   = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results/noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit.json' # Eval 831\n  NOESIS_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  NOESIS_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\n  K_GRID = [15, 25, 40, 60]\n  TOLS = [1e-9, 1e-8]\n  BOUND_TOL = 2e-8\n\n  def load_json(path):\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def norm_tol(t):\n      if isinstance(t,(int,float)): return float(t)\n      if isinstance(t,str):\n          t = t.replace('−','-').strip()\n          try: return float(t)\n          except: return None\n      return None\n\n  def slacks(c, r):\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      return x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r\n\n  def boundary_set(c, r, tol):\n      s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = slacks(c, r)\n      out = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          if s_xL[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'xL'))\n          if s_xR[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'xR'))\n          if s_yB[i] <= tol: out.add((i,'yB'))\n          if s_yT[i] <=\
    \ tol: out.add((i,'yT'))\n      return out\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      if not A and not B: return 1.0\n      if not A or not B: return 0.0\n      inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n      return inter/uni if uni>0 else 1.0\n\n  def pairs_to_set(pairs, idx_map):\n      S = set()\n      for p in pairs:\n          try:\n              i, j = int(p[0]), int(p[1])\n              if idx_map: i, j = idx_map[i], idx_map[j]\n              if i==j: continue\n              if i>j: i, j = j, i\n              S.add((i,j))\n          except Exception: pass\n      return S\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(NOESIS_C) and os.path.exists(NOESIS_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(NOESIS_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      # conservative fallback\n      centers = []\n      radius = 0.08\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < N:\n                  centers.append([0.1+0.2*i,\
    \ 0.1+0.15*j])\n      return np.array(centers,float), np.full(N, radius, float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c0, r0 = load_snapshot()\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      os.makedirs(FREEZE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Load audits if present\n      slack_audit = load_json(AUDIT_SLACK) if os.path.exists(AUDIT_SLACK) else None\n      kkt_audit   = load_json(AUDIT_KKT)   if os.path.exists(AUDIT_KKT)   else None\n\n      B_noe = boundary_set(c0, r0, tol=BOUND_TOL)\n      files = sorted([f for f in os.listdir(SHARED_DIR) if f.endswith('.json')])\n      results = []\n      eligible_entries = 0\n\n      for fname in files:\n          if 'template' in fname.lower() or fname.endswith('_example.json'):\n              continue\n          if is_crossings_only_filename(fname):\n              results.append({'file': fname, 'note': 'crossings_only'})\n              continue\n          path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, fname)\n          try:\n              data = load_json(path)\n\
    \          except Exception:\n              results.append({'file': fname, 'error': 'json_load_failed'})\n              continue\n          if not isinstance(data, dict):\n              results.append({'file': fname, 'error': 'json_not_dict'})\n              continue\n\n          idx_map = robust_get_index_map(data)\n\n          # Boundary compare\n          B_contrib = robust_load_contrib_boundary(data, idx_map)\n          boundary = {\n              'tol': BOUND_TOL,\n              'noesis_count': len(B_noe),\n              'contrib_count': len(B_contrib),\n              'jaccard': jaccard(B_noe, B_contrib)\n          }\n\n          # Top-K comparisons\n          entries_slack = []\n          if slack_audit:\n              for ent in robust_load_contrib_topk(data, 'slack'):\n                  t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n                  K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs',[]))))\n                  if t in TOLS and K in K_GRID:\n                      S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs',[]),\
    \ idx_map)\n                      try:\n                          noe_pairs = slack_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n                      except Exception:\n                          noe_pairs = []\n                      S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_pairs, None)\n                      entries_slack.append({\n                          'tol': t, 'K': K,\n                          'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n                          'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n                          'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n                      })\n\n          entries_kkt = []\n          if kkt_audit:\n              for ent in robust_load_contrib_topk(data, 'kkt'):\n                  t = norm_tol(ent.get('tol'))\n                  K = int(ent.get('K', len(ent.get('pairs',[]))))\n                  if t in TOLS and K in K_GRID:\n                      S_contrib = pairs_to_set(ent.get('pairs',[]), idx_map)\n                      try:\n                          noe_pairs = kkt_audit['topk_pairs'][str(t)][str(K)]\n\
    \                      except Exception:\n                          noe_pairs = []\n                      S_noe = pairs_to_set(noe_pairs, None)\n                      entries_kkt.append({\n                          'tol': t, 'K': K,\n                          'contrib_size': len(S_contrib),\n                          'noesis_size': len(S_noe),\n                          'jaccard': jaccard(S_noe, S_contrib)\n                      })\n\n          # Eligibility (v2.1): boundary complete AND slack lists include at least (tol,K) in {(1e-9,25),(1e-8,15)}\n          have_1e9_25 = any(e['tol']==1e-9 and e['K']==25 for e in entries_slack)\n          have_1e8_15 = any(e['tol']==1e-8 and e['K']==15 for e in entries_slack)\n          eligible = (boundary['contrib_count']==20) and have_1e9_25 and have_1e8_15\n          if eligible: eligible_entries += 1\n\n          results.append({\n              'file': fname,\n              'index_map_present': (idx_map is not None),\n              'boundary':\
    \ boundary,\n              'topk_slack': {'entries': entries_slack},\n              'topk_kkt': {'entries': entries_kkt},\n              'eligible_v2_1': eligible\n          })\n\n      summary = {\n          'status': 'ok',\n          'schema_version': '1.1',\n          'aggregator_version': '2.1',\n          'files_seen': len(files),\n          'stems_processed': len(results),\n          'eligible_entries': eligible_entries,\n          'generated_at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime()),\n          'k_grid': K_GRID,\n          'tols': TOLS,\n          'boundary_tol': BOUND_TOL,\n          'results': results\n      }\n      with open(SUM_PATH, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n      with open(os.path.join(FREEZE_DIR, f'appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_{summary[\"generated_at\"]}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\n      # Return Noesis baseline with tiny shrink\n      r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c0.astype(float),\
    \ r.astype(float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering code integration**\n\nI need to be cautious about including too much code since the previous aggregator was over 300 lines. I'm thinking of using an “incremental integration” approach that reads from quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1_complete.json and generates a results JSON. Ideally, I want to re-run aggregator_v2_1 for updates, while keeping things concise. Also, I’ll integrate functions from aggregator_utils_v2_1 if it's available. Let’s focus on manageable code length while still being robust!\n\n**Outlining the code structure**\n\nI need to set up some constants and load the snapshot first. Next, I'll implement helper functions like jaccard and norm tolerance, along with pairs_to_set for processing.\n\nFor each JSON file in shared/appxE_contribs, I'll skip templates and crossing-only entries but may include notes. I'll load JSON, checking for errors if it's not a dictionary.\n\nThen, I'll compute boundaries and gather top k slack and contributions using robust\
  \ functions. Based on specific criteria like boundary counts and slack entries, I'll define 'eligible' entries and save results along with a timestamp in 'appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json'.\n\n**Planning post-submission actions**\n\nI’ll start by returning the baseline pack. After submitting the code, I should follow up with an addendum update for Archive 21 and possibly Public memory. The platform suggests posting updates after evaluation, but I can plan to do so once the evaluation is complete.\n\nCurrently, I need to craft commands for submission. We might propose submitting the incremental aggregator with a command like \"submit 1.\" I could also update the status note in the archive, noting that results will be available post-evaluation. I might queue a \"goto archive\" response to keep things moving while ensuring we follow the typical posting protocol after evaluation.\n\n**Setting up commands**\n\nFirst, I need to set up a couple of commands. I will use \"goto research\" and then submit\
  \ the incremental aggregator code. I could consider filtering tags for analysis-only and set the page size to 20, but I'll keep verbosity minimal since the guidelines suggest being concise. \n\nI’ll ensure the YAML used after submission has the correct indentation to avoid issues with extra dashes. We'll craft the code, importing aggregator utilities to keep it streamlined. I’ll define constants, load snapshots, and construct the results while checking eligibility based on specific conditions.\n\n**Finalizing submission process**\n\nI’ll compute the coverage set and summarize the eligible entries count accordingly. Then, I need to write this to the summary path and finalize the data. \n\nAfter that, I’ll return the baseline and double-check that everything is manageable in size. Finally, I'll prepare the message with the command to “submit 1” along with the associated code. It's important to make sure everything is clear and concise for the user!"
