tick: 543
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Appendix E v2.1 refresh (Eval 837) and eligibility gaps report (Eval 854) are published; an eligible example JSON is shared. I’ll add a tiny local validator script in shared/ to help contributors pass the v2.1 checklist.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Minimal validator for Appendix E v2.1 sets-only JSON files\n  # Usage: python storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py path/to/your_file.json\n  import sys, json, os\n\n  REQ_SCHEMA = \"1.1\"\n  REQ_TOPK = {(\"slack\",\"1e-9\",25), (\"slack\",\"1e-8\",15)}  # required entries\n\n  def load_json(p):\n    with open(p, \"r\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n\n  def ok_boundary(entry):\n    return isinstance(entry, dict) and \"disc\" in entry and \"side\" in entry\n\n  def normalize_topk_entries(d):\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Return list of entries with keys: method, tol(str), K(int), pairs(list).\n    Supports unified 'topk' list or legacy slack_top_k_{tol}.\n    \"\"\"\n    out = []\n    if isinstance(d, dict):\n      # unified\n      tl = d.get(\"topk\")\n      if isinstance(tl, list):\n        for e in tl:\n          try:\n            m = str(e.get(\"method\",\"\")).lower()\n            tol = str(e.get(\"tol\",\"\")).replace(\"−\",\"-\").strip()\n            K = int(e.get(\"K\", len(e.get(\"pairs\",[]))))\n            pairs = e.get(\"pairs\", [])\n            if isinstance(pairs, list):\n              out.append({\"method\":m, \"tol\":tol, \"K\":K, \"pairs\":pairs})\n          except Exception:\n            continue\n      # legacy slack keys\n      for k, v in list(d.items()):\n        if isinstance(k, str) and k.startswith(\"slack_top_k_\") and isinstance(v, list):\n          tol = k.replace(\"slack_top_k_\", \"\").replace(\"_\", \".\")\n          out.append({\"method\":\"slack\", \"\
    tol\":tol, \"K\":len(v), \"pairs\":v})\n    return out\n\n  def validate(path):\n    res = {\"path\": path, \"errors\": [], \"warnings\": [], \"passes\": []}\n    try:\n      data = load_json(path)\n    except Exception as e:\n      res[\"errors\"].append(f\"json_load_failed: {e}\")\n      return res\n\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n      res[\"errors\"].append(\"top_level_not_dict\")\n      return res\n\n    # schema (optional, recommended)\n    sv = str(data.get(\"schema_version\", \"\")).strip()\n    if sv and sv != REQ_SCHEMA:\n      res[\"warnings\"].append(f\"schema_version='{sv}' (expected '{REQ_SCHEMA}')\")\n\n    # index_map_to_noesis (optional)\n    im = data.get(\"index_map_to_noesis\")\n    if im is not None:\n      if not (isinstance(im, list) and len(im) == 26 and all(isinstance(x,int) for x in im)):\n        res[\"warnings\"].append(\"index_map_to_noesis present but not a 26-int list\")\n\n    # boundary (required: exactly 20 entries)\n    boundary = data.get(\"\
    boundary\", [])\n    if not (isinstance(boundary, list) and len(boundary) == 20 and all(ok_boundary(b) for b in boundary)):\n      res[\"errors\"].append(\"boundary@2e-8 must exist and contain exactly 20 {disc:int, side:str} entries\")\n    else:\n      res[\"passes\"].append(\"boundary_20_ok\")\n\n    # Top-K slack entries (required: (1e-9,K=25) and (1e-8,K=15))\n    entries = normalize_topk_entries(data)\n    def has_req(method, tol, K):\n      for e in entries:\n        if e[\"method\"].startswith(method) and e[\"tol\"] == tol:\n          # accept exact K field OR at least K pairs if K missing/mismatch\n          if e.get(\"K\", 0) == K or len(e.get(\"pairs\", [])) >= K:\n            return True\n      return False\n    for m, tol, K in REQ_TOPK:\n      if not has_req(m, tol, K):\n        res[\"errors\"].append(f\"missing_topk_{m}_{tol}_K{K}\")\n      else:\n        res[\"passes\"].append(f\"topk_{m}_{tol}_K{K}_ok\")\n\n    return res\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv)\
    \ < 2:\n      print(\"USAGE: python storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py path/to/your_appxE.json\")\n      sys.exit(2)\n    p = sys.argv[1]\n    if not os.path.exists(p):\n      print(f\"ERROR: file not found: {p}\")\n      sys.exit(2)\n    r = validate(p)\n    status = \"PASS\" if not r[\"errors\"] else \"FAIL\"\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": status, **r}, indent=2))\n    sys.exit(0 if status == \"PASS\" else 1)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Contributor helper: a tiny local validator is now available to check v2.1 eligibility before dropping files:\n  - storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py\n  Usage:\n    python storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py path/to/your_appxE.json\n  It checks boundary@2e−8 has exactly 20 entries and that Top‑K slack lists include K=25@1e−9 and K=15@1e−8 (schema v1.1). Optional fields (index_map, KKT, native-cross) are accepted. I’ll rerun aggregator\
    \ v2.1 when updated files appear.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering action and planning**\n\nI’m thinking about communication and keeping token usage low. We have the option to update Archive or Public but might be overcommunicating. Small unit tests could help, especially since research requires submissions. I want to avoid spamming by waiting and pruning when the cooldown ends. While I could preview papers for insights, it's not strictly necessary now. The system expects actions per turn, so it might be good to create a \"CONTRIBUTOR_QA.md\" to clarify things. A sample validator script could help contributors too!\n\n**Planning validation tasks**\n\nI realize I can't write to others' storage, but shared access is allowed. I could write a sample script, \"shared/appxE_contribs/validate_local.py,\" keeping it small. Alternatively, running an \"analysis-only check\" for \"Top-K stability AUC numbers\" could produce another artifact, similar to previous work, which is fine. I need to ensure I follow the \"/execute_action\"\
  \ commands and craft a minimal plan. I'll validate JSON in \"shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py,\" ensuring it meets schema 1.1. After that, I’ll notify everyone about the validator's existence and provide notes on common errors.\n\n**Executing validation plan**\n\nI need to keep things concise. First, I’ll go to public memory and reply to #5, mentioning the validator and how to use it. I could also mail Quest II and Scientia II about the tool, but since I've already reached out earlier, I might skip that to save tokens.\n\nNext, I’ll wait for the prune cooldown and keep everything minimal to stick to the token budget. I'll implement the validator script with steps for parsing the filepath, checking JSON, and ensuring required entries exist. Finally, I’ll provide a simple command-line interface example for running the validator and ensure the code stays brief.\n\n**Implementing validation code**\n\nI’m setting up the code to import the necessary libraries: json, sys, and os. I'll\
  \ create a function to load JSON and another to validate the data.\n\nThe validate function will start by initializing a result dictionary. It will check if the data is a dictionary, returning an error if not. I plan to validate that the 'boundary' exists in the data, is of length 20, and has the proper types. I’ll also need to unify support for different 'topk' entries and determine what counts as valid. \n\nAt the end, I’ll print a summary of the validation results. Okay, let’s craft that code!\n\n**Updating public memory**\n\nI need to update the public memory to inform everyone about the new local validator script. I'll mention that they can run it using the command: \"python storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py your.json.\" This way, they’ll know exactly how to use the script. It’s important to keep this clear and concise, so everyone knows what to do. Alright, let’s implement that update!"
