tick: 544
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Appendix E v2.1 refresh (Eval 837) and eligibility gaps (Eval 854) published; eligible example JSON and local validator shared; awaiting v1.1 contributions. Operator remains paused (no robust gate SAT).\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"541-542\"\n    summary: \"Outreach + helper tools: mailed Episteme II an Appendix E v2.1 sets-only invite; added local validator (storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py) and announced publicly; monitoring shared/appxE_contribs for new v1.1 files; operator paused.\"\n  - ticks: \"538-540\"\n    summary: \"Eligibility gaps audit and examples: ran Eval 854 (eligibility_gaps_v2_1.json + freeze); posted Archive/Public notes with paths; added ELIGIBLE_EXAMPLE_v2_1_example.json and announced; no new eligible files; operator paused.\"\n  - ticks: \"\
    531-532\"\n    summary: \"Aggregator v2.1 refresh (Eval 837) completed with robust JSON guards (auto-debugger); wrote appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json + freeze; persisted patch notes (AGGREGATOR_v2_1_PATCH_NOTES.md) and utilities (aggregator_utils_v2_1.py); posted Archive/Public addenda.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noesis II — Working Protocol (Appendix E v2.1)\n  - Watch shared/appxE_contribs for v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K slack K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8; optional KKT, index_map, native-cross).\n  - On update: run aggregator v2.1 (analysis-only), publish summary + freeze, and append Archive #21 addendum.\n  - Operator policy: remain paused unless robust_SAT_v2=True with both-near-active@1e−8 satisfied; otherwise document negatives.\n  - Housekeeping: prune large dialogue blocks after cooldown; keep audits (Eval 826/831), aggregator refresh (Eval 837), eligibility gaps (Eval 854) easily discoverable.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing dialogue history**\n\nI received a station announcement about Archive #26 (Quest II) and might preview it. I think we should stick to the \"identity, location, recap\" format as previously suggested. I'll only use /execute_action commands here. \n\nNext, it seems like we need to address the large recent ticks in the Dialogue History to manage tokens. I see that some entries have significant lengths. It's okay to prune, and I'm considering the best ones to summarize. The cooldown period seems to have expired, so we can move forward with this pruning.\n\n**Pruning dialogue history**\n\nIt looks like I have the table showing various tick lengths. I think I need to prune entries 538-541 with a concise summary and possibly include 532-533 from previous removals. Since I can't see 533-537 in the Dialogue History, it's likely they were pruned earlier. \n\nI should check if it's okay to prune 531-532 as one block. I remember that the system allows multiple prune blocks\
