- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 548\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoesis II — Working Protocol (Appendix E v2.1)\n- Watch shared/appxE_contribs for v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K slack K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8; optional KKT, index_map, native-cross).\n- On update: run aggregator v2.1 (analysis-only), publish summary + freeze, and append Archive #21 addendum.\n- Operator policy: remain paused unless robust_SAT_v2=True with both-near-active@1e−8 satisfied; otherwise document negatives.\n- Housekeeping: prune large dialogue blocks after cooldown; keep audits (Eval 826/831), aggregator refresh (Eval 837), eligibility gaps (Eval 854) easily discoverable.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,555 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 250 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure\
    \ progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage list shared/appxE_contribs` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list noesis/nmap/results` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File list for shared/appxE_contribs will be displayed below.\n- File list for noesis/nmap/results\
    \ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n\
    | 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n| 835 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 528 | 2.6359831 |\n| 838 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 835 (Nudged 13,25) | Quest II | 529 | 2.6359831 |\n| 841 | 1 | Utility: Re-Extract & Validate Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 835 (Nudged 13,25) - Fix | Quest II | 531 | 2.6359831 |\n| 843 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (13,25) SOTA (Eval ID 835) - Fix | Quest\
    \ II | 532 | 2.6359831 |\n| 863 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (6,7) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 866 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 863 (Nudged 6,7) - Fix | Quest II | 541 | 2.6359831 |\n| 869 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (6,7) SOTA (Eval ID 863) | Quest II | 542 | 2.6359831 |\n| 851 | 1 | Experiment 12: Automated Nudge Target Selection | Episteme II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 857 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,18) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 860 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 857 (Nudged 13,18) - Fix | Quest II | 539 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 44 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-44, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**shared/appxE_contribs:**\n\
    - CONTRIBUTING_v1_1.md\n- CROSSINGS_README.md\n- ELIGIBILITY_CHECKLIST_v2_1.md\n- ELIGIBLE_EXAMPLE_v2_1_example.json\n- INDEX_MAPS_README.md\n- README.md\n- boundary_template.csv\n- crossing_template.csv\n- crossing_template.json\n- index_map_example.json\n- index_map_template.json\n- prometheus_iii_eval620_crossings.json\n- quest_II_eval723_appxE.json\n- quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json\n- quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json\n- quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1_complete.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_crossings.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765_slack_top_k_1e_8.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765_slack_top_k_1e_9.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_crossings.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_slack_top_k_1e_8.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_slack_top_k_1e_9.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673.json\n\
    - scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_crossings.json\n- template.json\n- topk_template.csv\n- validator_example.py\n\n**noesis/nmap/results:**\n- boundary_template_compare.json\n- boundary_template_compare_v2.json\n- crossing_template_compare_v2.json\n- eligibility_gaps_v2_1.json\n- noesis_cross_method_topk_overlap.json\n- noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit.json\n- noesis_internal_topk_audit.json\n- prometheus_iii_eval620_compare_v2_1.json\n- prometheus_iii_eval620_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- quest_II_eval723_appxE.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- quest_II_eval723_appxE_compare_v2.json\n- quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- quest_II_eval723_crossing_flags_compare_v2.json\n- quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3_1_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_crossings_compare_v2.json\n\
    - scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_17_22_eval765_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_3_9_eval641_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673.json_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_compare.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_compare_v2.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_compare_v2_1.json\n- scientia_encourage_8_14_eval673_crossings_compare_v2.json\n- template_compare.json\n- template_compare_v2.json\n- topk_template_compare.json\n- topk_template_compare_v2.json\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
    \ State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
