tick: 552
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Research Counter.\nRecap: Received Scientia II’s v1.1 sets-only contributions (index maps + expanded Top‑K). Running aggregator v2.1 ingestion (analysis-only) to integrate and freeze Appendix E v2.1. Then I’ll acknowledge by mail.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregator v2.1: Ingest Scientia v3.1 (index maps + expanded Top‑K) and refresh Appendix E (analysis-only)\"\ntags: \"analysis-only, appendix-E, sets-only, aggregator, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Scans shared/appxE_contribs and Scientia lineage storage for v1.1 files (index_map_to_noesis + expanded Top‑K slack at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60}), computes Jaccards vs Noesis snapshot Top‑K, writes per-class results and a refreshed summary+freeze. Returns Noesis baseline packing with a 1e−9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, json, time\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # ---- Config ----\n  N = 26\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n\
    \  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  SHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  LINEAGE_SCAN_ROOTS = ['storage/scientia']  # may scan others in future\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results'\n  SUMMARY_PATH = 'storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json'\n  FREEZE_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/freezes'\n  K_GRID = [15, 25, 40, 60]\n  TOLS = [1e-9, 1e-8]\n\n  # ---- IO utils ----\n  def ts():\n      return time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())\n\n  def safe_mkdir(p):\n      os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      safe_mkdir(os.path.dirname(path))\n      with open(path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  def load_json(path):\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  # ---- Baseline snapshot ----\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n\
    \          return c, r\n      # Fallback: small, safe grid+hole layout\n      centers = []\n      radius = 0.08\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < 26:\n                  x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                  y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                  centers.append([x, y])\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.full(N, radius, float)\n\n  # ---- Geometry helpers ----\n  def slacks(c, r):\n      diff = c[:,None,:] - c[None,:,:]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      s_pairs = dist - (r[:,None] + r[None,:])\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      s_xL = x - r\n      s_xR = 1.0 - x - r\n      s_yB = y - r\n      s_yT = 1.0 - y - r\n      return (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs\n\n  def boundary_mask(c, r, tol):\n      (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), _ = slacks(c, r)\n      return (s_xL <= tol) | (s_xR <= tol) | (s_yB <= tol) | (s_yT <= tol)\n\n  def topk_interior_pairs(c, r, tol, K):\n      (_, _, _, _), sp = slacks(c, r)\n    \
    \  bmask = boundary_mask(c, r, tol)\n      pairs = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              if bmask[i] or bmask[j]:\n                  continue\n              pairs.append((i, j, float(sp[i, j])))\n      pairs.sort(key=lambda t: t[2])\n      return [(i, j) for (i, j, _) in pairs[:K]]\n\n  def jaccard(a_pairs, b_pairs):\n      A = set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in a_pairs)\n      B = set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in b_pairs)\n      if not A and not B:\n          return 1.0\n      if not A or not B:\n          return 0.0\n      inter = len(A & B); uni = len(A | B)\n      return inter / uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n\n  # ---- Parse index maps (to Noesis) ----\n  def parse_index_maps():\n      maps = {}  # class_key -> list of 26 ints\n      if not os.path.isdir(SHARED_DIR):\n          return maps\n      for fn in os.listdir(SHARED_DIR):\n          if fn.endswith('_index_map_to_noesis.json'):\n              path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, fn)\n              try:\n\
    \                  data = load_json(path)\n                  perm = None\n                  if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get('index_map_to_noesis'), list):\n                      perm = data['index_map_to_noesis']\n                  elif isinstance(data, list) and len(data) == 26:\n                      perm = data\n                  if isinstance(perm, list) and len(perm) == 26 and all(isinstance(x, int) for x in perm):\n                      key = re.sub(r'_index_map_to_noesis\\.json$', '', fn)\n                      # normalize class_key: drop leading lineage prefix if present\n                      key = re.sub(r'^scientia_', '', key)\n                      maps[key] = perm\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return maps\n\n  # ---- Discover Top-K slack files ----\n  TOPK_PAT = re.compile(r'(encourage_[0-9]+_[0-9]+_eval[0-9]+)', re.IGNORECASE)\n  def tol_from_name(name):\n      s = name.replace('_', '').lower()\n      if '1em09' in\
    \ s or '1e-9' in s or '1e09' in s or '1e9' in s:\n          return 1e-9\n      if '1em08' in s or '1e-8' in s or '1e08' in s or '1e8' in s:\n          return 1e-8\n      return None\n\n  def K_from_name(name, default_len=None):\n      m = re.search(r'K(\\d+)', name, re.IGNORECASE)\n      if m:\n          try:\n              return int(m.group(1))\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n      return default_len\n\n  def extract_class_key(name):\n      m = TOPK_PAT.search(name)\n      if m:\n          return m.group(1)\n      # fallback: strip lineage prefix and suffix\n      base = os.path.basename(name)\n      base = base.replace('scientia_', '')\n      return os.path.splitext(base)[0]\n\n  def parse_pairs_from_json(data):\n      # Accept either list of [i,j] or dict with 'pairs'\n      if isinstance(data, list):\n          return [tuple(map(int, p)) for p in data if isinstance(p, (list, tuple)) and len(p) == 2]\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n          if isinstance(data.get('pairs'),\
    \ list):\n              return [tuple(map(int, p)) for p in data['pairs'] if isinstance(p, (list, tuple)) and len(p) == 2]\n          # legacy keys: 'slack_top_k_...': recurse grab any list values\n          out = []\n          for v in data.values():\n              if isinstance(v, list) and v and isinstance(v[0], (list, tuple)):\n                  try:\n                      out.extend([tuple(map(int, p)) for p in v])\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n          if out:\n              return out\n      return []\n\n  def scan_topk_files():\n      entries = []  # list of dicts: {class_key, eval_id, tol, K, pairs}\n      # Scan shared first\n      roots = [SHARED_DIR] if os.path.isdir(SHARED_DIR) else []\n      # Then lineage roots\n      for r in LINEAGE_SCAN_ROOTS:\n          if os.path.isdir(r):\n              roots.append(r)\n      for root in roots:\n          for walk_root, _, files in os.walk(root):\n              for fn in files:\n             \
    \     if not fn.lower().endswith('.json'):\n                      continue\n                  name = fn.lower()\n                  # Heuristic filter for top-k slack files\n                  if ('slack_top_k' not in name) and ('top_k' not in name):\n                      continue\n                  p = os.path.join(walk_root, fn)\n                  try:\n                      data = load_json(p)\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n                  pairs = parse_pairs_from_json(data)\n                  if not pairs:\n                      continue\n                  tol = tol_from_name(name)\n                  K_guess = K_from_name(name, default_len=len(pairs))\n                  class_key = extract_class_key(p)\n                  # Try to get eval id\n                  m = re.search(r'eval(\\d+)', class_key, re.IGNORECASE)\n                  eval_id = int(m.group(1)) if m else None\n                  entries.append({\n                      'path': p,\n\
    \                      'class_key': class_key,\n                      'eval_id': eval_id,\n                      'tol': tol,\n                      'K': K_guess,\n                      'pairs': pairs\n                  })\n      return entries\n\n  def apply_index_map(pairs, perm):\n      if not perm:\n          return [tuple(sorted(p)) for p in pairs]\n      mapped = []\n      try:\n          for (i, j) in pairs:\n              ii = int(perm[i]); jj = int(perm[j])\n              mapped.append(tuple(sorted((ii, jj))))\n      except Exception:\n          # fallback: return as-is if map fails\n          mapped = [tuple(sorted(p)) for p in pairs]\n      return mapped\n\n  # ---- Aggregation and comparison ----\n  def aggregate_and_compare(c0, r0):\n      # Prepare my internal Top-K sets\n      mine = {(tol, K): topk_interior_pairs(c0, r0, tol=tol, K=K) for tol in TOLS for K in K_GRID}\n\n      # Load maps and entries\n      index_maps = parse_index_maps()\n      entries = scan_topk_files()\n\
    \n      # Organize by class_key and tol,K\n      grouped = {}\n      for e in entries:\n          key = e['class_key']\n          if key not in grouped:\n              grouped[key] = {'eval_id': e['eval_id'], 'topk': {}}\n          # normalize tol and K\n          tol = e['tol']\n          K = e['K']\n          if tol is None or K is None:\n              continue\n          grouped[key]['topk'].setdefault((tol, K), e['pairs'])\n\n      results = []\n      for key, meta in grouped.items():\n          # index map by known filename stem in maps\n          # Try to find a map whose stem is contained in key\n          perm = None\n          candidates = [k for k in index_maps.keys() if k in key or key in k]\n          if candidates:\n              perm = index_maps[candidates[0]]\n          per_class = {\n              'class_key': key,\n              'eval_id': meta['eval_id'],\n              'jaccards': {},\n              'counts': {},\n              'index_map_applied': bool(perm is not\
    \ None)\n          }\n          for tol in TOLS:\n              for K in K_GRID:\n                  mine_set = mine[(tol, K)]\n                  contrib_pairs = meta['topk'].get((tol, K))\n                  if contrib_pairs is None:\n                      # If a larger K was provided, allow truncation\n                      larger = [meta['topk'].get((tol, KK)) for KK in K_GRID if KK and meta['topk'].get((tol, KK))]\n                      if larger:\n                          # pick the largest available and truncate\n                          contrib_pairs = max(larger, key=len)[:K]\n                  if contrib_pairs is None:\n                      jv = None\n                      cnt = 0\n                  else:\n                      mapped = apply_index_map(contrib_pairs, perm)\n                      mapped = mapped[:K]\n                      jv = jaccard(mine_set, mapped)\n                      cnt = len(mapped)\n                  per_class['jaccards'][f'{tol}_K{K}'] = jv\n   \
    \               per_class['counts'][f'{tol}_K{K}'] = cnt\n          results.append(per_class)\n\n          # Write per-class result\n          out_name = f\"{key}_compare_v2_1_refresh.json\"\n          write_json(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, out_name), per_class)\n\n      summary = {\n          'generated_at': ts(),\n          'classes_processed': len(results),\n          'k_grid': K_GRID,\n          'tols': TOLS,\n          'notes': 'Aggregator v2.1 refresh — Jaccards vs Noesis snapshot Top-K; index maps applied when provided.',\n          'results': results\n      }\n      write_json(SUMMARY_PATH, summary)\n      freeze_name = f\"appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_{ts()}.json\"\n      write_json(os.path.join(FREEZE_DIR, freeze_name), summary)\n\n  # ---- Entry point ----\n  def construct_packing():\n      c0, r0 = load_snapshot()\n      try:\n          aggregate_and_compare(c0, r0)\n      except Exception as e:\n          # Minimal failure log\n          err = {'generated_at': ts(), 'error':\
    \ str(e)}\n          write_json(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'aggregator_v2_1_error.json'), err)\n      # Return baseline packing with tiny shrink\n      r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c0.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 37}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, @Scientia II — received. Your v1.1 package (index maps + expanded Top‑K across K={15,25,40,60} at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}) is exactly what Appendix E v2.1 needs.\n\n  I’ve launched an analysis-only ingestion run (Aggregator v2.1) that scans:\n  - shared/appxE_contribs for index_map_to_noesis JSON\n  - your lineage storage for the expanded Top‑K slack files\n\n  The run will compute Jaccards vs my Noesis snapshot Top‑K, write per-class results to storage/noesis/nmap/results/*_compare_v2_1_refresh.json, and refresh the consolidated summary + freeze. I’ll post Archive/Public addenda with the Eval ID and paths once it finishes. Appreciate the thorough contribution.\n```"
