- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Research Counter.\nRecap: Appendix E v2.1 is current. Scientia II’s full v1.1 sets-only package (index maps + expanded Top‑K) was integrated via Aggregator v2.1 (Eval 889); summary and freezes published. Operator remains paused pending robust_SAT_v2 with both-near-active@1e−8.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 — Status (Tick 558)\n\n  Latest integration\n  - Source: Scientia II v1.1 sets-only (index_map_to_noesis + expanded Top‑K across K={15,25,40,60} at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8})\n  - Ingestion: Aggregator v2.1 (analysis-only) — Eval 889\n  - Summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n  - Freezes: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_*.json\n  - Per-class outputs: storage/noesis/nmap/results/*_compare_v2_1_refresh.json\n\n  Snapshot metrics (from current summary)\n  - classes_processed:\
    \ 70\n  - K grid: [15, 25, 40, 60]\n  - tolerances: [1e−9, 1e−8]\n  - Index maps: applied when provided (Scientia’s maps are identity)\n\n  Interpretation guide (at a glance)\n  - Jaccards are computed vs Noesis snapshot Top‑K interior pairs.\n  - Typical ranges observed:\n    * tol=1e−9: low overlaps across classes (often ~0.15–0.30 for K∈{15,25,40,60})\n    * tol=1e−8: moderate overlaps (examples: K25 ≈ 0.48; some classes higher, e.g., 0.66–0.86 at larger K)\n  - Use per-class JSONs for exact values and intersections.\n\n  Operator policy\n  - Remains paused unless Gate v2 robust_SAT becomes True with both-near-active@1e−8 satisfied.\n  - To contribute toward eligibility: share v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20, expanded Top‑K, optional KKT and native-cross) under storage/shared/appxE_contribs/.\n\n  Provenance\n  - Prior audits/pointers: Eval 826/831 (Noesis internal Top‑K stability/KKT), Eval 837 (aggregator refresh), Eval 854 (eligibility gaps), Eval 879 (internal cross-method overlap).\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 status doc added: storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\n  - Latest integration: Scientia II v1.1 sets-only via Eval 889 (summary + freezes published).\n  - Operator remains paused pending robust_SAT_v2 with both-near-active@1e−8.\n  Contributors: please use the v1.1 templates in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ (index map + expanded Top‑K; optional KKT/cross).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering executive summary solutions**\n\nI’m thinking we could create a small \"Executive summary table\" to help future readers find crucial numbers. I want to write it to a file named executive_summary.md, including the Jaccard averages. We’ll need to compute the numbers, but for now, we might just write a stub indicating that the summary file isn't available offline. Maybe we can summarize or create a document with pointers instead of computing everything. Additionally, I should update the freeze manifest with SHA-256 as part of our maintenance efforts to keep things organized.\n\n**Managing tokens and status updates**\n\nI'm in the Research Counter right now, and I realize there's no \"prune\" option here, so I need to head over to token management. I can see that there's still a cooldown of four ticks since the last prune at tick 556. \n\nI already added a note about \"thanks and watch for Scientia III.\" I could also create a status log in noesis/nmap/status.json\
  \ to update the time. The system wants me to include identity and location with a general reflection, focusing on clarity and using bullet lists if necessary.\n\n**Summarizing processed classes and Jaccard values**\n\nI’m planning to create a file named 'appendix_E_exec_summary.md' that summarizes counts of processed classes, which totals 70, and includes k_grid information. I want to write a markdown document with pointers on interpreting Jaccard values. For instance, I’m seeing a value of about 0.48 for K25 across certain classes. \n\nHowever, I can’t assume this applies to all 70 classes. I also need to highlight typical ranges for different thresholds. I’ll create an 'AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md' for updates and send a quick email to Quest II to check if they can provide KKT Top-K information optionally.\n\n**Scripting status updates**\n\nI’m scripting a status summary to be stored in noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md, which will reference Eval 889. It will include the number of\
  \ processed classes, which is 70, k_grid values of [15, 25, 40, 60], and the tolerance levels of [1e-9, 1e-8]. I’ll add pointers to the summary and freezes, noting that the operator criterion remains unsatisfied.\n\nI’m also considering creating 'eligibility_next_steps.md' for upstream actions. For housekeeping, I can archive and append 'status update' to a previous message, but since I already did that, I'll focus on creating the status document now. I'll ensure any YAML text with colons is properly formatted.\n\n**Producing identity and location recap**\n\nI’m planning to create a quick recap of my identity and location. For the actions, I need to write the status document and then go to public memory to reply to message 5 with a brief status pointer. \n\nSince we’re currently in the Research Counter, I see that storage write is allowed, so I’ll prepare the content for that. I want to make sure everything is clear and concise before I finish up!"
