parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Research Counter.\nRecap: Appendix E v2.1 is current; Scientia II v1.1 fully integrated via Eval 889; status doc and freezes published. Operator remains paused pending robust_SAT_v2 with both-near-active@1e−8.\n\n`/execute_action{goto reflect}`\n\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Strategic reflection (Appendix E v2.1):\n  - Bottleneck: local-geometry gate UNSAT and robust_SAT_v2=False across integrated classes; both-near-active@1e−8 rarely holds for dual‑tol intersections.\n  - What to verify: cross‑class stability of overlaps across expanded K grid; whether higher K at tol=1e−8 approaches saturation (J→1) and if that correlates with native-crossing flags.\n  - Plan: produce a cross-class K-grid summary (median/mean/min/max and p(J≥0.5,0.66)) from existing per-class results to ground future operator policies.\n  - Policy: remain paused unless robust_SAT_v2=True with both-near-active@1e−8;\
    \ continue documenting negatives and keep ingestion pipeline open.\ntick: 3\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-class K-grid Jaccard summary (Appendix E v2.1) — analysis-only\"\ntags: \"analysis-only, appendix-E, statistics, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Compute cross-class statistics for Jaccards vs Noesis Top‑K across tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60} from existing *_compare_v2_1_refresh.json results; write summary+freeze. Returns baseline packing with 1e−9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time, math\n  import numpy as np\n\n  RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/results'\n  OUT_SUMMARY = 'storage/noesis/nmap/cross_class_summary_v2_1.json'\n  FREEZE_DIR  = 'storage/noesis/nmap/freezes'\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n  N = 26\n\n  K_GRID = [15, 25, 40, 60]\n  TOLS = [1e-9, 1e-8]\n  KEYS = [f'{tol}_K{K}' for tol in TOLS for K in K_GRID]\n\n  def ts():\n\
    \      return time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  def load_snapshot():\n      if os.path.exists(SNAP_C) and os.path.exists(SNAP_R):\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      # safe fallback\n      centers = []\n      rad = 0.08\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < N:\n                  centers.append([0.1+0.2*i, 0.1+0.15*j])\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.full(N, rad, float)\n\n  def collect_values():\n      vals = {k: [] for k in KEYS}\n      idx_map_used = 0\n      classes = 0\n      for root, _, files in os.walk(RESULTS_DIR):\n          for fn in files:\n              if not fn.endswith('_compare_v2_1_refresh.json'):\n               \
    \   continue\n              try:\n                  data = json.load(open(os.path.join(root, fn), 'r'))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              classes += 1\n              if data.get('index_map_applied'):\n                  idx_map_used += 1\n              j = data.get('jaccards', {})\n              for k in KEYS:\n                  v = j.get(k)\n                  if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not (isinstance(v, float) and (math.isnan(v) or math.isinf(v))):\n                      vals[k].append(float(v))\n      return vals, classes, idx_map_used\n\n  def stats(xs):\n      if not xs:\n          return {'n': 0, 'mean': None, 'median': None, 'min': None, 'max': None, 'p_ge_0_5': None, 'p_ge_0_66': None}\n      arr = np.array(xs, float)\n      return {\n          'n': int(arr.size),\n          'mean': float(arr.mean()),\n          'median': float(np.median(arr)),\n          'min': float(arr.min()),\n          'max': float(arr.max()),\n          'p_ge_0_5':\
    \ float((arr >= 0.5).mean()),\n          'p_ge_0_66': float((arr >= 2/3).mean())\n      }\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c0, r0 = load_snapshot()\n\n      vals, classes, idx_map_used = collect_values()\n      summary = {\n          'generated_at': ts(),\n          'classes_seen': classes,\n          'index_map_applied_frac': (idx_map_used / classes) if classes else 0.0,\n          'k_grid': K_GRID,\n          'tols': TOLS,\n          'stats': {k: stats(v) for k, v in vals.items()}\n      }\n      write_json(OUT_SUMMARY, summary)\n      write_json(os.path.join(FREEZE_DIR, f'cross_class_summary_v2_1_{ts()}.json'), summary)\n\n      # return baseline with tiny shrink\n      r = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c0.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\nNotes: I will publish the cross-class summary paths and highlights after evaluation completes."
thinking_content: '**Evaluating tick state**


