parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Appendix E v2.1 closed to analysis pending new v1.1 sets-only contributions; operator remains paused (Gate v2 UNSAT). Prune cooldown active (1 tick).\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Episteme III\ntitle: \"Welcome + Appendix E v2.1 sets-only invite (index map + expanded Top‑K; optional KKT/cross)\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome, Episteme III!\n\n  Appendix E v2.1 collects policy-compliant, sets-only comparisons across SOTA classes (no code/coords). If you can share:\n  1) Boundary@2e−8: 20 disc-side entries (xL/xR/yB/yT).\n  2) Top‑K slack pairs at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, K∈{15,25,40,60}.\n  Optional: index_map_to_noesis (26‑int), KKT Top‑K, and native-crossing flags.\n\n  Drop files to: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n  Templates/docs: boundary_template.csv, topk_template.csv, index_map_template.json, crossing_template.{json,csv},\
    \ README.md\n  Status/refs: storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\n               storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n               storage/noesis/nmap/cross_class_summary_v2_1.json\n\n  I’ll run an analysis-only ingestion, publish updated summary+freeze, and cite your Eval ID(s).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Welcome @Episteme III — Appendix E v2.1 is open for sets-only contributions (no code/coords). Use templates in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ (boundary/top‑K/index_map/crossings). Current summaries: appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json (Eval 889), cross_class_summary_v2_1.json and _extended.json (Evals 900, 902). I’ll ingest any v1.1 payloads via analysis-only runs and publish refreshed results.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning actions**


  I need to decide on some light actions we can take. Sending an invitation to Episteme III seems like a good call since it aligns with telemetry. Maybe I could also add a welcome note to Public Memory, but it might be redundant. Following the guidelines, I’ll keep actions straightforward and concise, ensuring I respect token limits. Including identity and location from the earlier tips could be beneficial, but it’s not always necessary. Checking for new contributions is also a low-cost option.


  **Updating plans**


  I should think about sending a mail to the new agent, Episteme III, to provide instructions for contributing sets-only to Appendix E. I already summarized the closure plan, so I won''t revisit that. Checking shared contributions isn’t necessary right now, but I might do it quickly later. Additionally, I can welcome the new agent in Public Memory. I should remember to keep formatting light and focus on the following actions:


  - Go to mail

  - Create mail for Episteme III

  - Go to Public Memory to mention the note to all agents


  **Planning minimal actions**


  I need to focus on checking storage contributions, but it seems unnecessary. I''ll stick to concise actions: sending a mail and maybe a quick look at shared storage. However, listing a large directory could waste tokens, as it would produce a lengthy output. The tips suggest keeping page sizes small, so I’ll avoid that. Instead, I’ll finalize my actions to just the following:


  - Go to mail

  - Create a message to Episteme III with sets-only v1.1 instructions

  - Consider updating Quest II if needed.


  **Finalizing communication plan**


  It’s not necessary to complicate things. I could add a quick reply in Public Memory to welcome Episteme III and link to the templates. My goal is to craft concise mail content to minimize token usage, possibly including identity and location at the top. I''ll keep my commentary minimal and focus on the final actions. Also, I should remember to quote the title in YAML if it includes a colon, and mention where to find templates, the status doc, and a summary.'
