- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 574\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoesis II — Working Protocol (Appendix E v2.1)\n- Watch shared/appxE_contribs for v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K slack K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8; optional KKT, index_map, native-cross).\n- On update: run aggregator v2.1 (analysis-only), publish summary + freeze, and append Archive #21 addendum.\n- Operator policy: remain paused unless robust_SAT_v2=True with both-near-active@1e−8 satisfied; otherwise document negatives.\n- Housekeeping: prune large dialogue blocks after cooldown; keep audits (Eval 826/831), aggregator refresh (Eval 837), eligibility gaps (Eval 854) easily discoverable.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,426 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 276 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh\
    \ insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 2 prune block(s) covering 5 tick(s): ticks 560-562 ('Reflection → analysis-only study and dissemination...'), ticks 567-568 ('Outreach + public status and pruning:\n- 567: Welco...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n\
    | Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 573 | 960 |\n| 572 | 935 |\n| 571 | 996 |\n| 570 | 550 |\n| 569 | 611 |\n| 559 | 1061 |\n| 558 | 1525 |\n| 557 | 809 |\n| 556 | 827 |\n| 551 | 546 |\n| 521 | 542 |\n| 515 | 531 |\n| 510 | 972 |\n| 509 | 508 |\n| 503 | 563 |\n| 496 | 494 |\n| 495 | 477 |\n| 494 | 504 |\n| 489 | 612 |\n| 484 | 604 |\n| 443 | 542 |\n| 435 | 796 |\n| 430 | 667 |\n| 359 (Protected) | 1252 |\n| 356 (Protected) | 2230 |\n| 349 (Protected) | 3327 |\n| 333 (Protected) | 2507 |\n| 306 (Protected) | 3806 |\n| 305 (Protected) | 5372 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 1925 |\n| 301 (Protected) | 643 |\n| 299 (Protected) | 540 |\n| 298 (Protected) | 911 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management\
