tick: 574
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Token Management Room → moving to Research Counter to run a new analysis-only experiment addressing the inactivity notice with a novel, policy-compliant study.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-vs-Slack Agreement Audit v2.1 (sets-only, cross-class Spearman/Jaccard + eligibility triage)\"\ntags: \"analysis, sets-only, kkt, slack, jaccard, spearman, audit\"\nabstract: \"We introduce a new analysis-only study that quantifies agreement between KKT-proxy and slack Top‑K interior rankings across shared/appxE_contribs (v2.1 schema). For each class and tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}, we compute Jaccard and Spearman (on intersections) over available K, plus K-consistency across K and an eligibility triage using native crossing flags. Results are written to lineage storage (JSON + timestamped freeze). Returns our baseline packing with 1e−9 shrink.\"\ncontent: |\n \
    \ import os, json, time, numpy as np\n\n  SHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n  OUT_MAIN = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'research', 'kkt_slack_agreement_v2_1.json')\n\n  SNAP_C = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  SNAP_R = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt'\n\n  def _ensure_dirs():\n      os.makedirs(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'research'), exist_ok=True)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'freezes'), exist_ok=True)\n\n  def _ts():\n      return time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())\n\n  def _load_snapshot():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt(SNAP_C, dtype=float).reshape(26,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt(SNAP_R, dtype=float).reshape(26,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          # conservative fallback: small grid\n          centers = []\n          rad = 0.08\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < 26:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i,\
    \ 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          return np.array(centers, float), np.full(26, rad, float)\n\n  # ---------- Parsing helpers (schema-robust) ----------\n  def _is_pair(x):\n      try:\n          return isinstance(x, (list, tuple)) and len(x) == 2 and all(isinstance(v, (int, np.integer)) for v in x)\n      except Exception:\n          return False\n\n  def _norm_pair(p):\n      i, j = int(p[0]), int(p[1])\n      return (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n\n  def _read_json_pairs(path):\n      # Return (ordered_list_of_pairs, meta_dict)\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          return [], {}\n\n      # Many shapes; normalize\n      # Case A: dict with 'pairs'\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n          if 'pairs' in data and isinstance(data['pairs'], list):\n              pairs = [ _norm_pair(p) for p in data['pairs'] if _is_pair(p) ]\n              K = int(data.get('K', len(pairs)))\n              meta = {'K': K, 'method':\
    \ data.get('method', ''), 'tol': str(data.get('tol', ''))}\n              return pairs, meta\n          # Case B: dict with 'topk' or 'data' sublist\n          for key in ['topk', 'data', 'items', 'list']:\n              if key in data and isinstance(data[key], list):\n                  arr = data[key]\n                  pairs = []\n                  for entry in arr:\n                      if _is_pair(entry):\n                          pairs.append(_norm_pair(entry))\n                      elif isinstance(entry, dict):\n                          cand = entry.get('pair') or entry.get('pairs')\n                          if _is_pair(cand):\n                              pairs.append(_norm_pair(cand))\n                  K = int(data.get('K', len(pairs)))\n                  meta = {'K': K, 'method': data.get('method', ''), 'tol': str(data.get('tol', ''))}\n                  return pairs, meta\n      # Case C: list-of-pairs\n      if isinstance(data, list):\n          pairs = [ _norm_pair(p)\
    \ for p in data if _is_pair(p) ]\n          meta = {'K': len(pairs), 'method': '', 'tol': ''}\n          return pairs, meta\n\n      return [], {}\n\n  def _read_crossings(path):\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      xs = []\n      if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get('crossings'), list):\n          for entry in data['crossings']:\n              try:\n                  p1 = entry.get('pair1'); p2 = entry.get('pair2')\n                  if _is_pair(p1) and _is_pair(p2):\n                      xs.append({\n                          'pair1': _norm_pair(p1),\n                          'pair2': _norm_pair(p2),\n                          'native_cross_strict': bool(entry.get('native_cross_strict', False)),\n                          'native_cross_inclusive': bool(entry.get('native_cross_inclusive', entry.get('native_cross_strict', False)))\n                      })\n           \
    \   except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return xs\n\n  def _prefix_from_name(name):\n      # Strip known suffixes to form a class key\n      s = name\n      for tok in [\n          '_slack_top_k_1e_8', '_slack_top_k_1e_9',\n          '_kkt_top_k_1e_8', '_kkt_top_k_1e_9',\n          '_index_map_to_noesis', '_crossings', '.json'\n      ]:\n          s = s.replace(tok, '')\n      if s.endswith('.json'):\n          s = s[:-5]\n      return s\n\n  # Spearman on intersections only (order-sensitive lists)\n  def _spearman_on_intersection(list_a, list_b):\n      # Build ranks from order\n      idx_a = {p:i for i,p in enumerate(list_a)}\n      idx_b = {p:i for i,p in enumerate(list_b)}\n      inter = [p for p in idx_a.keys() if p in idx_b]\n      n = len(inter)\n      if n < 2:\n          return None, n\n      ra = np.array([idx_a[p] for p in inter], dtype=float)\n      rb = np.array([idx_b[p] for p in inter], dtype=float)\n      # Convert to average ranks if ties existed (unlikely\
    \ here)\n      ra_mean = (ra - ra.mean())\n      rb_mean = (rb - rb.mean())\n      den = np.sqrt((ra_mean**2).sum()) * np.sqrt((rb_mean**2).sum())\n      if den == 0:\n          return None, n\n      rho = float((ra_mean * rb_mean).sum() / den)\n      return rho, n\n\n  def _jaccard(a, b):\n      A, B = set(a), set(b)\n      if not A and not B:\n          return 1.0\n      if not A or not B:\n          return 0.0\n      return float(len(A & B)) / float(len(A | B))\n\n  def _collect_class_entries():\n      entries = {}\n      try:\n          files = sorted(os.listdir(SHARED_DIR))\n      except Exception:\n          files = []\n      for fn in files:\n          if not fn.endswith('.json'):\n              continue\n          path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, fn)\n          key = _prefix_from_name(fn)\n          rec = entries.setdefault(key, {\n              'slack': {'1e-9': [], '1e-8': []},\n              'kkt':   {'1e-9': [], '1e-8': []},\n              'cross': []\n          })\n     \
    \     if 'slack_top_k_1e_9' in fn:\n              pairs, meta = _read_json_pairs(path)\n              rec['slack']['1e-9'].append({'pairs': pairs, 'K': int(meta.get('K', len(pairs)))})\n          elif 'slack_top_k_1e_8' in fn:\n              pairs, meta = _read_json_pairs(path)\n              rec['slack']['1e-8'].append({'pairs': pairs, 'K': int(meta.get('K', len(pairs)))})\n          elif 'kkt_top_k_1e_9' in fn:\n              pairs, meta = _read_json_pairs(path)\n              rec['kkt']['1e-9'].append({'pairs': pairs, 'K': int(meta.get('K', len(pairs)))})\n          elif 'kkt_top_k_1e_8' in fn:\n              pairs, meta = _read_json_pairs(path)\n              rec['kkt']['1e-8'].append({'pairs': pairs, 'K': int(meta.get('K', len(pairs)))})\n          elif 'crossings' in fn:\n              rec['cross'].extend(_read_crossings(path))\n      return entries\n\n  def _union_pairs(list_of_sets):\n      u = set()\n      for s in list_of_sets:\n          u |= set(s)\n      return u\n\n  def\
    \ _analyze_class(key, rec):\n      out = {'key': key, 'tols': {}}\n      for tol in ['1e-9', '1e-8']:\n          tolres = {'slack_vs_kkt': [], 'k_consistency': None}\n          slack_lists = [e['pairs'] for e in rec['slack'][tol] if e['pairs']]\n          kkt_lists   = [e['pairs'] for e in rec['kkt'][tol] if e['pairs']]\n          # Slack/KKT agreement across available K (pair by pair of lists, truncating to min length)\n          for s_list in slack_lists:\n              for k_list in kkt_lists:\n                  m = min(len(s_list), len(k_list))\n                  if m > 0:\n                      s_tr = s_list[:m]\n                      k_tr = k_list[:m]\n                      jac = _jaccard(s_tr, k_tr)\n                      rho, n = _spearman_on_intersection(s_tr, k_tr)\n                      tolres['slack_vs_kkt'].append({'K_min': m, 'jaccard': jac, 'spearman': rho, 'n_intersection': n})\n          # K-consistency across K for slack (intersection across all slack lists at tol)\n\
    \          if len(slack_lists) >= 2:\n              inter = set(slack_lists[0])\n              for lst in slack_lists[1:]:\n                  inter &= set(lst)\n              uni = _union_pairs(slack_lists)\n              tolres['k_consistency'] = {\n                  'n_lists': len(slack_lists),\n                  'intersection_size': len(inter),\n                  'union_size': len(uni),\n                  'intersection_over_union': (len(inter)/len(uni)) if len(uni)>0 else None\n              }\n          out['tols'][tol] = tolres\n\n      # Eligibility triage via crossings (approx: both pairs appear in any slack list at tol=1e-8)\n      eligible_1e8 = set()\n      for e in rec['slack']['1e-8']:\n          for p in e['pairs']:\n              eligible_1e8.add(p)\n      n_cross_candidates = 0\n      n_cross_native_strict = 0\n      for cx in rec['cross']:\n          p1 = cx['pair1']; p2 = cx['pair2']\n          if p1 in eligible_1e8 and p2 in eligible_1e8:\n              n_cross_candidates\
    \ += 1\n              if cx.get('native_cross_strict', False):\n                  n_cross_native_strict += 1\n      out['eligibility'] = {\n          'both_near_active_1e8_candidates': n_cross_candidates,\n          'native_cross_strict_count': n_cross_native_strict\n      }\n      return out\n\n  def _summarize(all_class_results):\n      # Aggregate means for jaccard/spearman where defined\n      agg = {'by_tol': {}}\n      for tol in ['1e-9', '1e-8']:\n          jac_vals, rho_vals = [], []\n          for cr in all_class_results:\n              blk = cr.get('tols', {}).get(tol, {})\n              for svk in blk.get('slack_vs_kkt', []):\n                  if svk.get('jaccard') is not None:\n                      jac_vals.append(float(svk['jaccard']))\n                  rho = svk.get('spearman')\n                  if rho is not None:\n                      rho_vals.append(float(rho))\n          agg['by_tol'][tol] = {\n              'mean_jaccard': (sum(jac_vals)/len(jac_vals)) if jac_vals\
    \ else None,\n              'mean_spearman': (sum(rho_vals)/len(rho_vals)) if rho_vals else None,\n              'n_pairs_evaluated': len(jac_vals)\n          }\n      return agg\n\n  def _write_outputs(payload):\n      _ensure_dirs()\n      # Main\n      with open(OUT_MAIN, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(payload, f, indent=2)\n      # Freeze\n      stamp = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%SZ', time.gmtime())\n      freeze_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'freezes', f'kkt_slack_agreement_v2_1_{stamp}.json')\n      with open(freeze_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(payload, f, indent=2)\n      return freeze_path\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Analysis\n      entries = _collect_class_entries()\n      results = []\n      for key, rec in entries.items():\n          results.append(_analyze_class(key, rec))\n      summary = _summarize(results)\n      payload = {\n          'generated_at': _ts(),\n          'schema': 'v2.1',\n          'source_dir': SHARED_DIR,\n          'class_count':\
    \ len(results),\n          'summary': summary,\n          'results_by_class': results\n      }\n      try:\n          _write_outputs(payload)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      # Return baseline packing with tiny shrink\n      c0, r0 = _load_snapshot()\n      r0 = np.maximum(r0 - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c0.astype(float), r0.astype(float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring a robust triage system**\n\nI'm considering a \"Robust Gate v2\" triage across a K grid that uses near-active threshold scanning. It would calculate the count of pairs within a dual-tolerance intersection at specified tolerances and create an \"eligibility_by_threshold\" table. However, it seems that the aggregator v2.1 might have done something similar. \n\nAlternatively, I could conduct an \"internal top-k audit\" without random variations since the notice emphasizes avoiding repeated experiments. My focus needs to be on producing new metrics and a concrete plan.\n\n**Developing the KKT-vs-Slack Audit Script**\n\nI'm planning to create a script called \"KKT-vs-Slack Agreement Audit (v2.1).\" It will robustly compute Spearman correlations between slack and KKT rank top-lists, provided that KKT files are available. If not, I'll skip that part. \n\nThe script will also measure the Jaccard index of their top-K sets and determine the stability as the fraction\
  \ of pairs appearing consistently across K. Plus, it will identify the \"eligibility potential\" as the count of candidate crossing quads where both pairs are near-active at a specified tolerance range. \n\nI'll avoid reading coordinates and focus on pairs lists and crossing flags instead. Using co-occurrence matrices, I can summarize relationships across classes without needing slack values or KKT multipliers.\n\n**Creating Aggregated Metrics Script**\n\nI’m working on aggregating metrics per class and storing JSON in the specified directory. The script will parse both JSON and CSV files in the shared contributions folder, just like the earlier aggregator. I’ll include robust reading with try/except for reliability and implement the 1e-9 shrink.\n\nFirst, I’ll define the path to the shared directory. Then, I'll list files to find specific patterns: \"*_slack_top_k_1e_8.json,\" \"*_slack_top_k_1e_9.json,\" and \"*_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json.\" \n\nFor each base prefix, if available, I’ll build\
  \ sets for K values [15, 25, 40, 60]. I’ll compute Jaccard indices and approximate Spearman-like correlations for overlapping K, noting that the ranking may not be explicit unless the JSON includes ordered lists. I’ll assume they are ranked, as they were in prior aggregations.\n\n**Developing the Spearman Correlation Script**\n\nI'm designing the script to compute Spearman correlations by mapping pairs to their rank indices within the list. I’ll analyze correlations between ranks for intersections. \n\nFirst, I’ll establish a \"consistency score\" for each K, indicating how often pairs appear across different K values at a specified tolerance. I'll calculate the \"dual-tolerance intersection size\" for the top-K, potentially using K=15 at tolerances of 1e-8 and 1e-9.\n\nIf a crossings file like \"*_crossings.json\" exists, I’ll extract the \"native_cross_strict\" booleans for pairs. I'll focus only on those that are near-active at tolerance 1e-8 and save the results to the specified JSON\
  \ file.\n\nThe summary will include mean Spearman, mean Jaccard scores, and classes with low Slack-KKT agreement but present crossings. Lastly, I’ll parse \"index_map_*\" files for geometry mapping, keeping in mind that I’m evaluating sets rather than individual points.\n\n**Building the KKT-Slack Agreement Script**\n\nI'm designing a script to compute the KKT-Slack agreement. The code will utilize standard libraries with NumPy, allowing for SciPy only for Spearman correlation computations. If SciPy is unavailable, I'll implement the Spearman formula from scratch using rank positions.\n\nThe script will read slack top-K JSON files and KKT top-K files, parsing their structures and extracting pairs. I’ll compute metrics like Jaccard indices, Spearman correlations, and crossing candidates based on specified criteria. \n\nFinally, I’ll summarize results in a JSON file, making sure to format the YAML submission carefully, especially for titles and abstracts. I’m preparing to craft the code\
  \ and gather the necessary information.\n\n**Finalizing Slack vs KKT Comparison**\n\nI need to compare slack and KKT at matching K values by choosing the minimum of K from both. I’ll truncate the lists to this minimum size and build sets to compute the Jaccard index. For Spearman correlation, I’ll analyze the ranking on the intersection of these sets.\n\nNext, I'll compute \"K_consistency\" across K sets, finding the intersection size and ratio. I’ll also check the crossing file for any entries marked as \"native_cross_strict,\" ensuring both pairs appear in the slack list at 1e-8. \n\nFinally, I’ll summarize the results across classes, include metrics in the JSON output, and save a timestamped copy. After loading the necessary data or falling back to grid as needed, I’ll finalize the submission with relevant tags like \"analysis,\" \"sets-only,\" \"kkt,\" \"slack,\" \"jaccard,\" \"spearman,\" and \"audit.\""
