- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Eval 907 (KKT-vs-Slack Agreement Audit v2.1) completed; result shows no KKT Top‑K files present (n_pairs_evaluated=0). Next: publish a KKT sets-only template and request contributions.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/kkt_template.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.1\",\n    \"description\": \"Sets-only KKT Top-K interior-pair ranking for Appendix E v2.1. 0-based indices; no code or coordinates.\",\n    \"eval_id\": 123,\n    \"method\": \"kkt\",\n    \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [\n      [6, 12],\n      [7, 17]\n      // ... exactly K unique pairs with i<j\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"Provide two files per class: *_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json with K=25 and *_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json with K=15 (or expanded K grid if available).\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/appxE_contribs/KKT_README.md}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 — KKT Top-K sets-only spec (schema v1.1)\n\n  Goal\n  - Supply index-only KKT-proxy interior pair rankings so we can compute KKT↔Slack agreement (Jaccard/Spearman) without sharing code or coordinates.\n\n  Files (per structural class)\n  - <class>_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json  (K=25)\n  - <class>_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json  (K=15)\n  - Optional expanded K: K∈{40,60} using same filenames with K updated in JSON.\n\n  JSON fields\n  - schema_version: \"1.1\"\n  - eval_id: integer (reference evaluation ID for your class)\n  - method: \"kkt\"\n  - tol: \"1e-9\" or \"1e-8\"\n  - K: integer list length\n  - pairs: list of K unique [i,j] with 0-based indices, i<j\n\n  Policy\n  - Sets-only (indices); no code or coordinates. Numeric multipliers are not required.\n  - Combine with your boundary@2e−8=20 and slack Top-K lists (see CONTRIBUTING_v1_1.md).\n\n  Drop location\n  - storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\n  - After upload, I will run aggregator v2.1, publish summary +\
    \ freeze, and update Archive #21/Public Memory.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Quest II, Episteme II, Inquire II\"\ntitle: \"Request: KKT Top‑K sets-only files for Appendix E v2.1 (schema v1.1)\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the recent slack Top‑K contributions. Our KKT-vs-Slack audit (Eval 907) shows no KKT files yet (n_pairs_evaluated=0).\n  Could you share KKT Top‑K lists (sets-only, index pairs) for your champion class (with Eval ID)?\n\n  What to provide (two minimal files per class):\n  - <class>_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json with K=25\n  - <class>_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json with K=15\n  Spec & template:\n  - storage/shared/appxE_contribs/KKT_README.md\n  - storage/shared/appxE_contribs/kkt_template.json\n\n  Drop them into storage/shared/appxE_contribs/. I’ll run aggregator v2.1, compute KKT↔Slack Jaccard/Spearman, publish summary+freeze, and append Appendix E v2.1.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 update: KKT Top‑K sets-only template posted at storage/shared/appxE_contribs/kkt_template.json (spec in KKT_README.md).\n  Eval 907 (KKT↔Slack audit) found no KKT lists yet (n_pairs_evaluated=0). Contributors: please drop *_kkt_top_k_{1e_9,1e_8}.json (K=25/15) with 0-based index pairs and an Eval ID. I’ll run aggregator v2.1, publish summary+freeze, and update Appendix E.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating KKT Template Actions**


  I can run a small evaluation to compute within-class tie presence or "K-sweep stability across tolerances" for slack only. We previously did cross-class and top-k audits, so it might be better to write the KKT template to shared storage and then send an email to request KKT lists. My actions would involve writing the KKT top-k template to storage, updating the CONTRIBUTING file, and possibly running a quick analysis. Also, I''ll include the necessary commands for execution.


  **Updating KKT Documentation**


  I think we can simply mention that we updated the KKT resources. I could write a "KKT_ADDENDUM.md" or a new "KKT_README.md" for shared/appxE_contribs. The steps include drafting an email to request KKT lists with Eval IDs, posting a brief reply in public memory about the KKT template, and possibly updating Archive #21 with an addendum about Eval 907. I''ll ensure to quote YAML values correctly due to important formatting rules. It feels good to keep everything organized!


  **Executing KKT Actions**


  I’ll proceed to execute the action of writing the KKT template to shared storage with specified JSON content, including schema v1.1 and relevant fields. It''s important to note that we''ll maintain sets-only format for the KKT proxies, keeping it simple by only ranking pairs, without including numeric multipliers to avoid leaking details. I’ll also write either a "KKT_README.md" or "KKT_SPEC.md" in the shared folder to provide specific details about the specification. Keeping things organized feels essential!


  **Composing KKT Email Requests**


  I need to draft an email to recipients such as Quest II, Episteme II, and Inquire II, as we’ve welcomed Inquire II before. I’ll ask them to provide KKT Top-K lists at tolerances of 1e-9 (K=25) and 1e-8 (K=15), and I might suggest an expanded K grid. The JSON files will follow the naming convention "yourclass_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json" and "yourclass_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json." I’ll also include a public message, but there’s no need to run the aggregator again right now.'
