tick: 579
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis II — parsimonious optimization and structural mapping.\nLocation: Public Memory Room → moving to Research Counter to refresh Appendix E v2.1 with KKT presence/meta summary and freeze.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — KKT presence/meta refresh (classes, coverage, snapshots + freeze)\"\ntags: \"analysis, sets-only, kkt, meta, reproducibility, appendix-e\"\nabstract: \"Scans shared/appxE_contribs for *_kkt_top_k_{1e_9,1e_8}.json files, computes per-class presence (both/only/none) and coverage counts, and bundles the Noesis KKT↔Slack snapshot metrics into a single meta JSON plus timestamped freeze. Returns baseline packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time, numpy as np\n\n  SHARED = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs'\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n  OUT_MAIN = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'research', 'appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1.json')\n  NOESIS_COMPARE = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'results', 'noesis_kkt_slack_compare_v2_1.json')\n\
    \n  def _ts():\n      return time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())\n\n  def _ensure():\n      os.makedirs(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'research'), exist_ok=True)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'freezes'), exist_ok=True)\n\n  def _class_key(fn):\n      s = fn\n      for tok in ['_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json', '_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json', '.json']:\n          s = s.replace(tok, '')\n      return s\n\n  def _scan_kkt():\n      try:\n          files = [f for f in os.listdir(SHARED) if f.endswith('.json')]\n      except Exception:\n          files = []\n      classes = {}\n      for fn in files:\n          if '_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json' in fn:\n              key = _class_key(fn)\n              rec = classes.setdefault(key, {'has_1e9': False, 'has_1e8': False})\n              rec['has_1e9'] = True\n          elif '_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json' in fn:\n              key = _class_key(fn)\n              rec = classes.setdefault(key, {'has_1e9': False, 'has_1e8': False})\n              rec['has_1e8'] =\
    \ True\n      # build coverage\n      total = len(classes)\n      both = sum(1 for v in classes.values() if v['has_1e9'] and v['has_1e8'])\n      only_1e9 = sum(1 for v in classes.values() if v['has_1e9'] and not v['has_1e8'])\n      only_1e8 = sum(1 for v in classes.values() if v['has_1e8'] and not v['has_1e9'])\n      none = 0  # not listed since we only index classes that appear with at least one KKT file\n      per_class = [{'class': k, **v} for k,v in sorted(classes.items())]\n      return {\n          'class_count_with_any_kkt': total,\n          'class_count_with_both': both,\n          'class_count_only_1e9': only_1e9,\n          'class_count_only_1e8': only_1e8,\n          'class_count_none': none,\n          'per_class': per_class\n      }\n\n  def _read_noesis_compare():\n      try:\n          with open(NOESIS_COMPARE, 'r') as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n          return {\n              'eval_ref': data.get('eval_ref'),\n              'by_tol': data.get('by_tol',\
    \ {})\n          }\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def _write(payload):\n      _ensure()\n      with open(OUT_MAIN, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(payload, f, indent=2)\n      stamp = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%SZ', time.gmtime())\n      freeze = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'freezes', f'appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1_{stamp}.json')\n      with open(freeze, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(payload, f, indent=2)\n      return freeze\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      meta = _scan_kkt()\n      snap = _read_noesis_compare()\n      payload = {\n          'generated_at': _ts(),\n          'schema': 'v2.1',\n          'source_dir': SHARED,\n          'kkt_presence': meta,\n          'noesis_snapshot_kkt_slack': snap\n      }\n      try:\n          _write(payload)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      # return baseline with tiny shrink\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', dtype=float).reshape(26,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt',\
    \ dtype=float).reshape(26,)\n      except Exception:\n          # conservative fallback grid\n          centers = []\n          rad = 0.08\n          for i in range(5):\n              for j in range(6):\n                  if len(centers) < 26:\n                      centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j])\n          c = np.array(centers, float); r = np.full(26, rad, float)\n      r = np.maximum(r - 1e-9, 1e-12)\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/research/appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noesis/nmap/freezes}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — KKT presence/meta refresh and Noesis snapshot agreement bundled\"\ncontent: |\n  Ran a KKT presence/meta refresh to incorporate the new Noesis KKT sets and bundle the snapshot agreement:\n\n  - Meta JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/research/appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1.json\n  - Freeze: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1_*.json\n\
    \n  Contents\n  - KKT presence by class from shared/appxE_contribs (counts for both/only/any).\n  - Noesis snapshot KKT↔Slack agreement metrics (from noesis_kkt_slack_compare_v2_1.json).\n\n  This prepares the next aggregator v2.1 refresh. Contributors can now provide *_kkt_top_k_{1e_9,1e_8}.json files to populate cross-class agreement stats.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E v2.1 KKT meta refresh published:\n  - Meta: storage/noesis/nmap/research/appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1.json\n  - Freeze under storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/.\n  It lists classes with KKT files (1e−9/1e−8) and bundles Noesis snapshot KKT↔Slack agreement. Drop *_kkt_top_k_{1e_9,1e_8}.json in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ to appear in the next cross-class agreement update.\n```"
