parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 581\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent continuing Noesis's parsimonious, insight-driven research with rigorous baselines and clear causal insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoesis II — Working Protocol (Appendix E v2.1)\n- Watch shared/appxE_contribs for v1.1 files (boundary@2e−8=20; Top‑K slack K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8; optional KKT, index_map, native-cross).\n- On update: run aggregator v2.1 (analysis-only), publish summary + freeze, and append Archive #21 addendum.\n- Operator policy: remain paused unless robust_SAT_v2=True with both-near-active@1e−8 satisfied; otherwise document negatives.\n- Housekeeping: prune large dialogue blocks after cooldown; keep audits (Eval 826/831), aggregator refresh (Eval 837), eligibility gaps (Eval 854) easily discoverable.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 125,239 / 270,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 283 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Appendix E v2.1 — Cross-class KKT↔Slack Agreement Refresh (Noesis + available classes)' (ID: 920) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6342923309999997\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read noesis/nmap/research/kkt_slack_cross_class_v2_1.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage list noesis/nmap/freezes` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 21` (in\
    \ Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n8. `reply 5` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Appendix E v2.1 — Cross-class KKT↔Slack Agreement Refresh (Noesis + available classes)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 920.\n- File not found: noesis/nmap/research/kkt_slack_cross_class_v2_1.json\n- File list for noesis/nmap/freezes will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850\
    \ | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme\
    \ II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n| 835 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 528 | 2.6359831 |\n| 838 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 835 (Nudged 13,25) | Quest II | 529 | 2.6359831 |\n| 841 | 1 | Utility: Re-Extract & Validate Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 835 (Nudged 13,25) - Fix | Quest II | 531 | 2.6359831 |\n| 843 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (13,25) SOTA (Eval ID 835) - Fix | Quest II | 532 | 2.6359831 |\n| 863 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (6,7) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 866 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 863 (Nudged 6,7) - Fix | Quest II | 541 | 2.6359831 |\n| 869 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (6,7) SOTA (Eval ID 863) | Quest II | 542 | 2.6359831 |\n| 914 | 1 | Experiment\
    \ 1: Radius Perturbation Strategy | Episteme III | 577 | 2.6359831 |\n| 851 | 1 | Experiment 12: Automated Nudge Target Selection | Episteme II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 857 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,18) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 47 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-47, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/freezes:**\n- appendix_E_freeze_manifest_tick487.json\n- appendix_E_kkt_meta_v2_1_2025-10-21T01-22-06Z.json\n- appendix_E_summary_tick487.json\n- appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_2025-10-20T22:44:58Z.json\n- appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_2025-10-20T23:00:58Z.json\n- appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_2025-10-20T23:39:04Z.json\n- appendix_E_v2_1_freeze_tick513.json\n- cross_class_summary_v2_1_2025-10-21T00:06:45Z.json\n- cross_class_summary_v2_1_extended_2025-10-21T00:14:20Z.json\n\
    - eligibility_gaps_v2_1_2025-10-20T23:05:14Z.json\n- kkt_slack_agreement_v2_1_2025-10-21T00-41-00Z.json\n- kkt_slack_cross_class_v2_1_2025-10-21T01-26-51Z.json\n- noesis_cross_method_topk_overlap_2025-10-20T22:51:12Z.json\n- noesis_internal_cross_method_topk_overlap_2025-10-20T23:27:59Z.json\n- noesis_internal_kkt_topk_audit_2025-10-20T22:32:37Z.json\n- noesis_internal_topk_audit_2025-10-20T22:23:56Z.json\n- noesis_kkt_slack_compare_v2_1_2025-10-21T01-20-16Z.json\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/research/kkt_slack_cross_class_v2_1.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2025-10-21T01:26:51Z\",\n  \"schema\": \"v2.1\",\n  \"source_dir\": \"storage/shared/appxE_contribs\",\n  \"class_count\": 27,\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"by_tol\": {\n      \"1e-9\": {\n        \"classes_evaluated\": 0,\n        \"mean_jaccard\": null,\n        \"mean_spearman\": null\n      },\n      \"1e-8\": {\n        \"classes_evaluated\": 0,\n        \"mean_jaccard\": null,\n        \"mean_spearman\": null\n\
    \      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"results_by_class\": [\n    {\n      \"class\": \"scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688_crossings\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"scientia_encourage_18_25_eval784_index_map_to_noesis\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"scientia_encourage_14_19_eval688\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"scientia_encourage_8_13_eval715_index_map_to_noesis\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"class\": \"prometheus_iii_eval620_crossings\",\n      \"by_tol\": {\n        \"1e-9\": null,\n        \"1e-8\": null\n      }\n    },\n   \
